order=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have no idea what you're talking about!</div> </div> </div> </div>Horngeek's referencing My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic - your character concept sounds very close to one of the main characters, being a farmgirl with the name AJ who's strong and stubborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:09:24-07:00","id":960902,"title":"","content":"Did you notice Kyman201's smiley? I'm pretty sure he/she/it got the reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:24:57-07:00","id":960906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=960902#post960902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you notice Kyman201's smiley? I'm pretty sure he/she/it got the reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'll just be over here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T00:33:24-07:00","id":960934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=960902#post960902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you notice Kyman201's smiley? I'm pretty sure he/she/it got the reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it in one (He, if you're dying to know). At one point I had an aborted project to try and stat up Celestia and Luna using the 1e Divine Patron rules.<br /> <br /> I might take a stab when Scion 2e hits, so I can get a measure of the Sisters' Callings and Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T04:45:01-07:00","id":960979,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I'd probably play a librarian Scion of a star and magic deity (not actually sure which ones like that there are) if I were to play in a game like that. With a dragon companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T04:55:07-07:00","id":960982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=960894#post960894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, werewolves, and pretty much every type of therianthrope from across the planet. 1e had them as the result of a Titan-created disease with multiple 'strains'; it could change in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yep, they appear in Demigod. Typically, the disease draws them closer to Titan worship, but some Therianthropes have broken free of their control with the help of the Gods, so they can be taken as allies. Also, the different strains have different triggers of activation.<br /> <br /> <i>Werewolves</i> = Full Moon<br /> <br /> <i>Selkies</i> (wereseals) = Being submerged in seawater<br /> <br /> <i>Bouda</i> (wherehyena) = New Moon<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fun fact:</b> Selkies don't have a proper bite attack, because of their animal form. They have to hold you down and nibble on you until they break the skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-31-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:02:19-07:00","id":962083,"title":"","content":"<b>A Scion of Inari</b> who owns a preservation shelter for foxes. Invoking the Health purview, they extend the life span of those in the shelter, allowing them to become future Kitsune in service to Inari.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:48:42-07:00","id":962923,"title":"","content":"Here are two concepts I have I will likely never get to play, Ah well:<br /> <br /> Anji Kedia - Reporter in Delhi and Scion of Agni. She was born to a wealthy Hindi family, but not particularly devout, at least until Agni came and told her what she was. Feeling the calling of the Divine, she left home to become a spy for the Divine, while performing her day job as an international reporter.<br /> <br /> Johann Patterson - Growing up in Brooklyn, with his mother, of Scandinavian heritage. He was told by his father, Odin, that he would be called upon if needed, but mostly left to his own devices. His main birthright is <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">F\u01ebr, the clutchmate </span>to </span></span>Huginn and Muninn, the Ravens that fly around the world each night. Although more limited, the raven is still able to report to him of the goings ons in the city and he has made a living as a player in the criminal and supernatural undegrounds as an information broker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T15:21:31-07:00","id":962984,"title":"","content":"A Scion of Hera who survived an assassination attempt by Zeus on the day he was to receive his visitation. His mortal parents were not so lucky as the house fire killed them both. Horribly disfigured in the attack, Hera's child now willingly serves Gaia, who claimed to have shielded him from Zeus's hypocritical vengeance. He has a particularly strong connection with ants, Myrmidons included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:27:29-07:00","id":967461,"title":"","content":"Playing out &quot;The Wicked + The Divine&quot;, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:56:35-07:00","id":967473,"title":"","content":"I've got another one! An FBI agent daughter of the Morrigan. Spends her whole life thinking her mother died in child birth, but her mother, during her visitation, reveals to her that her father actually killed her 'mother' when she threatened to leave him after having an affair with the woman he did not know was the Morrigan. So the Morrigan's first task is for her to track down and kill her own father.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:00:09-07:00","id":969840,"title":"","content":"<b>Jules Clemont</b>, Scion of Eris/Discordia was, like all his half-siblings, subject to her whims at any given moment. However, while most Scions will have her alternatively help or hinder them at random, Jules only ever seemed to receive her scornful moods. Wherever he went in life, chaos would soon follow. On the day he was born, riots broke out in the city. When he turned three, a mass influenza broke out. On the day he passed that test he had been studying all week for, an earthquake hit. Upon his Visitation, a suicide bomber blew themselves up in a crowded stadium.<br /> <br /> The only thing that changed after his Visitation was that he knew why these events were happening and that he was responsible. People would eventually start to notice that disaster followed him like a crazed lover and he would become known as a harbinger of doom - though if he played his cards right people might believe that he arrives to warn them of it, not bring it upon them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Arman Rahimmi</b>, Scion of Tishtrya. Born in Iran, Arman was very frequently exposed to the violence that religious extremist groups could enact upon anyone, especially 'their own people' and it culminated in him witnessing the public execution of his mother, who had been fighting for women's rights. After that traumatic event, he dedicated himself to trying to end war and instil peace in the near/middle east. After his Visitation, this goal would extend itself to the entire world and, if he could manage it, beyond even that...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brandon Njordson</b>, Scion of Njord. Icelandic son of Njord, I imagine him becoming a god of fire and, after Ragnarok, killing Surtr and taking his sword. As he's a child of Njord, he could potentially try to reform the Vanir as their new king, or he could become part of the new post-Ragnarok Aesir. His godly name would be Brandr.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, since he's already taken Surtr's sword, he could try to take his role as a Titan Avatar of Muspelheim too! That would probably be more difficult, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 01-21-2018, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:35:43-07:00","id":971754,"title":"","content":"<b>Lycurgus Psomas:</b> The product of Circe managing to entice some wandering Hero into her bedchambers, Lycurgus was made aware of his divine heritage from an extremely early age. Unfortunately, there wasn't a whole lot he was able to do with it, as he grew up on the magical island of Aeaea which had little contact with the outside world. He tried to convince his mother to teach him the ways of magic as a way to easing his boredom, but her focus would be completely diverted whenever some handsome man washed up on the shores of their home.<br /> <br /> Lycurgus would become a young man by the time he felt he was finally ready to explore the outside world, and it was during his 21st year of life that he got a lucky break when a new batch of Scions arrived on the beach. Their vessel drawn there by Circe's magical interference as she had developed a fancy for some of the men on board. Lycurgus waited in the foliage for them to disembark and travel to his mother's temple, then he sprang from his hiding place, stole their boat and sailed away on his own adventure. So far as he knows, the vessel's original owners are still on the island, likely having been turned into beasts by now!<br /> <br /> Lycurgus' sudden escape plan didn't leave him much time to pack his belongings. The only possession he managed to bring from home was an olive branch that he uses like a wand to channel the Magic and Animal purviews.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional Note:</b> Due to Circe's neglectful training regiment, Lycurgus' power is not on her level (at least not yet, anyways). However, he has begun to show symptoms of his mother's personality quirks, particularly a fascination with shapeshifting other people and forcing them to become his pets. Additionally, Circe probably wasn't the best role model when it came to relationships, causing Lycurgus to develop fleeting attachments to others based entirely on their physical attractiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2016, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:29:27-07:00","id":972227,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you'll be able to play a vampire of any sort in 2e. While I get that it's a little bit beyond the normal scope of what a Scion is, I'd love to play a Scion of Sekhmet or Tezcatlipoca whose gifts manifest somewhat similarly to classic vampirism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:00:15-07:00","id":972323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=972227#post972227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you'll be able to play a vampire of any sort in 2e. While I get that it's a little bit beyond the normal scope of what a Scion is, I'd love to play a Scion of Sekhmet or Tezcatlipoca whose gifts manifest somewhat similarly to classic vampirism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Considering that one of the Shinsengumi (Orlanda Eliot) tried to do exactly that, I don't see why it wouldn't be possible. Assuming that in 2E there are ways for Scions other than the Aztecs to derive power from blood sacrifices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T00:06:46-07:00","id":972374,"title":"","content":"Joe Carriker mentioned the possibility of vampire PCs very early on, but that was some considerable while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:10:43-07:00","id":972474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=972374#post972374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joe Carriker mentioned the possibility of vampire PCs very early on, but that was some considerable while back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, I kind of want to see playable Titanspawn now, too. Who's to say they can't rise through the ranks and become Gods? I mean the Gods themselves are Titanspawn, when you think about it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:56:58-07:00","id":972492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=972474#post972474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I kind of want to see playable Titanspawn now, too. Who's to say they can't rise through the ranks and become Gods? I mean the Gods themselves are Titanspawn, when you think about it!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in luck; in the RPGnet thread, Neall mentioned you could play titanspawn, including titanspawn Scions, out of the corebook. Mechanics for Titan Knacks are slated for a supplement, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:20:14-07:00","id":972503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=972492#post972492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're in luck; in the RPGnet thread, Neall mentioned you could play titanspawn, including titanspawn Scions, out of the corebook. Mechanics for Titan Knacks are slated for a supplement, though</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nice! Now to start thinking of ideas for such characters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:11:02-07:00","id":973050,"title":"","content":"Figured this guy could be used as either a PC or NPC, depending on how you want to run your game.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Aodh O Forannain:</b> Not all Scions are lucky enough to receive their visitation in time, not even a son of Aengus, irish God of love and beauty. But where the Gods see failure, the Titans see opportunity, and Mami Wata was all to happy to step into Aodh's life and claim her for himself.<br /> <br /> Irish born and raised, Aodh was born to a fishing family, which meant that he grew up around the sea for much of his life. Aengus has taken the form of his mother's husband during the night of his conception, so neither of them knew about his true heritage. But regardless, Aodh exhibited charming and handsome features throughout his life. With fair skin, silky blond hair and bright blue eyes, it did not take much effort for Aodh to sweet talk any girl in town. Which is probably why he drew the attention of a young maiden who was still suffering from the early stages of therianthropy.<br /> <br /> At 21 years of age, having only just entered manhood, Aodh O Forannain strolled the beach near his home under the pale blue light of the full moon. There, he came upon the form of a young woman sprawled naked and unconscious upon the shore. Not one to leave a girl helplessly exposed like that, he hastily approached her and began to remove his evening coat to shroud her. But just as he was within reach, the tide surged forth unnaturally, sinking Aodh up to his shins in sea water. The mystery woman, however, transformed into a seal right before his eyes and thrashed around in panic, biting his hand before getting dragged out to sea by the receding tide. The next thing Aodh remembers clearly after that was waking up on a rock somewhere off the coast, surrounded by barking seals. And there beside him, stroking his perfectly blond hair, was the mermaid form of Mami Wata, smiling with affection!<br /> <br /> In the days that followed, Aodh was brainwashed into becoming a loyal inhabitant of The Drowned Road. He never did find out who the Selkie was that bit him, and by this point, he's beyond the point of caring anymore. Feigning pity for the god child, Mami Wata 'blessed' him with access to some of her own power. All she asked for in payment was that Aodh agree to be placed under a Fatebond of her own creation. The specifics of this bond is that Aodh can never escape the call of the sea, which he is now spiritually bound to. During the time of the full moon (roughly 3 nights), Aodh is compelled to return to the sea and may not step upon dry land until the moon enters its next phase. In this way, Mami Wata is able to keep frequent check ups on the progress of her new pet, instead of trying to force him to visit her.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if it were as simple as just living near the ocean forever, Aodh's existence could have been overlooked by other Scions. But the young Selkie has grown lonely from his isolation and his sense of romance has been twisted by Mami Wata's influence. He has begun to make more frequent trips to dry land in search of beautiful young girls to woo. Should he find one, he plans to bring them back to the sea with him, where they will become his Selkie bride. And as if that wasn't bad enough, Aodh doesn't seem to have a problem with polygamous relationships, which means he could be thinking of building an entire harem of Selkie concubines!<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> Under the patronage of Mami Wata, Aodh has been granted access to the Water, Animal (Seal) and Health Purviews. The Water and Animal purviews are channeled through his harpoon (Walrus Tusk) which adds +2L to the Hasta template. The Health purview is channeled through a golden collar that he wears around his neck. The collar was given to him by Mami Wata in order to emphasize his role as the Titan's pet Scion.<br /> <br /> <b>Purviews:</b> Water 2, Animal 2, Health 1<br /> <br /> <b>Boons:</b> Water Breathing, Water Control, Animal Communication (Seals), Animal Command (Seals), Assess Health<br /> <br /> <b>Divine Powers:</b> <i>Epic Appearance</i> 2 (Center of Attention, Come Hither), <i>Epic Manipulation</i> 1 (Takes One to Know One), <i>Epic Charisma</i> 2 (Charmer, Engender Love), <i>Epic Stamina</i> (Extended Youth).<br /> <br /> <i>Selkie Form:</i> Aodh's seal-man form is capable of amphibious performance, although he feels most comfortable in the water. The supernatural nature of this form enables him to survive underwater up to nearly any depth (an handy substitude, should he lose access to his Water Breathing boon) and can swim at 5 times his normal movement rate.<br /> <br /> <i>Tough Hide:</i> While in his manimal form, Aodh's thick pelt grants him a +4 to Lethal and Bashing soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-20-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:29:11-07:00","id":973479,"title":"","content":"I've got two right now. The first is Caitl\u00edn \u00d3 M\u00e1ille, a daughter of Brigid with more than a hint of the Dagda (who, according to Wikipedia, is Brigid's father) about her. Very much the warrior-craftswoman, and rather passionate- she's inherited her grandfather's traits of being a passionate fighter, she's passionate about both her art and her smithing (and other gear creation), and she's a passionate lover as well (or at least, the women she beds certainly think so).<br /> <br /> The second, a former undercover cop named Vera Wolff... doesn't actually know who her divine parent is. Oh, she knows she's of the Aesir, Odin told her that when he made her Visitation <i>personally</i>, but he specifically told her that he wasn't her sire, and refused to tell her who.<br /> <br /> It's Loki. She wasn't told because the Aesir look at his Scions with suspicion at best. Odin picked her because she has a lot of Loki's more <i>useful</i> traits, but unlike him, if Vera gives her loyalty, it's dammed near absolute. She'll go undercover, sure, and play the part well, but at the end of the day her convictions are firm.<br /> <br /> (The unaware bit isn't essential to the second, mind you)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","user":"horngeek","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:50:04-07:00","id":973847,"title":"","content":"I'll throw in my players' concepts (they've been sitting on them since june of last year when it was announced that the basic system would be released for open playtesting<br /> <br /> Game is set in Kansas City, Missouri in the mid sixties<br /> <br /> \u200bBarbara McGrath, The first woman patrol officer of the KCPD (and the country), Daughter of Vidar<br /> <br /> River Lowery, B\u00e1xoje nurse-midwife looking to start fresh with her son in the big city, scion of Kali.<br /> <br /> Jackson Cobb, Good natured counterfeiter just getting out of Leavenworth, Son of Shango<br /> <br /> Norman Tokugawa, a retired cattle rancher enjoying his golden years, Son/Chosen of Hachiman,<br /> <br /> Emily Tokugawa, Norman's great grand daughter, on her way to Mizzou, Daughter of Sun Wukong (Don't tell Hachiman, he won't think its funny).<br /> <br /> Fates going to have them all running into each other at Union Station during a heist gone wrong. Thought they know who they want to be scions of they'll be playing origin level characters (cuz duh) they already have some ideas for Relics though, goofy kids.<br /> <br /> Character I've always wanted to play:<br /> <br /> &quot;trailor trash&quot; Scion of Zeus, a woman with a very bright future whose every decision seems to be the wrong one, she's been Hera's punching bag her whole life and now that she's been visited and Dad gave her a pair of lightning bolts she's not going to take the torments any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:38:32-07:00","id":973975,"title":"","content":"<b>Fujiyama Kazushi:</b> The byproduct of an attempt to build relations between the Aesir and the Amatsukami (both warrior cultures), Fujiyama is part of a Scion exchange program. The Norse pantheon adopted a Japanese Scion, and likewise the Japanese pantheon adopted a Norse Scion. Before receiving his visitation, Fujiyama was born and raised in Japan, where he developed an interest in sumo wrestling during his high school years. His parents supported his interest, first as an extracurricular activity, and later developing into a career opportunity.<br /> <br /> By subjecting himself to the rigorous training regiment of sumo, Fujiyama grew into a big man. Exceeding 200 pounds by the time he finished highschool, and growing even larger as he dedicated himself professionally to the sport. This is when Fate decided to get involved and sent an agent to test him during one of his training exercises. A weak (yet still formidable) frost giant attacked Fujiyama while he was alone in his master's dojo and challenged him to a wrestle match.<br /> <br /> The sight of an 8 foot tall man of ice probably would have been more shocking to somebody who's country didn't have shrines dedicated to any number of nature spirits, but something inside Fujiyama compelled him to accept the challenge. In typical fashion, the giant thought himself the easy victor of any clash with a human opponent. But sumo wrestlers are able to lift, throw and push 400 pound men around, and Fujiyama's strength caught the giant by surprise as he was forced on the defensive and eventually forced out of the arena!<br /> <br /> With his victory over the frost giant, Fate decided the time was right, and that's when Fujiyama received a visit from Vidar, who claimed him for the Aesir. It would later be discovered that Fujiyama's replacement among the Amatsukami had been adopted by Hachiman, thus making the program an exchange between two Gods of War.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As both a sumo wrestler and the heir to giant's blood, Vidar's trademark paranoia has set in hard when it comes to his adoptive Scion. Fujiyama is already large for a mortal, and there's no telling how much bigger he'll grow if his powers are allowed to develop further. To prevent the possibility of Fujiyama going rogue, he keeps him under close supervision. He also seems to be a demanding task master who is hard to impress even when Fujiyama does a good job. But Fujiyama is accustomed to hard work and discipline, so he does not hold a grudge against his adoptive father.<br /> <br /> <i>At least not this early on, anyways.</i><br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Fujiyama is the tank of whatever band he's in. Huge, strong, and specifically trained to repel similar individuals, Fujiyama is ready to place himself between advancing enemies and those he wishes to protect. And yet for all his raw power, Fujiyama is not a testosterone fueled meat head and is quite capable of remaining calm under pressure. Giving him an edge that most warriors of his caliber often lack!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-21-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:40:21-07:00","id":974405,"title":"","content":"Ya know what I want:<br /> THE DOGS OF WAR!<br /> a scion / pugmire crossover<br /> The cats of Mau have betrayed us to the wild things as is their nature but in our lowest hour, Lassie has returned to take us back to Timmie. And this time he is not in the well. We checked. Circled it three times and then suddenly fell to sleep. Prophetic visions of endless fields of bones left us drooling, but we woke ready to sniff out the path to a brighter future. And even though monsters stand at the gates, the heart of Scooby-Doo beats in all dogs<br /> AWOOOOOO!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:10:22-07:00","id":975056,"title":"","content":"<b>Edgar Viste:</b> in an effort to improve stability between two warrior cultures, the Gods of the Japanese and Norse pantheons decided to exchange one of their Scions. Edgar Viste is who the Aesir chose to give up, and now the Amatsukami are seriously wondering if they got the raw end of the deal on this exchange.<br /> <br /> Born in Norway, Edgar would grow up to become a problem child. He would constantly get into fights with other children his age, and the fact that he often won such confrontations did not improve his reputation much, either. Perhaps, in some part of their consciousness that the Aesir would never acknowledge, they hoped that the Amatsukami might be able to teach him discipline and self control. Regardless of their reasons, Fate decided that Edgar's family would be moving to Japan due to, as his parents put it, improved career opportunities.<br /> <br /> While initially unhappy with the sudden transfer to a country who's language he barely spoke, Edgar found a way to cope with his frustrations by joining the school's kendo club. Edgar felt surprisingly uplifted with a weapon in his hand, even if it was only made of wood and quickly began to establish himself as one of the best students in the class. Of course, this moment of respite only persisted during school hours. Outside of class, he was still the violent and unruly boy he'd always been. As he grew older and his skill with the sword improved, he would eventually go onto start his own street gang of troublesome teens who used their muscles and numbers to get their way.<br /> <br /> The Amatsukami decided enough was enough, it was time that Edgar Viste learned some proper discipline, and clearly he wasn't going to learn it on his own. Hachiman, the Japanese God of War saw the fighting spirit within Edgar, and decided to claim him as his own. It would later be discovered that Edgar's replacement had been adopted by Vidar, the Norse God of War, thus making it an arguably fair exchange.<br /> <br /> Hachiman's original intention was to groom Edgar into a proud, disciplined samurai who the Amatsukami would have been proud to count among their warriors. It didn't take, and Edgar Viste became a ruthless thug who seemed eager to draw his blade (now very much real) on anything he perceived as a threat. Edgar's been taking some history lessons, and discovered that all that crap about Bushido and honor was only created during the final years of the Samurai in a desperate attempt to remain in power. The real samurai were blood thirsty thugs who oppressed the population so badly, they inspired the greatest assassins in history!<br /> <br /> Today, Edgar still commands his street gang of violent delinquents. Although now that he's a Scion with access to super human abilities, he's begun to expand his horizons to worse crimes than petty theft and vandalism. He may be planning to build his own criminal empire, if he can safely avoid the Yakuza for now. Hachiman has given him veiled threats that some members of the organization share his special gifts, and they aren't very tolerant of rival organizations, especially not ones lead by foreigners!<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Since his visitation, Edgar has been granted the katana which has since become his most cherished possession. It enables him to channel the War purview and adds +2L -2 Speed to the Katana template. He has taken to calling this weapon <i>Satsujin-sha</i>, which means Manslayer.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Edgar has access to the gang of Thugs he managed to round up before his visitation. His gang measures 25 members in total (Followers 5)<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Hot tempered and violent, you make for an effective warrior to your band's ranks, though only because you're the most ruthless among them. You don't follow the code of Bushido, because you feel that it was bullshit to begin with; just a desperate attempt for the samurai to appeal to the government before they were disbanded. The gods gave you a sword, and the purpose of a sword is to kill people!<br /> <br /> Although you may have been claimed by the Amatsukami, you <i>are not</i> <i>welcomed</i> by them. Your belligerent attitude and criminal associates has brought shame to Hachiman who thought he could make you a better person. Instead of earning the Amatsukami's approval, you're only hope for continued advancement is to prove that your methods of dealing with the Titans are too effective to simply be cast aside. Sure, people might get caught in the cross fire, but if your manage to kill more Titanspawn than pedestrians, you're confident the Gods won't be complaining <i>too much.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:36:14-07:00","id":975172,"title":"","content":"Obviously not complete, but:<br /> <br /> Sedjert (ancient Egyptian: &quot;vigil&quot;)<br /> <br /> Divine Parent: Anpu (Anubis)<br /> Callings: Liminal (Favored), Warrior, Judge<br /> <br /> Origin Path: Made of Stone and Anpu's Will (began life as a stone idol made by Anpu; Asset Skills: Athletics, Occult)<br /> Role Path: &quot;The dead must stay dead.&quot; (Created as a weapon against undead and necromancers; Asset Skills: Close Combat, Firearms)<br /> Relationship Path: &quot;Duty does not define me.&quot; (No longer wishes to be a tool for his creator; Asset Skills: Empathy, Culture)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:39:34-07:00","id":975857,"title":"","content":"Idea:<br /> <br /> A prodigy fighter or soldier, one who instead of subscribing to one Pantheon worship? Before each match or battle she walks into, she invokes the name of MANY War Gods. Ares, Athena, Tyr, Sehkmet, half of the Tuatha, all for their blessing.<br /> <br /> The War Gods then got together, and Athena organized a branching tournament, with the winner being allowed to appear before her and Choosing her. It makes me imagine Ares appearing, panting, and saying &quot;You would not BELIEVE what I had to go through to earn this right.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:57:43-07:00","id":975988,"title":"","content":"Ai (Artifical Idol)<br /> <br /> Divine Parent: Baron Samedi<br /> Callings: Liminal (Favored), Lover, Creator<br /> <br /> Origin Path: Virtual Idol made Flesh (Programmers guided by the Baron made a sentient AI; Asset Skills: Science, Technology)<br /> Role Path: &quot;Encore? You got it!&quot;(The oringnal form of the programs was a vocaloid; Asset Skills: Performance, Persuasion)<br /> Relationship Path: &quot;Well what do we have here!&quot; (The Loa fine her a novelty creation and want to test her constantly; Asset Skills [Whatever the Loa get])<br /> <br /> This is a character I'd like to see how it would work out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:24:29-07:00","id":976097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=975988#post975988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ai (Artifical Idol)<br /> <br /> Divine Parent: Baron Samedi<br /> Callings: Liminal (Favored), Lover, Creator<br /> <br /> Origin Path: Virtual Idol made Flesh (Programmers guided by the Baron made a sentient AI; Asset Skills: Science, Technology)<br /> Role Path: &quot;Encore? You got it!&quot;(The oringnal form of the programs was a vocaloid; Asset Skills: Performance, Persuasion)<br /> Relationship Path: &quot;Well what do we have here!&quot; (The Loa fine her a novelty creation and want to test her constantly; Asset Skills [Whatever the Loa get])<br /> <br /> This is a character I'd like to see how it would work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>...you just want to play a fucking Vocaloid, don't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:06:03-07:00","id":976292,"title":"","content":"Why not!<br /> Embrace chaos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:56:16-07:00","id":976337,"title":"","content":"<b>Ash Sims:</b> This noble savage is one of Artemis' adopted Scions. But while his motherly patron is known for hunting wild animals, Ash prefers to commune with them. A social introvert from an early age, he has trouble relating to human society and prefers to surround himself with the company of pets. The fact that his mortal family worked as veterinarians and ran an animal shelter only made it easier for him to spend time with his beloved animals. His parents just thought he was being helpful around the work environment, unaware he was using it as an excuse to avoid associating with humans.<br /> <br /> The reasons for Ash's anti-social behavior are unclear. Perhaps Fate intended for Artemis to claim him from the start, and orchestrated his behavior in such a way. Artermis is also known for spurning the company of men, so this theory is not as strange as it seems. Regardless of the reasons, Ash found that he was reluctantly forced to venture into the world following the events of his visitation.<br /> <br /> One night, a wounded animal had been admitted to the shelter, with his parents planning to nurse it back to health. Eager to get to it first, Ash visited its pen to discover that the animal was actually a newly infected Therianthrope, still reeling from the shock of its first transformation. Ash watched as the creature warped and shifted before his eyes and rammed the pen hard enough to twist the metal out of shape. Once free of its trappings, it tried to lunge at the startled Ash.<br /> <br /> As if by instinct, Ash ducked under the crazed animal, wrapped his arms around its neck, and rolled his body to pin the animal underneath him! It was a technique liked to use when he was playfully wrestling the dogs at the shelter. The technique worked, and the shapeshifter seemed to be completely bewildered for a moment. As Ash loosened his hold, the beast squirmed free and then jumped out the window, running off into the night. When Ash rose to his feet, he turned to see Artemis standing behind him with a bow in her hand and an expression that seemed a mixture between curiosity and disappointment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Go catch it...&quot; she said, before thrusting a weapon into his hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:56:52-07:00","id":976372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=976097#post976097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...you just want to play a fucking Vocaloid, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDon't hate, appreciate the crazy awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:42:35-07:00","id":976411,"title":"","content":"Though I've gotten some flack on these forums before for this character's concept, I am hoping that Scion 2.0 will allow me the freedom to create this character the way I envisioned her.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Barbrah &quot;Babs&quot; Morgan</b>: raised as a druid by a Seelie father and an Unseelie mother (foster parents), Barbarah (though most call her Babs) knows that for every boon one receives, a price must be paid (though the price isn't always equal to the boon received). This is the way nature works... that beauty and brutality often go hand in hand... and that to heal a wound, healthy flesh must sometimes be sacrificed for the greater good. Never was this more true than the day she was visited by her mother... the Morrigan... where, to save her from the Fomorians that intended to kill her and her foster parents, Babs would have to choose whose life to sacrifice. Though the Morrigan had intended for one of her foster parents to die that night and seal Babs' path amongst either the Seelie or Unseelie... she instead chose to walk the line between by sacrificing one of her Fomorian attackers. While displeased with the choice, the Morrigan couldn't deny that her price had been met (as she never specified who must die so the others could live) and even admired her daughter's resourcefulness in finding the loophole in the bargain she offered. In addition to the items her foster parents bequeathed her, the Morrigan allowed her to keep the sacrificial dagger she gave Barbarah (her mother never calls her Babs)... as a reminder of the sometimes heavy price that must be made to receive or give a gift. Since then, Babs has wandered the land, helping those who need it... and can meet her price for her gifts; all the time walking the line between Seelie and Unseelie... the darkness and the light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 09-26-2016, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:50:06-07:00","id":992601,"title":"","content":"The one I'm kicking around right now is scion of \u200bDagda. Student that is also a burgeoning YouTube star, whose followers eventually becomes his cult, as he becomes God of the Internet. Its a little loose for now, but Ill tighten it up as I get more info.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12581-jedkight","name":"jedkight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:55:21-07:00","id":992632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jedkight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=992601#post992601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one I'm kicking around right now is scion of \u200bDagda. Student that is also a burgeoning YouTube star, whose followers eventually becomes his cult, as he becomes God of the Internet. Its a little loose for now, but Ill tighten it up as I get more info.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Build Your Own Purview section of the Companion should be very helpful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:58:43-07:00","id":992637,"title":"","content":"Created could encompass, say, a Scion who is a mummy and remembers their life before their death with their remains used millenia later to help make something ex nihilo right? Sitting somewhere between Prometheans and Arisen compared to the CofD, I know, but I was thinking about how one can get scary powerful mummies as well as the shambling servants you can create as shown in the KS relic preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:00:07-07:00","id":992638,"title":"","content":"I want to play a scion who is a wizard, because I love playing sorcerous characters. I am not sure which pantheon would be better for that, but at a glance I'm torn between the Theoi (Because I really like metamorphosis as a PSP) and the Netjer, because Egypt is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:18:34-07:00","id":992643,"title":"","content":"Vaughan Spartus- Satyr Reincarned Scion of Gallic Pantheon, I don't know which God.<br /> <br /> Basically the God for whom Vaughan is a Scion of reincarnated as a Satyr to disguise himself from the Theio, figuring they'd less likely suspect a Satyr of being of the Gallic Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:49:19-07:00","id":992654,"title":"","content":"I'm having a sudden crisis about whether or not my transwoman Incarnate Scion of Azar/Osiris who wants to reform the Netjer as a kinder, gentler Pantheon might be better suited as a Scion of Re, or possibly an adopted Scion of Hathor born of someone else.<br /> <br /> Also I really want to make a Scion of Mars tasked with handling the returning Nemetendevos threat (nevermind the fact that he couldn't care less about a war two thousand years past) and maybe a Scion of Tyr crused with lycanthropy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:10:28-07:00","id":992659,"title":"","content":"Wow, what's this jakki? You willingly considering making something besides Netjer scions? What upside down universe is this forum? Also do the Mars one sometime, that sounds baller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:19:06-07:00","id":992662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=992659#post992659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, what's this jakki? You willingly considering making something besides Netjer scions? What upside down universe is this forum? Also do the Mars one sometime, that sounds baller.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Netjer are my favorite, but that's no reason to ignore the other 11.5 Pantheons we're getting soon. Of everything in Scion, I'm actually most excited for Pantheons that are going to show up in Demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:36:02-07:00","id":992668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=992662#post992662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Netjer are my favorite, but that's no reason to ignore the other 11.5 Pantheons we're getting soon.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/986027-omen?p=986135#post986135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/986027-omen?p=986135#post986135\">Good luck ever getting me to stop picking Netjer when animal heads are an option.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I see you're clearly having a crisis here. The solution as I see it is more cowbell. On your cow head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:58:51-07:00","id":992715,"title":"","content":"Well this is more a start than a full character but my Idea was to have a scion created by the Norse God Loki when he stole fire from Odin's hearth and gave it the breath of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12592-kitsune","name":"Kitsune","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:19:34-07:00","id":992753,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoebe Finbar</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Divine Parent</b>: Poseidon<br /> <b>Callings</b>: Leader (Favored), Sage, Warrior<br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path</b>: Haunted Misfit (raised in a single parent household, spent most of her life running away from home chasing dreams and stories; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Occult, Survival)<br /> <b>Role Path</b>: &quot;Doesn't that make you <i>angry</i>? Don't you <i>care</i>?&quot; (After returning from Greece, dedicates herself to activism and stirring the hearts of people; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Leadership, Persuasion)<br /> <b>Relationship Path</b>: &quot;You were Fated for more than childish dreams.&quot; (Is opposed to her father's plans for her, and is willing to fight to get her way; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Close-combat, Athletics)</span><br /> <br /> Born in Ocean Beach, California. Phoebe was the only child to a single mother. As costs in California continued to grow out of hand, they eventually settled in the East County area of San Diego, the Alpine/Descanso area, so right up next to the Cleveland National Forest. It was an area that still had a bit of an 'old west' vibe, with lots of restaurants evoking the imagery, quite a few horse ranches. She spent a lot of time dealing with people riding them down hiking trails, or through the areas where she'd usually play, and got acquainted with the riders and their horses. Especially the horses. Things like The Firebringer Trilogy and The Last Unicorn were incredibly important to her when she was young.<br /> <br /> She and her mother didn't get along. Phoebe often ran away from home, scrounging up bus fair to make it at least as far as the coast. For reasons she couldn't express, the ocean had a soothing effect on her, especially the sensation of wave after wave hitting her.<br /> <br /> Growing up in a conservative community with exposure and access to liberal ideas embittered her quickly, and her mother, being of Irish descent with strong values, was not enthusiastic about her daughter's interest in pagan gods, books of magic, or the odd dreams she'd complain about. In one instance she went so far as to burn all of her daughter's books, on another occasion, she personally tried to perform an exorcism on her daughter.<br /> <br /> Life as a teenager wasn't much better. More and more she began to realize that a lot of the truths she'd been fed as a girl, the things she'd taken for granted as true, weren't. Her mother never bothered saving money for her college, and claimed that she should just 'get a scholarship' or 'get a grant'. The recession hit, and small towns were hit hard. She watched as one by one, stores began to close down. Any hopes of employment in her home town dwindled to waitressing at the same steakhouse her mother worked at. Indeed, her mother was increasingly insistent that Phoebe get to work to help pay the bills. Phoebe spiraled into a passion devouring depression, and as a desperate act, stole what money her mother had managed to save in order to fly to Greece. Corinth, more specifically.<br /> <br /> She'd had enough of humanity and made for the Fountain of Pirene. Heartbroken, she arrived only to find that the great spring of Pegasus had completely dried up. She leaped down to get a better look, and the moment her feet hit the ground, it began to shake. Water bubbled up, sweeping the dirt and dust away from the ruins. Phoebe drank from the fountain, uncertain of what to expect, but what happened is not something she ever imagined.<br /> <br /> She expected some form of transformation, like all the Greek myths, maybe even into a winged horse, like Pegasus himself, or even just a regular one. Anything would be preferable to human life with human problems, really. Instead, she was visited by her father, Poseidon. He laid out in no uncertain terms that she is his daughter, that she was to put aside childish dreams and fantasies, that Fate had a greater part for her to play in service to her divine family.<br /> <br /> Phoebe balked at that, recalling the story of Pegasus, broken by a golden bridle, of noble Areion, who in legend became little more than a king's favored mount. And her\u2014she'd been completely ignored until her existence was convenient for him. It was in that moment she realized: if Poseidon was her father, then those two horses of legend were her brothers, her actual siblings.<br /> <br /> Phoebe turned her back on her father, only grudgingly accepting his commands, if at all, and using what few brithrights he bestowed sparingly. After returning home, her mother confronted her about the money, then threw her out. But to Phoebe's astonishment, she learned that she'd become quite a bit more sturdy since her trip to the fountain. She still needed food, shelter, rest, but she could accomplish a lot more than her friends on a lot less. She took to the road, crashing on couches of friends and anyone of like mind.<br /> <br /> Through blogs and videos, her legend grew, especially when odd things start to come out of the woodwork wherever she goes.<br /> <br /> Purview wise she focuses on Metamorphosis, Beast (Horses) and Epic Strength, as she grows into her Ichor, she starts becoming increasingly dissatisfied with humanity, feeling the call of her equine kin more keenly. She spends increasingly more time as a horse - or rather, something a bit different. She becomes to horses what humans are to chimpanzees, and adopts a new overarching calling - to steal the fire of the gods and use it to uplift horses to the same level as humanity itself. (In our games, we tend to use the theft of fire myth as a parallel to Sophia breathing divine sparks into humanity)<br /> <br /> Stat wise, Phoebe is more Physical/Social, hot-blooded and quick to solve her problems by punching them (or kicking, as the case may be). Of note is Hermes, who is genuinely amused by her motivations and dreams, and takes it upon himself to place her in situations where her strength won't be of much use. She has some involvement with the Netjer through a bandmate, and has a scion of Dagda as a bit of a brother figure, with her Irish blood drawing some interest by unrelated gods, notably Macha and Fand\u2014who is always willing to explain to Phoebe that it's perfectly okay to abduct guys she likes and turn them into stallions. Where's the harm in that?<br /> <br /> Plus some potential involvement with Enbarr and Sleipnir, because horses with divine bloodties unite, right?<br /> <br /> Antagonist wise, the greatest threat is Athena. While Poseidon was responsible for creating horses, Athena is largely given credit for helping humans to domesticate and tame them, she's also the one who gave Bellerophon the golden bridle, which was necessary in order to break/tame Pegasus, Phoebe's older sibling. In the context of the game there is an organization forming that rounds up scions and puts them to work, known as Aeterna. It's run by a Scion of Horus, with one of Athena's daughter's near the top of the power structure, and constantly attempts to get in Phoebe's way. There's also a scion of Dian Cecht to round out their group.<br /> <br /> There's no chance Zeus would stomach the Hubris of a someone less than a god stealing the flame of the gods, but for now Phoebe is beneath his notice, so Athena contents herself with tormenting her cousin through scions of her own. It'll be interesting to see how far she gets in her ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":".  Fixed some issues with bouncing around between present and past tense. This was converted from notes taken while brainstorming with my friends, so sometimes it comes out more of a hustle, and I miss t 10-25-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:22:50-07:00","id":992754,"title":"","content":"I wanna play a Teenaged Scion of <b>Hephaestus</b>, a young somewhat-dorky socially-clueless-but-oddly-charismatic young man who is very much a technie, an electronics wiz, a hobbyist inventor, and overall more than a bit of a tinkerer. He has some friends, whom are very loyal to him-- walk through fire type friends,-- but isn't really in with the popular crowd at school. Despite that, he is generally well-liked and while he's a bit of a Dork he generally is well-thought of even outside of his social circle even if he's viewed as a bit naive and sometimes weird. The kind of kid that WANTS to go to the school dance, but has no idea how to ask a girl out, who is not infrequently getting in trouble for doing stuff he probably shouldn't. He was orphaned as a young age, but is being raised by his Aunt Thetis, and hopes to be a great Scientist-Hero when he comes of age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:52:08-07:00","id":992792,"title":"","content":"<b>Ula Stone</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent</b>: Skadi<br /> <b>Callings</b>: Sage (Favored), Healer, Lover<br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path</b>: Carved from basalt. (Created by Skadi's husband, Njord, by carving her from basalt, with waves and seafoam for hair; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Athletics, Survival)<br /> <b>Role Path</b>: &quot;High wind warning for the rest of the week, heavy snows.&quot; (Her weather forecasts are always right; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Culture, Science)<br /> <b>Relationship Path</b>: &quot;You have all of my grace, and his kindness.&quot; (Kind-hearted daughter of Skadi.; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Medicine, Stealth)<br /> <br /> In the time after Skadi joined the Aesir in Asgard, demanding her father's lands as well as weregild, she also demanded a husband. In response Odin blindfolded her, and bade her choose from the unmarried men of Asgard by feeling their feet. She chose the one with the finest feet, hoping to win the beautiful Baldur, but it was Njord, the Vanir Sea-King. He was good-looking and kind enough, so they married. Skadi's homeland, Thyrmheim in Jotunheim, and her inherited lands in Asgard, were in the mountains; but Njord could not bring himself to dwell long away from the sea. His home in Asgard, Noatun, and his Vanaheim home on the other side of the ocean, on the other hand, made Skadi uncomfortable; she complained about the noise of the sea-birds and the constant sound of the tide.<br /> <br /> As his bride's displeasure continued to mount, Njord led his daughter Freya to the shores of Noatun, there he carved a small girl from dark basalt, and fixed sea foam for her hair. Bidding his daughter to work her seidr magic, to sing a spell around the work of art, Njord took and applied a drop of his wife's blood, and the creation came to life - a daughter to his bride in spirit, if not by birth. The girl was a fine thing, with dark brown skin and hair the same shining white of the sea foam used to form it. When he brought his creation home to his wife, she was furious. Fidelity, responsibility, and oaths are all of utmost importance to Skadi, and here her husband had assigned to her the greatest responsibility of all, without her consent. It was the final straw in their relationship, and she left Njord's hall forever for her mountain home.<br /> <br /> Heartbroken, but fearing for the child's safety (he knew well the Aesir and their track record toward Jotuns) Njord called up Mani the moon god, and bid him take the child in his chariot to a place where she could grow in safety, for Mani is often known for his stewardship of abused and forsaken children. Mani did as he was asked, and a small child was left, appearing somewhat mysteriously at a designated drop off point, outside a fire station in Maine. When the men found her, there was only the basket, a small girl, and a pendant reading 'Ula'.<br /> <br /> Ula Stone grew up in the system, and she <i>hated</i> the sea. Whenever she stared at it for any appreciable length of time, a longing of the heart she couldn't explain would steal over her, one that could darken her thoughts for days. She had a quick mind and a kind soul, however, and when she graduated she moved as soon as she was able, traveling south to upstate New York. She settled in a small town within the Adirondack mountain range, and found what work she could. As a way of connecting with a community where most families had existed for generations - had known each other for generations, Ula started a community blog, chronicling events and whatever news in the area she could scrounge up. On a whim, she began doing astrology reports and weather readings, but an odd pattern began to emerge - where it came to the weather she was always, 100%, without fail correct. More locals began to follow her blog, placing bets on when the streak would come to an end. Old men and women would joke that their knees would ache whenever Ula walked by. Before long, Ula began to spread her net beyond the town, first to the mountains surrounding them, and then to much of New York itself. The community even took her and put her on local television, where she'd broadcast her weather reports an hour each night. Ula became a curiosity, going so far as to put together a late night talk show for all the night owls.<br /> <br /> It was a year plagued by storms, New York city was racked by hurricane winds, flooding, and record snow fall, the mountains weren't much better. Several hikers and vacationers had gotten stranded, separated from town by storms Ula had failed to predict - the streak was over. Rounding up men and women from her community, Ula built a party to go in search of the missing people, but over the course of the expedition, she became separated from the group.<br /> <br /> Time passed, and while others might have succumbed to hypothermia, Ula felt - fine, really. The wind and the winter cold was harsh, but bearable. She became more concerned when she found the search party - or what was left of them. Many of them had been ripped open, their blood frozen solid inside of them. Something was hunting them through the woods.<br /> <br /> It was only by Skadi's intervention that Ula survived, she took the creation that was meant to be her daughter in, explained the world to her. She told her that the bridge she'd hoped to build between the Aesir and the Jotuns was crumbling, and that more and more, the world would not be a safe place. Skadi begged her daughter's forgiveness, and charged her with stopping the chaotic actions of her kin, before they do something that can't be taken back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-25-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:05:27-07:00","id":992795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=992792#post992792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ula Stone</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ula may be my favorite concept thus far. Phoebe is really good, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:38:07-07:00","id":992917,"title":"","content":"Alex Mercer is absolutely sure of two things: her younger brothers are always covered in dirt; and pancakes make everything better. When her brothers got sick, Alex made them pancakes. When Mom got home from work after bed time, Alex made her pancakes. As if by magic, those golden brown, syrup and butter slathered pancakes always put a smile on everyone's face.<br /> <br /> Its not that she only knows how to make one dish, its just the dish that Alex likes best. She doesn't know why, but there's something so... zen about mixing and cooking the batter. She might not even know who she is cooking for, but, by the time she's done someone will need it.<br /> <br /> She's not the smartest, but she runs ger family, while her mother works two jobs. The house is clean, her siblings listen, and she's always there to help with homework. Well, except for four days a week, when she works at Mashall's diner. Technically she's a waitress, but Alex is more informed than the owner, Owen. <br /> <br /> Alex doesn't know it yet, but, she is the daughter of Frigg and things are about to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:24:17-07:00","id":992976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/7/74798/1666538-alex_mercer.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Alex Mercer </a>you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:31:17-07:00","id":992979,"title":"","content":"I'm sitting on a Scion of a syncretized Coyote-Renard, who really wants to shoot dear old Dad with an enchanted shotgun because he's actually kind of a creepy asshole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:10:52-07:00","id":993022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=992654#post992654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a sudden crisis about whether or not my transwoman Incarnate Scion of Azar/Osiris who wants to reform the Netjer as a kinder, gentler Pantheon might be better suited as a Scion of Re, or possibly an adopted Scion of Hathor born of someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmmmm, all those options sound sweet. Azar for the rebirth theme, Hetheru because she would be an unambigously good divine parent in a game that likes to emphasize the way deities can be callous from a human-centered point of view. And Re... the tension between having authority and power as part of her birthright and wanting to bring change that will undermine the foundation of that power would be glorious.<br /> If you end up exploring any of those options, do you plan to share the story with the forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:55:28-07:00","id":993084,"title":"","content":"This is a translation from a Gurps game my sister once ran, it was similar to Scion, but focused more on initiating into various magical traditions and mystery cults.<br /> <br /> <b>Isabella (</b><b>Citlalmina)</b><b> Heladio</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent</b>: Ixchel<br /> <b>Callings</b>: Leader (Favored), Hunter, Warrior<br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path</b>: Born of Night, taken in by the Moon. (Descendant of a long line of werejaguars which can trace their origins back to Tezcatlipoca, adopted by Ixchel; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Close-Combat, Survival)<br /> <b>Role Path</b>: &quot;I will restore the old empire, and banish the bloodlust that has consumed the gods.&quot; (Ambition is to return to Mexico and return it to the glory it enjoyed during the height of the Mayan Empire, banishing the influences of Catholicism and the Spanish; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Culture, Leadership)<br /> <b>Relationship Path</b>: &quot;The path of your father is seductive, I chose you for your strength.&quot; (Adopted scion of Ixchel, Jaguar goddess of war, childbirth, and medicine; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Athletics, Medicine)<br /> <br /> Isabella Heladio belongs to a long line of Jaguar priestesses out of Mexico. The gods of the Maya sought a means to change the Fate of their people, performing complex often dark rituals from the dawn of their pantheon's existence. The magic they worked changed them, turning them into something new, and ultimately more savage and primal than their previous incarnations. In the end, they could not change Fate, and their empire was all but lost by the time the Spanish arrived. The Aztecs, and what remained of the Maya, were clever and resourceful, keeping their lineages pure in whatever ways they could, hiding their very languages under the noses of the Spanish. Isabella's grandmother was the first to leave Mexica, settling in Brooklyn. She had two daughters, both of them possessed of the same gifts she possessed, but her youngest involved herself with the occult, and same sorts of gangs she had hoped to spare them from by leaving their homeland. In an effort to alter her daughter's course, they both perished, leaving Helena, Isabella's mother, alone.<br /> <br /> Helena swore off her inhuman nature, performing a ritual to cast the jaguar spirit from her, body and soul. Afterward she swore off the occult and chose to acknowledge only her Spanish heritage. She moved to Manhattan, met a man named Francisco, a doctor from Spain, and they soon married. They had two children, Isabella and Adrian, of which Isabella was the oldest. Both of them were curious about their heritage and ancestry, their mother's defensiveness only encouraged them. Isabella committed herself to study, using iron determination in place of a quick mind, and eventually was accepted into Columbia university. Adrian, still in High School, took a different approach, one eerily reminiscent of Helena's own sister. Isabella's life was relatively normal, until her brother got himself involved with a gang called 'Las Cinco Muertes'. One day, when picking Adrian up from school, she confronted them and their leader, ordered them to leave her brother out of whatever schemes they were up to. A fight broke out with her primal heritage more than carrying her through, until one of the leader's henchman shot her.<br /> <br /> Her dreams in the hospital were clouded, like smoke trapped in obsidian. In her dreams she experienced the thrill of the hunt, of running on all fours, of sacred blood rites and sacred pools deep underground. After she left the hospital, life was quite a bit different. She became increasingly distant from her family, exploring magic and her newfound shapeshifting powers, she didn't notice things were going south until the cult abducted her brother. <br /> <br /> The leader of Las Cinco Muertes, 'the five deaths', was a man calling himself 'Mecatl', with a strange accent and even stranger ambitions. He gathered to himself four Lieutenants, and initiated each of them into his cult by persuading them to commit specific highly ritualized murders: Javier, death by hanging. Thomas, death by poison. Demian, death by drowning. Claudio, death by burning. And Mecatl himself, whose favored method was ritually flaying his enemies alive. What's more, he represented the last in a line of Mayan Kings, and murdered his elder brother in order to seize a birthright - the Bracelet of Kings, a relic that the city states of the Mayan Empire spent its final years warring over. It possessed the power to open various existent gates to the Overworld. Mecatl's ambition was to use his cult, the bracelet, and a daughter of Tezcatlipoca, to open the gates to Xibalba, so that he might ride forth as a god among men, in service to the Xibalbans. <br /> <br /> But Isabella, or Citlalmina, as she came to call herself, was far too stubborn to serve as a puppet. Adrian, however, was of weaker will, and in a far more vulnerable place. 'His' own spirit began to stir, not long after her sister's, with Thomas's help, he began to dose Adrian with hormones and drugs without their knowing. The more her body transitioned, the more adamant her primal spirit became, infecting her thoughts and influencing her dreams. Horrified and confused, Adrian returned to the only group that had offered her answers in the past. Mecatl took her in, promising to help Adrian 'prove he's a man'. The gang tormented her, demeaning her even more so than other women in a dark exploration of how hispanic gangs often respond to queer behavior. Adrian was little more than an animal to them.<br /> <br /> Finally, Mecatl led Adrian into the Overworld, to the gates of Xibalba, and offered him the chance to prove once and for all whether she was a man, or wild beast. He began a ritual, and try as Adrian might, she couldn't resist joining in, her jaguar spirit asserting full control as she changed for the first time. The gate to Xibalba began to open, and in a moment of realization and horror, she threw herself against it, forcing it shut. <br /> <br /> Mecatl was furious, cursing her for nothing but a wild animal. With the spirits he had enslaved, he captured and imprisoned Adrian, throwing her into some old temple to a forgotten god.<br /> <br /> With the help of Hypatia (who managed to survive Alexandria by making a deal with the goddess Bastet, a deal which offered her some degree of immortality) Isabella managed to track down Mecatl's lieutenants, and with the help of her friends, she killed each of them, save Demian who had already turned away from the cult after all he'd been forced to do to Adrian, and Thomas, who Mecatl had betrayed by using his own magically enhanced cocktail of hormones and drugs against him. Isabella confronted her mother, forcing her to accept the spirit she'd struggled to cut from herself, and set out to stop Mecatl once and for all.<br /> <br /> A skeletal jaguar spirit, a shade sent by Tezcatlipoca himself, had already warned Mecatl of their arrival, and when Isabella found him he was garbed in full regalia, his birthright of flayed skin (his brother's) proudly on display. Isabella fought him, while he and the spirit tempted her in the voice of her divine father. In the end she only barely managed to kill him, and then only by the help of her friends. The gate to Xibalba closed completely, sealing itself, and she claimed the Bracelet of Kings for herself. <br /> <br /> Ixchel came to her then, adopting her as her own and praising her for her resistance to her father's manipulations, a presence she still feels in her dreams, speaking to her through a smokey obsidian mirror she can never long be rid of. Isabella left Manhattan for Mexico, armed with the Bracelet and a few other birthrights, she hopes to seize power and bring about sweeping reforms that can make Mexica a place of science, academia, and art. <br /> <br /> <b>Adrianna (Ichtaca</b><b>)</b><b> Heladio</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent</b>: Xochiquetzal <br /> <b>Callings</b>: Lover (Favored), Hunter, Guardian<br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path</b>: Jaguar spirit trapped in a human body. (Exhibited transgender tendencies from an early age, forced to conceal it due to cultural norms and shame; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Empathy, Subterfuge)<br /> <b>Role Path</b>: &quot;I will not live in my sister's shadow, and inspire Legend in my own right.&quot; (Hopes to restore respect for women, and with the help of fertility rites, reestablish her people ; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Culture, Medicine)<br /> <b>Relationship Path</b>: &quot;You are the moon to your sister's sun, just as radiant, but easier on the eyes.&quot; (Adopted scion of Xochiquetzal, goddess of women, beauty, and female sexual power; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Occult, Persuasion)<br /> <br /> Isabella's younger sister, growing up in Hispanic and Latino communities, even with a home in upscale Manhattan to retreat to, did not experience much support for her 'odd behaviors' from an early age. She quickly learned to cover these up, burying them in shame and self-disappointment. She instead flung herself into proving her worth as a man, something she had a hard time accomplishing when her older sister was seemingly more of a man than she could ever be. When she got into fights\u2014and she did, often\u2014she always won, Adrian usually needed her to come to the rescue. Things were going to be different with Las Cinco Muertes, she felt accepted. She had her <i>own</i> way to connect to their roots, and her sister stepping in to interfere only pushed her in deeper.<br /> <br /> Of course, that all went to hell when her body started changing with seemingly no rhyme or reason. When feelings began to build around herself and one of Mecatl's lieutenants, a soft spoken boy named Demian. On more than one occasion he'd stopped just short of asking her to come away with him, to leave Mecatl and his cult behind, until they found some place they could be safe. After Mecatl imprisoned Ichtaca, Demian sought out Isabella and her friends, and was instrumental in helping her locate Mecatl in the spirit world.<br /> <br /> While trapped inside an old abandoned temple, Ichtaca met the goddess Xochiquetzal, who claimed precious little worship or acknowledgement in the modern age. She took Ichtaca in, comforting her until such a time as she was able to escape, and help her sister seek revenge on Mecatl. <br /> <br /> <b>Mecatl</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent</b>: Xipe Totec <br /> <b>Callings</b>: Leader (Favored), Warrior, Liminal<br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path</b>: Last king of the Maya (The last in the bloodline, grew up on a farm with his grandfather and brother. On his Grandfather's death, murdered his brother to claim his birthright; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Close-Combat, Occult)<br /> <b>Role Path</b>: &quot;I will ride into Xibalaba and become as a god.&quot; (Wants to give the Xibalbans free reign in return for apotheosis; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Leadership, Persuasion)<br /> <b>Relationship Path</b>: &quot;Fail me, and perish.&quot; (Servant to Xipe Totec and Tezcatlipoca; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Academics, Athletics)<br /> <br /> Mecatl's older brother claimed he would seek out the lost line of jaguar priests, and take one as a bride, relying on her advice and assistance in order to build a new kingdom in Mexica. Disgusted by the idea of his brother bedding with a wild beast, Mecatl sought the attention of spirits, and found one willing to listen. The spirit seemed just as disgruntled as he, and was willing to assist. It acted as an intermediary between Mecatl and the gods, teaching the boy a ritual by which he might usurp his brother's birthright. On the day of their grandfather's death, Mecatl attacked his brother with a heavy stone, cracking open the skull. From there, he flayed his brother alive, taking the skin as a birthright, as well as their grandfather's relic: The Bracelet of Kings. <br /> <br /> His dreams and the spirits spoke to him, leading him all the way to New York, even if he had no intention of sleeping with a wild animal, he'd need the assistance of one to accomplish what he'd set out to do.<br /> <br /> <b>Disclaimer</b>: This is not meant to be cosmologically accurate. It takes many liberties with the lore and history itself, but felt appropriate in GURPs, and seems manageable in Scion, particularly as a setting where actual gods who go around flaying people and wearing their skins exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:34:42-07:00","id":993131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=992638#post992638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to play a scion who is a wizard, because I love playing sorcerous characters. I am not sure which pantheon would be better for that, but at a glance I'm torn between the Theoi (Because I really like metamorphosis as a PSP) and the Netjer, because Egypt is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>PSPs are now often the cultural magic of a people and frankly I'm sure you can probably fluff damn near any boon as casting spells and look totally awesome while doing it, but actual sorcerers in setting are mortals who wield stolen power of the gods. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I wonder if that's a potential pre-visitation origin that might be fun to explore for a character. They were a sorcerer, they <i>are </i>a Scion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:19:37-07:00","id":993159,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that a sorcerous type of character is probably just using the Sage Calling and fluffing their Purviews and stuff a particular way. When I said sorcerer, I didn't mean the formal definition, I just meant someone who knows about magical stuff and acts like a sage, summoner, that sort of think.<br /> <br /> I also think shapeshifting is cool, hence metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> Who would be good gods for a sorcerous kind of character like that? Thoth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:30:55-07:00","id":993166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=993159#post993159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that a sorcerous type of character is probably just using the Sage Calling and fluffing their Purviews and stuff a particular way. When I said sorcerer, I didn't mean the formal definition, I just meant someone who knows about magical stuff and acts like a sage, summoner, that sort of think.<br /> <br /> I also think shapeshifting is cool, hence metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> Who would be good gods for a sorcerous kind of character like that? Thoth?</div> </div> </div> </div>His name is <i>Djehuty</i>, thank you very much. And yes, he's there for the knowledge side of things while Aset is there to give you command over true names. Djehuty and Hermes get mushed together by medieval scholars to become the patron of alchemists as well, should you go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:31:02-07:00","id":993167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=993159#post993159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that a sorcerous type of character is probably just using the Sage Calling and fluffing their Purviews and stuff a particular way. When I said sorcerer, I didn't mean the formal definition, I just meant someone who knows about magical stuff and acts like a sage, summoner, that sort of think.<br /> <br /> I also think shapeshifting is cool, hence metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> Who would be good gods for a sorcerous kind of character like that? Thoth?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isis/Aset is the definitive 'Sorcerer' in Egyptian mythology, she also knows 'True Names' and things like that. Thoth is more of a Sage but he also has legends in which he does Sorcerous things. Odin is a god of magic who goes out of his way to learn every type he can, including learning Seidr under Freya as a woman/crossdressing. Loki is a mother of witches. The expression 'Hermetic Magic' is literally derived from Hermes. These are just the ones that immediately spring to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:09:44-07:00","id":993271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=993166#post993166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His name is <i>Djehuty</i>, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is good enough for Mardi Gras, its good enough for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:10:36-07:00","id":993298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=993166#post993166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His name is <i>Djehuty</i>, thank you very much. And yes, he's there for the knowledge side of things while Aset is there to give you command over true names. Djehuty and Hermes get mushed together by medieval scholars to become the patron of alchemists as well, should you go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is his proper name, I think it's okay to call him Thoth generally.<br /> <br /> Similarly, we don't all refer to Egypt as Kemet preferentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:36:08-07:00","id":993486,"title":"","content":"Name: Sophia Kallis<br /> Divine Parent: Athena<br /> Callings: Creator, Sage (Favored), Hunter <br /> <br /> Origin Path: Child prodigy of the science fair circuit. (Hailed as gifted from a young age, was quickly drawn to a love of science and explored this passion by entering and winning many science fairs and competitions.) <br /> Role Path : &quot;There's never been a case I couldn't solve!&quot; ( After solving the theft of a rival science project she was framed for at a competition, became interested in solving crimes and eventually became a well known private investigator and police consultant.)<br /> Relationship Path: &quot;I've always been proud of your craftiness.&quot; ( Daughter of Athena tasked with investigating potential threats to the Theoi.)<br /> <br /> From a young age, it was clear Sophia was intelligent and inquisitive. Raised by a single father who was a crime scene technician, as soon as she could read she began to pour through any books she could get her hands on. She especially enjoyed her father's old college science textbooks. Recognizing a budding passion in his daughter, he encouraged her to conduct experiments and began entering her into science fairs and other competitions. Sophia quickly became known as a prodigy, always placing in the top three of every contest she entered and winning first more often than not.<br /> <br /> When she was 13, a new passion began to grow as she became fixated with mystery novels. She loved imagining herself as a great detective solving mysteries and catching criminals. Sophia's two passions unexpectedly collided a year later when she entered a prestigious national science fair. The talk of the fair was that the grand prize was going to be a close contest between Sophia's entry and that of another child prodigy. Yet when the boy's project mysteriously disappeared, only to be found destroyed under Sophia's table, it seemed like she would be disqualified. However, in light of her protests that she was innocent the head judge, a older man in a wheelchair who looked strangely familiar to Sophia, told her to solve the case and find the real culprit. As she examined the crime scene, she found that the clues just jumped out to her, and she was quickly able to identify the culprit as the mother of another contestant who was the popular pick for third place. <br /> <br /> From that day forward, she knew she wanted to be a real detective. She worked incredibly hard all through high school and college, eventually earning her private investigator's license at the age of 20. The morning after, she was visited by two people. One was the wheelchair bound judge who had given her the chance to prove her innocence and the other was a woman who bore a striking resemblance to Sophia. The woman was her mother, Athena, and the man was her uncle Hephaestus. Athena explained that she had sent Hephaestus to that science fair and set up the sabotage as a way to test Sophia and nudge her into her destiny. Athena explained that Olympus had many enemies who lurked in the shadows and plotted their downfall in secret. The gods were in need of a bright young investigator who could learn about these threats and bring them into the light to meet justice. Her uncle then presented her with a gift, a pocket knife that he referred to as an &quot;Olympus Army Knife&quot; that he explained would always have the right tool for the job. Armed with only her wits and her knife, Sophia Kallis quickly embraced her destiny to become the investigator for the gods!<br /> <br /> Notes: Sophia was my first Scion character. She's inspired by my love of shows like McGyver, Monk, and Psych. The idea is that she combines the hyper perceptive observational abilities of characters like Sherlock Holmes or Shawn Spencer with McGyver's scientific knowledge and ability to improvise gadgets from materials found in the field. Her eventual destiny is to become Goddess of Investigation, watching over detectives and scientists alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:27:27-07:00","id":993733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=993166#post993166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His name is <i>Djehuty</i>, thank you very much. And yes, he's there for the knowledge side of things while Aset is there to give you command over true names. Djehuty and Hermes get mushed together by medieval scholars to become the patron of alchemists as well, should you go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the mashing began in the Ptolemaic period well before the Middle Ages - and then the Romans threw in Mercury for good measure, hence the eventual title of &quot;Thrice-Great&quot; in Alchemical lore (though personally I think that's redundant as Mercury didn't show up in a recognizable form until Greek syncretization, so has never really had a distinct identity from Hermes unlike some Roman gods and their Greek counterparts - you really want to make a figure Thrice-Great you'll need to throw some tie to Wotan in their too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:13:24-07:00","id":993835,"title":"","content":"I think my Incarnate of Osiris is going on the back-burner for the moment, as she's torn in a good three directions (do I want to queer up the Osiris myth as a transgender narrative, do I want to force the Netjer to be a kinder and gentler Pantheon at great cost and effort, or do I just want a self-insert who happens to be delightfully Egyptian-themed) that are all fairly contradictory and I can't settle on one.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I think my Created of Anubis (who I'm tentatively naming Ms. Shabby the Ushabti, a tool to help keep the veil between living and dead un-meddled with so her creator can do her job - but then suddenly, that pesky free will strikes and she wants to be more than a rock/slave) and my Born of Apollo (who needs a name and is trying to become the snake and prophecy goddess of the Theoi due to a perceived kinship with Python, killed at her father's hand long ago at Delphi) will take the limelight. I'm also chewing on some idea for a Scion of Tyr who somehow deals heavily with werewolves, but I don't truly know enough about the Aesir to develop that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:33:41-07:00","id":993862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=993835#post993835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my Incarnate of Osiris is going on the back-burner for the moment, as she's torn in a good three directions (do I want to queer up the Osiris myth as a transgender narrative, do I want to force the Netjer to be a kinder and gentler Pantheon at great cost and effort, or do I just want a self-insert who happens to be delightfully Egyptian-themed) that are all fairly contradictory and I can't settle on one.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I think my Created of Anubis (who I'm tentatively naming Ms. Shabby the Ushabti, a tool to help keep the veil between living and dead un-meddled with so her creator can do her job - but then suddenly, that pesky free will strikes and she wants to be more than a rock/slave) and my Born of Apollo (who needs a name and is trying to become the snake and prophecy goddess of the Theoi due to a perceived kinship with Python, killed at her father's hand long ago at Delphi) will take the limelight. I'm also chewing on some idea for a Scion of Tyr who somehow deals heavily with werewolves, but I don't truly know enough about the Aesir to develop that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of them, but especially the born of Apollo. Ophion was a titan associated with snakes, so you could always name her Sophie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:38:28-07:00","id":994435,"title":"","content":"Redwood is unlike the rest of her satyr kin, wholly uninterested in drunken revelry and sexual escapes her entire life; when another satyr tried to force himself upon her, she blinded him in one eye and turned her back on the Dionysian troupe forever. She wandered the wild places of the world and grew angry at man's encroachment upon it, but hers was the steely anger of a woman wronged, not the raving fury of the Maenads she had left behind, and so she took up the role of a primal avenger, watching from the forest and acting without mercy on any who tried to harm the natural world. Artemis appeared to her in one of Northern California's mighty oceans of trees and appointed her their guardian, gifting her with a divine bow and the name she carries to this day.<br /> <br /> Over the years, Redwood has seen her hatred of humanity cool, softened by the reverence afforded to the mighty trees by countless tourists, rangers, and local hikers, but she does not forgive any perceived sleight against her home or the flora and fauna that share it with her. Her disgust towards to the mindless excesses of her kin has only grown with years and distance, and she's sworn to kill the man she blinded if she ever sees him again. A part of her deeply resents Dionysus himself for (in her eyes) leading the rest of her people astray to waste the ages in mindless vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:05:38-07:00","id":994589,"title":"","content":"Name: Hitomi Tsukino (She's Japanese American, so name is in Western order)<br /> Divine Parent: Tsukiyomi<br /> Callings: Trickster (Favored), Liminal, Warrior? (Not sure on the third one)<br /> <br /> Origin Path: Always the class clown. (Middle child in family of workaholic parents. Acted out with pranks and jokes for attention.)<br /> Role Path: Break-in artist turned security expert. (Began breaking into places for the adrenaline rush of it, got caught by a security company in the middle of a demo, were so impressed by her skills they hired her to test their services)<br /> Relationship Path: &quot;Would it kill you to show a little affection?&quot; (Daughter of Tsukiyomi dissatisfied with her father's distant nature)<br /> <br /> Growing up as the middle child and only daughter of her family, Hitomi was used to being invisible. Her mother was a world famous astronomer and her father was an aspiring astronaut turned founder of a private company trying to achieve space travel after a heart condition kept him out. As such, they were never home, always working. What time they were home they spent doting on Hitomi's baseball ace older brother or her math genius younger brother. So, like most kids she began to act out. She became the class clown, telling jokes and pulling pranks to try and earn her parents' attention. Yet no matter what she did, her parents rarely seemed to have time for her. The only thing she found solace in was the strangely peaceful feeling of belonging she got when she looked at the moon.<br /> <br /> Eventually, as she got older she figured if people were going to treat her as invisible she'd take advantage of it. She began sneaking around, going places behind her parents' backs. She found such a rush in sneaking around she even began breaking into places. She never really felt the need to take anything, at least not anything important or valuable. Maybe a glass of milk from the neighbor's fridge or a pen from a teacher's desk, petty souvenirs. Really, the thrill for her was all in the actual sneaking in and out, and she was really good at it. So she kept on doing it and doing it, very rarely getting caught. <br /> <br /> It all paid off after she graduated high school. She moved out on her own, crashing with some friends as she pondered her future. One day, on a whim she decided to break into an office building. After a few days of casing the place, she made her move. Parkouring her way into a second floor window, things were going smoothly for a while as she avoided people, slunk through blind spots in security cameras, and stole a sandwich from a breakroom fridge. As she sat there in an empty room eating it, she was surprised when a large group of people entered. Turns out that a security company looking for a contract was showing off their services to the board members of the company that owned the building. The building owners were furious and were going to call the police when the security consultant stopped them. He grilled Hitomi heavily on how she had gotten there, and why she had broken in. When her explanation revealed several vulnerabilities in their security net, and she explained that she wasn't going to take anything she just wanted to break in for fun, the security consultant saw an opportunity. He offered her a job. She would try to break into places this company protected to help highlight weak points in their security. Hitomi was delighted, and she accepted the job immediately.<br /> <br /> A few years later, Hitomi got an unusual request from the company she worked for. A hotel nearby was hosting an important person, although details were scarce on who. Her boss wanted her to see if she could sneak in, find the person's room and see if she could make it inside. Apparently the hotel was concerned about assassins. Figuring a job was a job, Hitomi went about preparing her break in, and on the night of her job a full moon shone brightly on her successful attempt. She was surprised to find that this important person was a seemingly plain Japanese salaryman. Just as she was about to leave, figuring she had the wrong room, the man called her out by name even though his back was turned to her. With a shimmer of moonlight his clothing changed into ornate robes. He explained that he was Tsukiyomi, and that he was her true father, conceived when he fooled Hitomi's mother by taking the form of her mortal father. He then continued by saying that this job was a test to make sure Hitomi was truly skilled enough to justify him putting effort into developing her potential. He presented her with a mask, carved into the shape of a rabbit's face, and told her he expected much from her.<br /> <br /> Hitomi is a little unsure of her life now. While she loves her new abilities and the new places they let her sneak into, she's let down that she has yet another parent that seems to barely notice her. She's now determined that if nothing else, she's going to earn the respect of her father and make him pay attention to her.<br /> <br /> Notes: My second Scion character. I was looking at the purviews of Tsukiyomi in 1st Ed and their boons when I realized what a great cat burglar a Scion of Tsukiyomi would make. Yet as I built the character I realized she wasn't a thief and instead she became this adrenaline junkie break in artist. If you're wondering about her mask, it's supposed to look like the ANBU masks from Naruto. She has a rabbit motif, and her calling card when she breaks into somewhere is a little oragami bunny. I kind of had the idea she could become the Goddess of the Obscuring Darkness, darkness that hides people and protects them, as a way to do a good deity of darkness. I'm sure she'd get thieves that would pray to her, but I imagine she's also the goddess who would protect say, that poor abused wife who finally had enough and who is running and hiding and Hitomi would send her shadows to hide her from her abuser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:08:38-07:00","id":994592,"title":"","content":"So my table has expressed interest in picking up Scion 2e and here are their character concepts so far:<br /> <br /> 1) The daughter of an Inuit polar bear god who covers her nose instead of face palming. She's supposed to be an intellectual type character and I'm already thinking of letting her take any knacks for a werebear if those are detailed in the Beastiary.<br /> <br /> 2) A member of the Catholic Inquisition (So I'm pretty interested in how monotheism is treated in 2e. If there's room to do it, what I'm going to do is have this player be a chosen of an angel and the Inquisition would have been retooled in the late 1800's to basically hunt down monsters/titanspawn/evil scions and otherwise provide the same benefit's to his character that a parent god's cult would. Regardless, there's going to be quite a bit of homebrew to facilitate this character concept).<br /> <br /> 3) A wizard type character based off Harry Dresden from the Dresden Files.... which is amusing because if any of you read the Dresden Files, Harry is friends with therianthropes (werewolves in the books) and a holy knight (Michael Carpenter). The group did not coordinate these character concepts.<br /> <br /> Judging by the character's my players are coming up with, it's looking like I'll be treating them to a supernatural mystery game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:51:49-07:00","id":994669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994435#post994435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redwood is unlike the rest of her satyr kin, wholly uninterested in drunken revelry and sexual escapes her entire life; when another satyr tried to force himself upon her, she blinded him in one eye and turned her back on the Dionysian troupe forever. She wandered the wild places of the world and grew angry at man's encroachment upon it, but hers was the steely anger of a woman wronged, not the raving fury of the Maenads she had left behind, and so she took up the role of a primal avenger, watching from the forest and acting without mercy on any who tried to harm the natural world. Artemis appeared to her in one of Northern California's mighty oceans of trees and appointed her their guardian, gifting her with a divine bow and the name she carries to this day.<br /> <br /> Over the years, Redwood has seen her hatred of humanity cool, softened by the reverence afforded to the mighty trees by countless tourists, rangers, and local hikers, but she does not forgive any perceived sleight against her home or the flora and fauna that share it with her. Her disgust towards to the mindless excesses of her kin has only grown with years and distance, and she's sworn to kill the man she blinded if she ever sees him again. A part of her deeply resents Dionysus himself for (in her eyes) leading the rest of her people astray to waste the ages in mindless vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) A member of the Catholic Inquisition (So I'm pretty interested in how monotheism is treated in 2e. If there's room to do it, what I'm going to do is have this player be a chosen of an angel and the Inquisition would have been retooled in the late 1800's to basically hunt down monsters/titanspawn/evil scions and otherwise provide the same benefit's to his character that a parent god's cult would. Regardless, there's going to be quite a bit of homebrew to facilitate this character concept).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds a bit like asking the Neo-Nazis to retool to hunt down titanspawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The daughter of an Inuit polar bear god who covers her nose instead of face palming. She's supposed to be an intellectual type character and I'm already thinking of letting her take any knacks for a werebear if those are detailed in the Beastiary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually an interesting concept, though I'm not really sure what face-palming has to do with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's supposed to look like the ANBU masks from Naruto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof. Naruto.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He offered her a job. She would try to break into places this company protected to help highlight weak points in their security.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever see <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sneakers_(1992_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Sneakers</a>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her mother was a world famous astronomer and her father was an aspiring astronaut turned founder of a private company trying to achieve space travel after a heart condition kept him out. [...] Hitomi's baseball ace older brother or her math genius younger brother</div> </div> </div> </div>So her parents are both exceptionally world-famous? Does this factor into her character at all?<br /> Her other siblings are apparently lesser Heroes themselves @_@<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He explained that he was Tsukiyomi, and that he was her true father, conceived when he fooled Hitomi's mother by taking the form of her mortal father.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose this form of rape <i>is</i> the basis of King Arthur's story, but think carefully when including that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Overall the concept feels a bit frenetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:04:32-07:00","id":994731,"title":"","content":"@Jachra<br /> <br /> Honestly, Hitomi's backstory is something that's a work in progress. The key points are mostly to establish her as that &quot;invisible middle child &quot; who acts out for attention. I'm more than willing to change some details about the specifics. Mostly I just needed to create a reason why she starts sneaking around and breaking into things without being a thief.<br /> <br /> The security consultant thing was actually a suggestion a friend made. I think he had actually been watching a show about a guy who used to be a thief who would break into places to show people how unsecure their home or business was when he made the suggestion. However I may have to check out that movie. <br /> <br /> As for her conception, I was thinking more of that one time Zeus did it in Greek myth, but yeah it's definitely a squicky thing even if it is an established thing in myth. I know my playgroup wouldn't find issue with it, but that's definitely a detail I'd change if I was dealing with anyone else. I'm not the type to normally include rape in my characters' back stories. I really was just going for something I saw once in a myth.<br /> <br /> And I'll defend my use of a visual nod to Naruto by saying that the writing may be atrocious but despite the plot holes, obvious retcons between parts one and two, and the poorly written main characters...the setting was interesting, some of the supporting cast was enjoyable, and part one actually had a decent story arc going before he decided to toss out all the decent parts with the time skip. Besides, if you tell people your character is wearing an animal like mask and want a decent reference point, there's worse aesthetics you could go with than an ANBU mask. At least they have a nice simple design to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:37:22-07:00","id":994789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994731#post994731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Jachra</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to sound unnecessarily harsh and I don't mean it that way - there's a quote button that lets you inform the other person they're being quoted, even if you don't actually take a quote.<br /> Not meant as a criticism, just would prefer it for being spoken to in a thread. Thanks~<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994731#post994731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Hitomi's backstory is something that's a work in progress. The key points are mostly to establish her as that &quot;invisible middle child &quot; who acts out for attention. I'm more than willing to change some details about the specifics. Mostly I just needed to create a reason why she starts sneaking around and breaking into things without being a thief.</div> </div> </div> </div>While details can give a person life, there's such a thing as conservation of detail too - your parents are world-class individuals. That should be a fundamental part of your character concept both before and after her Visitation. Details like 'world-class' stick out and demand attention, they aren't just ho-hum background notes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994731#post994731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The security consultant thing was actually a suggestion a friend made. I think he had actually been watching a show about a guy who used to be a thief who would break into places to show people how unsecure their home or business was when he made the suggestion. However I may have to check out that movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this isn't inherently a bad thing, I think her motivation is a bit weak. Also she got her ass <i>caught,</i> she can't be all that good. Maybe if the contractor showed up on the park bench next to her one day or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994731#post994731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for her conception, I was thinking more of that one time Zeus did it in Greek myth, but yeah it's definitely a squicky thing even if it is an established thing in myth. I know my playgroup wouldn't find issue with it, but that's definitely a detail I'd change if I was dealing with anyone else. I'm not the type to normally include rape in my characters' back stories. I really was just going for something I saw once in a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character probably ought to be enraged on her behalf. She might become paranoid at the thought of someone doing that to her. How can she ever look at a boyfriend again without wondering if it's a god pretending to be him, come to seed her with his next scion? Certainly she should resent her father - it might even make her appreciate the man she <i>thought</i> was her sire and make sure that he understands that she appreciates how he's been such a good father to her, because Blood Isn't Everything.<br /> <br /> It's a violating thought that should be a bigger note for your character if you include it. You and I both know how bodily autonomy isn't a joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994731#post994731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'll defend my use of a visual nod to Naruto by saying that the writing may be atrocious but despite the plot holes, obvious retcons between parts one and two, and the poorly written main characters...the setting was interesting, some of the supporting cast was enjoyable, and part one actually had a decent story arc going before he decided to toss out all the decent parts with the time skip. Besides, if you tell people your character is wearing an animal like mask and want a decent reference point, there's worse aesthetics you could go with than an ANBU mask. At least they have a nice simple design to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that Naruto is bad, though it is, it's that it borders on weeaboo to include it. Even if you're Japanese American, it's kind of a - warning sign.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest making reference to Japanese animal masks without the anime reference included. There's a rich and diverse history there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-28-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:15:43-07:00","id":994827,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5226_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5226\" data-vbnamecard=\"5226\">Jachra</a> should notify you, same as a quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:27:59-07:00","id":994840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994827#post994827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5226_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5226\" data-vbnamecard=\"5226\">Jachra</a> should notify you, same as a quote.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's odd, it did not in her case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:29:19-07:00","id":994842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994669#post994669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds a bit like asking the Neo-Nazis to retool to hunt down titanspawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or like a name named named Saul who hunted down Christians and turning them over to Romans for execution until he had a visit from the divine that ultimately lead to him stopping the persecution, taking the name Paul and authoring several letters that are all included in the Bible?<br /> <br /> Redemption is something of a thing in Christian theology so having someone (either God) try to turn an institution that did some unquestionably evil things into a force for good isn't necessarily without thematic grounds for the religion. In fact, I doubt it's the only one of the religions where that theme can be found. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994669#post994669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually an interesting concept, though I'm not really sure what face-palming has to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Polar bears hide their noses when they want to hide since it's the only part of their body that's really visible. So instead of her character doing a facepalm when people do something stupid and embarrass her character, she will cover her nose with her hand because that's what polar bears do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:30:41-07:00","id":994845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994840#post994840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's odd, it did not in her case.</div> </div> </div> </div>She didn't do it correctly.<br /> <br /> If you type out @resp you will see an autocomplete for my name (and someone else's) pop up. Then you have to click on the name and it'll automatically make it a link. Just typing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a> straight out won't do it but clicking the autocomplete <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a> will.<br /> <br /> Edit: I was wrong, typing it out did make the link. In that case I don't know what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:40:14-07:00","id":994902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994840#post994840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's odd, it did not in her case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry. I had seen other people on the forums do the thing with the at symbol, not sure why it didn't work with me. I'm typing on a smartphone so I was trying to keep the format of my post simple.<br /> <br /> Yeah, with your advice, I think I'm going to go over her backstory again, primarily her family stuff. I'm thinking her mom is still the world famous astronomer, more because that's how she caught Tsukiyomi's eye in the first place. Will probably work that into a bigger part of her personality. Probably will downgrade the mortal dad a bit to something more low key but still would keep him away from home a lot. <br /> <br /> Probably going to rework how she was conceived as well, because I feel like if I'm going to explore those themes, I'm going to aim them at someone who's known to do that in myth, like Zeus, rather than poor Tsukiyomi who honestly doesn't have a lot of myths about him (at least not that I've found) and probably doesn't deserve that kind of scorn.<br /> <br /> And I guess I should clarify, the ANBU mask thing isn't supposed to be an actual reference with her mask. Literally in-universe, it's just supposed to be a rabbit mask. The ANBU masks from Naruto are just the first thing I think of when picturing the mask. I don't know if those style of masks have a proper name or not. I'm just using the Naruto reference as a visual shorthand that's a common enough reference for most people to be able to clearly picture what I'm describing. <br /> So yeah, it's not that she's running around with a piece of Naruto cosplay on, but rather she's wearing a rabbit mask that the best way I can think to describe it is by comparing it to Naruto. Sorry if I wasn't clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:14:44-07:00","id":994926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994902#post994902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, sorry. I had seen other people on the forums do the thing with the at symbol, not sure why it didn't work with me. I'm typing on a smartphone so I was trying to keep the format of my post simple.<br /> <br /> Yeah, with your advice, I think I'm going to go over her backstory again, primarily her family stuff. I'm thinking her mom is still the world famous astronomer, more because that's how she caught Tsukiyomi's eye in the first place. Will probably work that into a bigger part of her personality. Probably will downgrade the mortal dad a bit to something more low key but still would keep him away from home a lot.<br /> <br /> Probably going to rework how she was conceived as well, because I feel like if I'm going to explore those themes, I'm going to aim them at someone who's known to do that in myth, like Zeus, rather than poor Tsukiyomi who honestly doesn't have a lot of myths about him (at least not that I've found) and probably doesn't deserve that kind of scorn.<br /> <br /> And I guess I should clarify, the ANBU mask thing isn't supposed to be an actual reference with her mask. Literally in-universe, it's just supposed to be a rabbit mask. The ANBU masks from Naruto are just the first thing I think of when picturing the mask. I don't know if those style of masks have a proper name or not. I'm just using the Naruto reference as a visual shorthand that's a common enough reference for most people to be able to clearly picture what I'm describing.<br /> So yeah, it's not that she's running around with a piece of Naruto cosplay on, but rather she's wearing a rabbit mask that the best way I can think to describe it is by comparing it to Naruto. Sorry if I wasn't clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough all around~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:17:07-07:00","id":995115,"title":"","content":"Well, I've been thinking of trying to make a mythological Mother figure in Scion. She's a chosen of Hathor (or Isis) and her son is the next very distant relation in line as &quot;Pharaoh&quot;, but he's 7. She is a very powerful scion who in some ways outstrips her son. Of course she brings her all to make sure her children can defend and know the world they were born into. Even her mortal daughters are becoming child sorcerers. She was raised knowing much of this in theory, but now she has no choice but to raise her children &quot;properly&quot;, something she is deeply conflicted over, because while she wants them to be prepared, she also wants to shield them from some of the terrors of their position. It's a losing battle, but what can she do but try?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:12:59-07:00","id":995267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=995115#post995115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I've been thinking of trying to make a mythological Mother figure in Scion. She's a chosen of Hathor (or Isis) and her son is the next very distant relation in line as &quot;Pharaoh&quot;, but he's 7. She is a very powerful scion who in some ways outstrips her son. Of course she brings her all to make sure her children can defend and know the world they were born into. Even her mortal daughters are becoming child sorcerers. She was raised knowing much of this in theory, but now she has no choice but to raise her children &quot;properly&quot;, something she is deeply conflicted over, because while she wants them to be prepared, she also wants to shield them from some of the terrors of their position. It's a losing battle, but what can she do but try?</div> </div> </div> </div>She outstrips her son who is seven?<br /> <br /> How does she reconcile her daughters being sorcerers, knowing that their magic is fueled by robbing the divine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:22:03-07:00","id":995271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=995115#post995115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I've been thinking of trying to make a mythological Mother figure in Scion. She's a chosen of Hathor (or Isis) and her son is the next very distant relation in line as &quot;Pharaoh&quot;, but he's 7. She is a very powerful scion who in some ways outstrips her son. Of course she brings her all to make sure her children can defend and know the world they were born into. Even her mortal daughters are becoming child sorcerers. She was raised knowing much of this in theory, but now she has no choice but to raise her children &quot;properly&quot;, something she is deeply conflicted over, because while she wants them to be prepared, she also wants to shield them from some of the terrors of their position. It's a losing battle, but what can she do but try?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love mother figures, they're an underused character in my mind, especially as a <i>main</i> character, at least in fantasy fiction, but this is a bit incoherent.<br /> <br /> Maybe you should start from the beginning by telling us who she is and she what she's like?<br /> <br /> Add in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11726_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11726\" data-vbnamecard=\"11726\">Solana</a>'s criticisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:15:28-07:00","id":995344,"title":"","content":"I like coming up with antagonistic mortal cults for the Gods as they make good foils for low legend Scions. Titanspawn are fun and all but nothing beats a human enemy who just think they're doing their gods' work.<br /> <br /> .An elite mercenary band that enforces the will of Maat to the extreme. They take jobs that target those who they feel have escaped the natural Justice of the world. <br /> <br /> . Cultists of Babulu Aye that masquerade as Red Cross workers to get into disease filled regions and further spread the blessings of their master.<br /> <br /> . A private prison company that is actually a front for a Mayasura (Hindu Titan of Illusion and patron of architecture) cult. As the whole cosmos is already a prison, they reason that they might as well make it a more concrete reality, all while making a nice profit off of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:26:39-07:00","id":995503,"title":"","content":"Back in 1E only the Greeks could have &quot;super skill master&quot; and I was upset that some random child of Hephaestus could be better with a bow then a child of archer god Raiden. Then I pictured the archer scion of Hephaestus-<br /> Huge compound bow with gears + pulleys + motor assisted ratchets, night vision googles with HUD &amp; GPS, camo ghillie suit with thermal dampening and scent masking. The MODERN god of HUNTING and MAN AS A TOOL USER","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The sea looks at the stability of the mountain and sighs. The mountain watches the freedom of the sea and cries.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11634-sea-envy","name":"Sea-Envy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11634_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:14:48-07:00","id":995772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sea-Envy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=995503#post995503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in 1E only the Greeks could have &quot;super skill master&quot; and I was upset that some random child of Hephaestus could be better with a bow then a child of archer god Raiden. Then I pictured the archer scion of Hephaestus-<br /> Huge compound bow with gears + pulleys + motor assisted ratchets, night vision googles with HUD &amp; GPS, camo ghillie suit with thermal dampening and scent masking. The MODERN god of HUNTING and MAN AS A TOOL USER</div> </div> </div> </div>Blanketly making them better than an archer child of archer Raiden is still pretty upsetting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:22:40-07:00","id":995777,"title":"","content":"I'm a little grouchy that I'm only really familiar with two of the twelve and a half Pantheons on the table in Scion, but at the same time mythology is so overwhelmingly large that I'll probably just wait for release to delve into some of the other material out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:23:28-07:00","id":995778,"title":"","content":"I've got a background for a character concept, hopefully one of many that I'll be able to use in a game or as fodder for fiction material. I've got a few ideas, I'm just short information on pantheons to start it with.<br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> Mark Rodach: Son of Brigid<br /> <br /> Background: Mark grew up in a home filled with opposites. His father worked as a mechanical engineer by day and as an artist by night. Brought up to use his head and his heart in his decisions, he always took the hardest classes, went for the biggest roles, and spoke up for the greatest causes. He always knew the value of honor, and standing by the things he believed in, and wished to inspire others much like his father. Growing up in a world with YouTube, he began by showcasing his talents there, from Artistry, Performance, and Music, to Magic, Mechanics, and building great big things. Throughout high school, he gained popularity and tasked himself with continuing to create and have fun with doing YouTube. Mark reveled in the ability to captivate the masses through the myriads of content on his YouTube channel.<br /> <br /> As he has been going to college, he always finds new ways to prove his ability, and create new content for his peers. Mark uses his skills, his art, and his voice as a YouTuber to forward good causes. He speaks up and speaks out for people who are downtrodden, by staging protests, running flash mobs, painting murals, and giving campus security a hell of a time, all while honoring his commitment to his channel. Mark performs weekly at a favorite bar of his with some friends in a band and does little bits of performance whenever, whether it be street magic or just busking with a guitar, to keep his skills flush. Mark always knew he was meant to inspire, and yet he feels there\u2019s always something missing to his performance, like some small ember that\u2019s struggling to alight.<br /> <br /> That changed in that fateful show. Mark was up on stage, getting ready with his bandmates, beers in hand, and a set list between them. They had heard a record label might be coming to visit through some of Mark\u2019s YouTube friends. They were really nervous, and had been deliberating over the set list for the last week. Mark peeked up from the huddle, and locked eyes with a redhead that to him looked like she had fire in her eyes. He knew, in that moment, that this show was going to be one of their best. He knew that the ember inside him had just caught flame. <br /> After the show, Mark found the redhead at the bar and went to thank her. The woman grabbed a couple of beers and took him aside, revealing herself as his mother, Brigid. \u201cNo need to thank me,\u201d she said, \u201cI just lit the match. Now use your fire to light up the world.\u201d<br /> <br /> Description: Mark has a tall and slim build; wiry, lightly toned muscle, with short strawberry blonde hair styled with an undercut that highlights his front man face, and the shocking blue eyes. He has tattoos around his arms and back, mostly of his own design, meant to evoke interest and other varied emotions. When he\u2019s not filming for YouTube, performing with his band, or causing general art based mischief, he can be found driving around town with his friends in a rebuilt 1970 Chevy Chevelle. His wardrobe consists of general hipster/artist fare, with special duds for shows and dates.<br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> Basically, I see him as being someone who uses his skills to inspire and forge new paths.<br /> I'll be writing up his actual visitation fiction later, as I know how that goes, there's just a bit of background that i'm not terribly sure about.<br /> <br /> I've also got a Scion of Hestia sitting in my list of things to write-up, both background and visitation fiction.<br /> Enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:11:49-07:00","id":995850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=995777#post995777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little grouchy that I'm only really familiar with two of the twelve and a half Pantheons on the table in Scion, but at the same time mythology is so overwhelmingly large that I'll probably just wait for release to delve into some of the other material out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. *ten characters*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:53:59-07:00","id":995956,"title":"","content":"The character that I'm most interested in converting from 1e started as a Ghost Rider rip-off but grew into his own character. Jacob Bjornsson is a Scion of Mictlantecuhtli whose mother was a Norwegian ambassador to Mexico. As far as 2e origins go, the closest one would be Chosen. Mictlantecuhtli gave his mother a card before he was born, and told her to spread her blood on it should her child's life not come. There were some complications with the pregnancy, and she spread blood on the card. What she didn't know was that before she did, he was dead in the womb. What Mictlantecuhtli did was bring the soul back and used some of his power to patch it back into the fetus.<br /> <br /> Jacob grew up mostly in Mexico City, and in his early twenties bought a motorcycle and started roaming North America. A few years later after a bar brawl back in Mexico City Jacob received his Visitation and was sent by Mictlantecuhtli on missions against the restless dead. His first one was a stretch of highway in the Sierra Nevada mountains that the cannibalistic ghosts of a wagon train haunted. The ghosts refused to move on until the descendant of the wagon train leader, and the one that started the cannibalism, was brought to them. So, that's what Jacob did.<br /> <br /> The eventual goal for the character was that he'd find ways to pay respect to both his pantheon and that of his mother's people: the Aesir. Things like sacrifices to him come godhood being the Blood Eagle. The souls of those sacrificed to him becoming his posse, kind of like an Aztec version of the valkyries/einherjar. Of course, his appearance upon reaching divinity would be a skeleton wreathed in flames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T19:10:33-07:00","id":997500,"title":"","content":"A pair of Tricksters (one from Br'er Rabbit, and one from Inari) who become fate bound rivals to each other shortly after their visitations. As their Legend continues to grow, they become serialized in popular children's novels featuring a rabbit and fox constantly trying to outsmart each other. By the time they finally reach godhood, they've become a household name, who's stories will be passed on for generations to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T04:25:17-07:00","id":997628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=994842#post994842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Polar bears hide their noses when they want to hide since it's the only part of their body that's really visible. So instead of her character doing a facepalm when people do something stupid and embarrass her character, she will cover her nose with her hand because that's what polar bears do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's adorable as hell, even if it is practical sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:53:01-07:00","id":997647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=997500#post997500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pair of Tricksters (one from Br'er Rabbit, and one from Inari) who become fate bound rivals to each other shortly after their visitations. As their Legend continues to grow, they become serialized in popular children's novels featuring a rabbit and fox constantly trying to outsmart each other. By the time they finally reach godhood, they've become a household name, who's stories will be passed on for generations to come.</div> </div> </div> </div>this reminds me of Splash Mountain minus the bear. and much more family friendly. I like this.<br /> i need to really get the concepts of my scions down, like, i have an idea for what purviews they would be using, and possibly where they might fit (one of them is probably an arthur incarnate from the plant don), but i ahvent really hammered out some of them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:51:14-07:00","id":997802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=997647#post997647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this reminds me of Splash Mountain minus the bear. and much more family friendly. I like this.<br /> i need to really get the concepts of my scions down, like, i have an idea for what purviews they would be using, and possibly where they might fit (one of them is probably an arthur incarnate from the plant don), but i ahvent really hammered out some of them yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splash Mountain is based on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_of_the_South#Controversies\" target=\"_blank\">something else entirely.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T16:45:49-07:00","id":997956,"title":"","content":"An Egyptian Scion with the potential destiny to surpass even the most powerful among their pantheon. As their power grows, they are being manipulated by Nu in order to dismantle his wayward grandchildren from the inside out.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Hera who was conceived for the express purpose of assassinating Zeus' bastards. This assignment makes working in a band with other Greek Scions very awkward for both parties.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Xipe Totec who works as a world renowned chef. He has adapted his sacrificial rituals to involve eating his victims, with his fellow Scions being popular delicacies.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Odin who received his visitation late into his life. He is a grizzled and ornery old man who refuses to take shit from any 'youngsters' who get in his way.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Apollo who received their visitation posthumously... after they became a hideous Nosferatu. Now infused by the Titan of Darkness, the undead Scion begins to amass enough power to take vengeance upon the Theoi, whom they blame for their untimely death at the hands of monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-03-2016, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:15:41-07:00","id":998094,"title":"","content":"I really want an occult scholar of some sort to have her Visitation and meet her parent/patron... Baphomet, a deity that seems to have almost exclusively existed as a mistranslation and made-up crime of the Templars. They're trying to explain the whole Scion thing to her, and she's just like &quot;Of all the gods, you are one of the least-real! Are you kidding me?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:12:51-07:00","id":998105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998094#post998094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want an occult scholar of some sort to have her Visitation and meet her parent/patron... Baphomet, a deity that seems to have almost exclusively existed as a mistranslation and made-up crime of the Templars. They're trying to explain the whole Scion thing to her, and she's just like &quot;Of all the gods, you are one of the least-real! Are you kidding me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget it's description of being a hermaphrodite, winged goat person, who's worshipers practice witchcraft and have massive orgies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> A Scion of Loki who takes after the rest of his father's pantheon by being a muscle headed brute. Much to the chagrin of his highly intelligent father who considers him to be an embarrassment to the rest of his more human offspring. No matter how many tests of cunning he places before him, his son always seems to lose his temper and start smashing his way towards his goal. Leaving Loki with a lot of wasted time and effort.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Amaterasu who believes Scions and Titanspawn may have gotten off on the wrong foot, and it's time to make amends for past mistakes. After all, Scions and Titanspawn are practically cousins, when you think about it. Instead of exterminating the Titanspawn on sight, they attempt to unify the two factions, bringing about a peaceful resolution to this millennia old war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-04-2016, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:40:57-07:00","id":998114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=997956#post997956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Egyptian Scion with the potential destiny to surpass even the most powerful among their pantheon. As their power grows, they are being manipulated by Nu in order to dismantle his wayward grandchildren from the inside out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were a GM I'd be instantly wary of any concept that began with &quot;to surpass even the most powerful among their pantheon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, it's interesting to note that, although the most likely explanation is that Baphomet is just a corruption of Mohammad, there's 19th century occultists who believe that it's a secret gnostic god/dess from waaay back. They're certainly, breathtakingly wrong, but it's a cool idea to play with.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, implying witchcraft and orgies are bad, tsk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:17:13-07:00","id":998124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998114#post998114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were a GM I'd be instantly wary of any concept that began with &quot;to surpass even the most powerful among their pantheon.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I said <i>potential destiny</i>, meaning it's not certain. I also just realized that I accidentally confused Nu and Shu when writing up their concept. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998114#post998114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, implying witchcraft and orgies are bad, tsk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now when did I say that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:18:34-07:00","id":998126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998114#post998114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were a GM I'd be instantly wary of any concept that began with &quot;to surpass even the most powerful among their pantheon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, it's interesting to note that, although the most likely explanation is that Baphomet is just a corruption of Mohammad, there's 19th century occultists who believe that it's a secret gnostic god/dess from waaay back. They're certainly, breathtakingly wrong, but it's a cool idea to play with.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, implying witchcraft and orgies are bad, tsk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that gives me a goat person who transgresses with gender is fine in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:24:47-07:00","id":998127,"title":"","content":"I've also seen the image of Baphomet associated with Shub-Niggurath. Also known as <i>The Black Goat of the Woods with A Thousand Young.</i><br /> <br /> Described as being a fertility goddess from Lovecraft's pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T02:08:04-07:00","id":998147,"title":"","content":"<b>Yasmine </b><b>Mahfouz</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent</b>: Yinepu<br /> <b>Callings</b>: Healer (Favored), Liminal, Lover<br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path</b>: Weirdo from Suburbia (Grew up as a minority in white upper middle class suburbs, subject to distrust, especially because of odd behavior; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Academics, Persuasion)<br /> <b>Role Path</b>: &quot;Healing,&quot; Papa would tell me, &quot;is not a science, but the intuitive art of wooing nature.&quot; (Moves to poorer ethnic communities, offers treatment and performs surgeries for people who can't afford 'the real thing'; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Empathy, Medicine)<br /> <b>Relationship Path</b>: &quot;I pray I never need weigh your heart.&quot; (Creepy daughter of Yinepu; <b>Asset Skills</b>: Occult, Science)<br /> <br /> Yasmine is the only daughter to Nura Mahfouz, a former hospice nurse and now single parent. If asked by her daughter (and she does ask, often) she can't quite remember the events that lead to the conception of her daughter, she instead rambles on, something about a funeral, too much wine, a charming man with intense eyes. A month later, she learned she was pregnant. A week after that, her patient died, only for her to discover that he had left her his not inconsiderable amount of money. Nura moved into the same house where she once she served, and put that money to use raising her daughter - or at least giving her the best chance she could.<br /> <br /> In her earliest years Yasmine seemed to lack self-control. She would collect dead things, cut them open, and carefully start gathering their organs into jars. Other kids were disgusted and awed, parents were horrified and concerned that the child was a psychopath, a budding serial killer waiting to happen. They'd all seen the movies, they knew animal cruelty was the earliest sign. Whenever Yasmine tried to explain that the animal was already dead, her cries fell on deaf ears. When she told them she 'needed' to do it, for their sake, her mother got her a therapist.<br /> <br /> The odd behaviors continued into high school, albeit without some of the ritual. She'd find herself in a biology class preparing to dissect an animal. The teacher would drone out the preparation instructions, Yasmine would drift off, someone would shake her back awake and she'd come to. Her animal would be perfectly opened, each organ and body part carefully tagged before the teacher had even instructed them to begin. Yasmine developed a close circle of friends, and it blossomed into a community that reached out beyond the fences and gates of her community. She found solace in minority communities, and places where low income drove people into the arms of the gods and spirits. Her mother's hopes for college and a professional career withered on the vine when Yasmine refused to apply, instead moving into a cheap apartment in poorer neighborhoods, or staying with friends. She learned all the natural remedies and their occult significance, and found that when she applied them they actually <i>worked</i>. She was reluctant at first, but a sick friend couldn't afford treatment, and so she performed the necessary surgery for offerings of food, water, precious items to keep on an altar to some figure in her dreams she could barely make out. The surgery was flawless, it was like her hands already knew everything they needed to, like they had a will of their own.<br /> <br /> Lately, the people coming to her for surgery come bearing injuries that are increasingly strange, and sometimes disturbing. She puts them all back together, collecting whatever samples she can and keeping them in tiny porcelain jars. <br /> <br /> And now a strange young man with an intense gaze has come asking to hire her on retainer, sending her about the country on a whim to treat people who should be able to afford the best medical care money can buy. He says he's her father, that she is the daughter of a god, and that her gifts are pivotal toward preserving Ma'at.<br /> <br /> Yasmine isn't sure how she feels about any of that, but the trappings fit what she knows, and putting people back together is all she knows how to do, anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T17:45:20-07:00","id":998520,"title":"","content":"<b>A Scion of Hel</b>, who's good intentions are masked beneath a veneer of unforgiving brutality. He truly has the Aesir's best interests at heart, but his immoral behavior makes his fellow Asgardians too reluctant to call upon his aid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Hephaestus</b> who's arms were torn off by a cyclops, leaving her crippled for life. To compensate, her father outfitted her with mechanical replacements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Set</b> who finds joy in unleashing natural disasters upon the world. Their specialty is weather manipulation, causing no end of complaints towards those responsible for the daily forecast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-10-2017, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:52:02-07:00","id":998593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998520#post998520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A Scion of Hel</b>, who's good intentions are masked beneath a vainer of unforgiving brutality. He truly has the Aesir's best interests at heart, but his immoral behavior makes his fellow Asgardians too reluctant to call upon his aid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Hephaestus</b> who's arms were torn off by a cyclops, leaving her crippled for life. To compensate, her father outfitted her with mechanical replacements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Set</b> who finds joy in unleashing natural disasters upon the world. Their specialty is weather manipulation, causing no end of complaints towards those responsible for the daily forecast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope they accurately capture the nuance of the different pantheons (that is to say, 'races' of god) within Norse Mythology, instead of just having everyone be on team Aesir.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a problem I had with 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:22:41-07:00","id":998606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998593#post998593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope they accurately capture the nuance of the different pantheons (that is to say, 'races' of god) within Norse Mythology, instead of just having everyone be on team Aesir.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a problem I had with 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are going in the hero core version (other shards may vary), that the Aesir and Vanir have effectively merged through intermarriage and exchange alliances at this point.<br /> <br /> I'm writing up a different take on the Norse Pantheon for a Shard for the Drivethru fan-material store. Among some of the differences will be a distinct set of Vanir (who are further from humanity than the Aesir and include Titans in their number: including Jord, Ran, and Aegir), the death of Baldr and binding of Loki having occurred in the Middle Ages with the fall of the Viking age, and Asgard having been frozen over in Fimbulwinter ever since. Much more Incarnate heavy take on the Pantheon, with Baldr, Hodor, and Nanna having already replayed their deaths as Hero Scions at least once (as described by Saxo Grammaticus)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:51:29-07:00","id":998626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998593#post998593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope they accurately capture the nuance of the different pantheons (that is to say, 'races' of god) within Norse Mythology, instead of just having everyone be on team Aesir.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a problem I had with 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was my understanding there were only a few or so Vanir survivors, and they were forcefully absorbed into the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Everything I thought I knew about Norse mythology was turned inside out when I looked at sources other than Marvel comics.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Manannan Mac Lir</b>, who received his visitation after completing his training for the IRA, using his supernatural powers to fight for Ireland's independence. Unfortunately, he spends less time fighting the Britains, and more time trying to contain the resurgence of Formorians in his homeland!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-05-2016, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T23:29:28-07:00","id":998631,"title":"","content":"Admittedly the problem with including the Vanir as a full Pantheon in their own right is that other than the crossovers to the Aesir none of them are explicitly NAMED in surviving myths. The deities I use as residents of Vanaheim at my own table are...<br /> <br /> Delling (god of the dawn and king of the Vanir)<br /> Nott (goddess of night and queen of the Vanir)<br /> Dagr (god of day and son of the ruling pair)<br /> Nerthus (goddess of fresh water, sister and former wife of Njord, mother of Freyr and Freyja)<br /> Meili (Vanir god of lightning, son of Odin and Jord who remained with his mother)<br /> Jord (earth titan)<br /> Aegir (sea titan)<br /> Ran (sea titan)<br /> Odr (god of mad ecstasy, husband of Freyja from before she joined the Aesir)<br /> Eostre (fertility goddess of spring and rebirth)<br /> <br /> Vili/Hoenir (Aesir exchange captive to the Vanir)<br /> <br /> Nine Daughters of Aegir and Ran (who are also the mothers of Heimdallr... some scholars would disagree with that conflation, but its common enough in art that I'm cool with rolling with it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:06:35-07:00","id":998658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998626#post998626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was my understanding there were only a few or so Vanir survivors, and they were forcefully absorbed into the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Everything I thought I knew about Norse mythology was turned inside out when I looked at sources other than Marvel comics.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Manannan Mac Lir</b>, who received his visitation after completing his training for the IRA, using his supernatural powers to fight for Ireland's independence. Unfortunately, he spends less time fighting the Britains, and more time trying to contain the resurgence of Formorians in his homeland!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Freya, Frey, and Njord were taken by the Aesir as part of brokering a peace, the Vanir got Mimir and someone else, I forget who. The Jotuns are still quite numerous, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:08:36-07:00","id":998659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998631#post998631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly the problem with including the Vanir as a full Pantheon in their own right is that other than the crossovers to the Aesir none of them are explicitly NAMED in surviving myths. The deities I use as residents of Vanaheim at my own table are...<br /> <br /> Delling (god of the dawn and king of the Vanir)<br /> Nott (goddess of night and queen of the Vanir)<br /> Dagr (god of day and son of the ruling pair)<br /> Nerthus (goddess of fresh water, sister and former wife of Njord, mother of Freyr and Freyja)<br /> Meili (Vanir god of lightning, son of Odin and Jord who remained with his mother)<br /> Jord (earth titan)<br /> Aegir (sea titan)<br /> Ran (sea titan)<br /> Odr (god of mad ecstasy, husband of Freyja from before she joined the Aesir)<br /> Eostre (fertility goddess of spring and rebirth)<br /> <br /> Vili/Hoenir (Aesir exchange captive to the Vanir)<br /> <br /> Nine Daughters of Aegir and Ran (who are also the mothers of Heimdallr... some scholars would disagree with that conflation, but its common enough in art that I'm cool with rolling with it)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily need them to be fully staffed (although that's a fun idea for an enterprising community creation person who wants to get imaginative), I just want the game to acknowledge that those sorts of distinctions and exist, and influence relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:16:28-08:00","id":999393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=997802#post997802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splash Mountain is based on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_of_the_South#Controversies\" target=\"_blank\">something else entirely.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>non non. I know. Hi, i'm a disney nerd. <br /> im just saying, the dynamic of the fox and hare doing that sort of thing, its reminiscent of most tiny characters running from bigger ones, like tom and jerry or something like that. i just used splash mountain as a reference due to its use of both a hare and a fox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:25:17-08:00","id":1000150,"title":"","content":"<b>Buta no-o:</b> A former scion of Susano-o, risen to godhood, despite the best wishes of the Amatsukami. While Buta no-o (King of Swine) has technically achieved godhood by Scion standards, the Amatsukami consider him to be a demon, in light of his behavior. Buta no-o has established himself as a spirit of sexual deviancy, encouraging his followers to indulge in their base lusts to the point of addiction. Amaterasu has barred him from establishing a permanent residence within the Overworld, and so he frequently returns to the World to party it up with mortals who have been twisted into his service.<br /> <br /> <br /> In his true form, Buta no-o takes the form of a morbidly obese man with the head, tail and legs of a great pig. When he's not preparing for battle, he prefers to wear lavishly comfortable robes made from either fine silks, or soft animal pelts. Alternatively, he may choose to wear nothing at all, which is often the case when he's not hosting important company. In battle, he wears a suit of traditional Japanese armor and wields his divine naginata (Inoshishi no Kiba) as his preferred weapon of choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> While spending time in the mortal World, he has taken forms that enable him to live in a life style as lavishly comfortable as his manner of dress would suggest. He has been a wealthy businessman, a criminal kingpin, an opium dealer, a brothel manager, an honored war veteran (with remarkably little battle damage), and the owner of some of the best night clubs in the country.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of Buta no-o are surprisingly rarer than you might expect from such a lecherous kami. It's not that he doesn't have children, it's that he has too many to keep track of, and so he stopped trying. Those who do earn his attention, however, live up to what you might expect from a child of a demonic pig. They come from poor backgrounds, with questionable parentage and often pursue immoral choices in life; such as prostitution, thievery, disorderly conduct, and violent outbursts. In truth, being granted a visitation is probably the best thing that's ever happened to his little piglets, as it gives them the chance to actually do something positive with their lives. Unfortunately, such an opportunity is quickly wasted under the hedonistic guidance of Buta no-o, he hopes to mold his Scions into future demons like himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Inoshishi no Kiba (Boar's Tusk) is an upgraded version of a previous relic that Buta no-o received earlier in his career. Since its upgrade, it now allows him to channel the Animal (swine) purview in addition to its original access of the Chaos purview. It also adds +2L and -1 Speed to the Naginata template.<br /> <br /> His armor, which he only wears when he's expecting a fight, is a suit of divinely empowered Yoroi armor which adds +2L /+2B soak to the normal template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-04-2017, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T15:02:59-08:00","id":1004129,"title":"","content":"My first concept in 1e was Nicholas Tophos, Scion of Nyx. (Yes, his name was a joke on nyktophobia.) The basic concept was that as a baby, he had been stolen from Nyx by a Theoi Band, and raised by the mother of the Scion of Apollo member of said Band. Nick called her grandma. The various members of the Band were simply doting aunts and uncles that wandered into and out of his life and taught him all sorts of neat things. Other than the abundance of aunts and uncles, Nick had a fairly normal life. Given that he was a stargazer, he majored in astrophysics in college. Then his Visitation happened provided by the Band consisting of his 'aunts and uncles'. Apollo had apparently issued a prophecy before Nick's birth that a Scion of Nyx would join the Theoi and take Nyx's mythological place in the pantheon. So the Band was sent to retrieve him and raise him. Needless to say, Nyx wanted him back. How he stayed concealed for so long was going to be a GM mystery.<br /> <br /> The GM passed on the concept because the game would have to be houseruled to make it work. What with him being technically a Titanspawn and not really adopted by any given Deity, it was a mess. Since it was her first Scion game she asked me to come up with something else more rules friendly. I really want to play this character in 2e.<br /> <br /> I settled on a Scion of Odin that was a crime scene photographer who was a bit obsessed with deaths and murder. Imagine my surprised when the movie Nightcrawler came out. Still, revisiting the character would be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":753,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","user":"Ariketh","date":". 11-16-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:32:55-08:00","id":1004223,"title":"","content":"<b>A scion of Sobek</b> who works as an assistant biologist and researcher. Despite her heritage, she failed to manifest Divine Intelligence, and thus her experiments seem woefully primitive to her more gifted peers. Regardless, she is driven to prove herself capable and earn the respect of her fellow scientists!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A scion of Amaterasu</b> who is, perhaps, a bit too enamored with the concept of dragons, and has devoted his efforts towards becoming one, himself. As chief of the pantheon, Amaterasu has promised to grant his wish after he proves himself worthy of such a blessing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A scion of Parvati</b> and a champion among men. With a rugged personality and hardy physique, mortal men recognize him as a symbol of masculinity and strive to emulate him as best they can. As his Legend grows, he comes to develop a cult following on the internet, for his daring feats of manliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:39:49-08:00","id":1005549,"title":"","content":"<b>A Scion of Hera</b> who is fascinated with stories of the preposterous actions performed by others throughout mythology. As his legend grows, he focuses himself around becoming the <i>God of Ridiculousness</i>, taking pride in his wildly unpredictable and over the top behavior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Bastet</b> who was revealed to have cat allergies shortly after receiving their visitation. To say they have an unstable relationship with the cat goddess would be an understatement. The fact that they eventually become the <i>God of Dogs</i> probably didn't help, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Erzulie</b> who was adopted when Kalfu disowned them during infancy. Embittered by their father's neglect, they begin to lash out both before and after their visitation. Eventually becoming known as the <i>God of Anger</i> for the Loa pantheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Odin</b> who, like his divine father before him, survived an excruciating ordeal in order to obtain great power. Over time, the Titanspawn come to realize that he is not easy to kill, and he eventually becomes known as the <i>God of Resilience</i> in recognition of his vast reserves of stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:41:44-08:00","id":1006005,"title":"","content":"I thought I'd share my two Scions that reached godhood in 1e (albeit heavily house-ruled) campaigns. I look forward to seeing the full 2e rules and figuring out how to recreate them.<br /> Note: these characters are described using 1e-based terminology. <hr /><br /> <i><b>Tsukiyono Keisuke, Scion of Tsuki-yomi:</b></i><br /> <br /> A Tokyo native and a child of career diplomats, Keisuke followed his late father's example and joined the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. What his mother didn't know was that, in addition to his job as a cultural attache, he had also been recruited by the Japanese Public Security Intelligence Agency as a covert operative. On one mission, he was captured and imprisoned by a Yakuza boss, but Tsuki-yomi chose that moment to Visit him and give him the means to free himself and save others (in the form of a moonstone ring and and a magically-silenced .45).<br /> <br /> Following his Visitation, Keisuke would continue to work for both the Japanese government and his divine father, but did so mainly solo, until encountering and joining his Band in Las Vegas. As the campaign progressed, Keisuke was eventually recruited by Interpol, and would frequently use those connections and resources to find titanspawn activity or pinpoint nascent trouble spots.<ul><li>Personality/Inspirations: In his persona as a diplomat, Keisuke is friendly, professional, and has just the right touch of wry humor to set someone at ease. Most of this persona is, in fact, a genuine part of his personality, but the \u201creal\u201d Keisuke is a little more frayed, his wry humor a little sharper. Being both a cop and spy (two professions that frequently conflict with each other) can be wearing, and while he leans in the moral direction whenever he can, the demands of pantheon and country frequently push him into ethically grey areas. His relationship with his divine father is a little awkward; as far as Keisuke is concerned, he <i>had</i> a real father, and Tsukiyono Hiroshi died just before he graduated high school. He respects and even likes Tsuki-yomi, but is unable to think of him as anything other than (weird as it sounds) a kind of <i>step</i>father. (Inspirations: Michael Westen (<i>Burn Notice</i>), \u201cTequila\u201d Yuan (<i>Hard Boiled</i>). Faceclaim: <a href=\"https://40.media.tumblr.com/3b768a9bf8b21f53af6b23c68254bc64/tumblr_nvhmar1c7v1rydsfoo1_500.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Aiba Hiroki</a>.)</li> <li>Powers: Keisuke's most commonly used purviews are Darkness and Psychopomp, as he finds them most useful to his his job as a spy. He also makes frequent use of Tsukumo-Gami, as well as Sky's flashier Boons (to wit, Wind's Freedom and Levin Fury). For Epic Attributes, he most commonly uses Epic Charisma, Epic Dexterity, and Epic Perception.</li> <li>Divine Name/Portfolio: <u><b><i>Tsukiyojin</i></b></u>, the Kami of moonlit nights. In some ways, this reflects the degree of duality in Keisuke's nature: a cop for Interpol, but a spy \u2013 a thief, an assassin, a liar \u2013 for the Japanese government; a Scion of a traditionalist pantheon, but very Westernized because of both his cover and \u201creal\u201d jobs, more comfortable in a Savile Row three-piece than in kimono and hakama. A moonlit night looks down upon deeds both fell and admirable, and if Keisuke as a private citizen tries to err in the direction of The Right Thing, his portfolio demands that he not neglect the other side of the scale. Balance, after all.</li> <li>Birthrights: <b>The Ring of the True Throne</b> is a ring made entirely of blue moonstone. It channels the Darkness, Moon, Psychopomp, and Sky purviews, and allows Keisuke to discern who the true leader or source of power in a group or organization is. <b>Hissori-Kiba (\u201cSilent Fang\u201d)</b> is an HK USP Compact .45; the weapon has been enchanted with a magical \u201csilencer\u201d effect, and to leave no physical evidence behind (either brass or slugs), making it an ideal assassin's weapon. Upon his advancement to demigodhood, Keisuke was granted an <b>enchanted magazine</b> that upgrades Hissori-Kiba's damage rating to aggravated and provides the weapon with unlimited ammunition. Upon apotheosis, he was granted a <b>set of traditional Japanese clothes </b>(haori, hakama, and kimono); these have soak equivalent to nemean hide, and can assume the form of any clothes Keisuke desires.</li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><i>Anita Tehrani, Scion of Anahita: </i></b><br /> <br /> Born and raised in New York, Anita chose to pursue a career in active medicine rather than the more sedate academic jobs her parents had. This mild adrenaline-junkie tendency, combined with a sense of guilt about growing up in affluent safety when many of her relatives didn't, drove her to join M\u00e9decins Sans Fronti\u00e8res. She worked extensively with them for several years, as part of field mission teams operating in the Middle East. It was during one such tour of duty in Syria that her compound was beset by extremists. Anita defied them, and, though she'd never used a scalpel outside of surgery, tried to fight them off. It was at this time that Anahita intervened on her daughter's behalf, saving her and the rest of the staff and patients present, and presenting her with Birthrights in the form of a dagger and a bracelet.<br /> <br /> Reeling from both the revelation of her heritage and the psychological effects of the attack, Anita took a leave of absence from MSF and returned to the United States to get her balance back. However, en route she was diverted to Baltimore, where she fell in with a Band trying to keep titanspawn-backed gangsters from dominating the docks. That kind of thing \u2013 the never quite getting to time to recover equilibrium before the next insane crisis \u2013 sort of set the tone for her career as a Scion.<ul><li>Personality/Inspirations: Before her Visitation, Anita was fairly vivacious and idealistic, genuinely feeling that she was making a difference in the World. Now, what idealism remains is cloaked in world-weariness and snark, usually accompanied with coffee and a smoldering cigarette. \u201cSome people, some things, are cancers on the World,\u201d her Band-mates frequently hear her say, \u201cand the best thing for everyone around them is to cut the tumor out.\u201d Still waters run deep, though, and her deep wellspring of compassion shows through in her dedication to healing her patients and saving as many people as she can. Sometimes the woman she used to be peeks out. Her relationship with Anahita is generally friendly, although her divine mother sometimes worries over the cynical turn Anita's personality has taken since her Visitation. (Inspirations: Akagi Ritsuko (<i>Neon Genesis Evangelion</i>), Doc Cottle (<i>Battlestar Galactica</i>). Faceclaim: <a href=\"http://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2014/10/09/1412854981516_wps_54_Nazanin_Boniadi_as_Fara_i.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Nazanin Boniadi</a>.)</li> <li>Powers: Unsurprisingly, Anita's most commonly used purview is Health. Seeing almost as much use, however, is Water, which she tends to wield in a fashion more reminiscent of <i>Avatar: The Last Airbender</i> than classical divine floods. Her infrequently-used War Boons tend to focus on overawing or intimidating an opponent. Epic Intelligence is by far her most commonly used Epic Attribute, but Epic Stamina is a close second.</li> <li>Divine Name/Portfolio: <b><u><i>Ihsanita</i></u></b> (literally, the \u201cKindly Myrtle\u201d), Yazata goddess of modern medicine<i>. </i>Unlike Keisuke, Anita's divine name and portfolio are pretty straightforward.</li> <li>Birthrights: <b>Argument's End</b> is a silver-chased kard-style dagger (uses the hadseax template), enchanted to add Anita's Legend rating to its damage. She also wears a <b>gold-and-lapis-lazuli bracelet</b> that channels the Health and Water purviews. Upon graduation to demigodhood, Anahita gifted her with the <b>royal robes of Queen Amestris</b>; these garments are enchanted with soak equivalent to riot gear, and channel the War purview. After achieving apotheosis, she received <b>a silver circlet inset with jewel-like droplets of pure, solidified water</b>; this adds Anita's Legend rating in dice to all rolls involving the Health and Water purview.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-26-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:10:50-08:00","id":1006453,"title":"","content":"<u>Here are some less expected Scions.</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Hypnos</b> who hunts the things that go bump in the night, ensuring that mortals get the peaceful sleep they deserve. They eventually become the <i>God of Dreams</i>, commanding power over the psyche of mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Demeter</b> who uses their agricultural background to feed the poor and hungry. Eventually becoming known as the <i>Goddess of Charity</i>, they are somewhat paranoid about suffering a similar fate to their sister, Persephone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Hodur </b>who got the unfortunate luck of receiving their visitation just prior to Ragnarok! The nearly endless fight for survival during this period hardens them into a merciless warrior. They eventually become the new God of Winter, taking their father's place in the pantheon after he is slain by Vali.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Werethekau</b> who hopes to add as many Scions to the Netjer as possible while the war continues to wage on. They eventually become a God of the Forge, crafting powerful birthrights to aid them in their journeys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-21-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:45:54-08:00","id":1006572,"title":"","content":"Here are a few Scions that have yet to be played as PCs, but that I think would be fun:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Mark Fischer,</i></b><i><b> Scion of Njord</b></i>: A former naval aviator, Mark became a water-bomber pilot after mustering out. During one particularly vicious firefighting season, his plane was nearly caught in a forest fire caused directly by Muspelheim, and his efforts to fight it off anyway brought about Njord's intervention and his Visitation. Now equipped with a relic airplane, he does his best to combat Muspelheim's destructive intrusions into the World (although he seems to spends as much time playing taxi for his Bandmates and other Aesir Scions).<br /> <br /> <b><i>Pauline &quot;Poppy&quot; Turner, Scion of Hera: </i></b>Poppy is a sharp-witted society blogger with a tongue to match. She made her bones by airing the dirty laundry of half the major families in the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, with a focus on cheating spouses. Her quiet defiance of threats and bribes, and her dedication to using her blog to see justice done rather than (merely) for attention, prompted Hera to Visit her and make her one of her active agents in the World. These days, she travels with her Band, her poisoned pen writing odes that bring down Titan-backed giants of industry and government (and if she just happens to embarrass the occasional Scion of Zeus, well, that's what her cattle-baron daddy would call a &quot;bank-shot&quot;).<br /> <br /> <i><b>Rebecca Feng, Scion of Houyi:</b></i> Before her Visitation, Rebecca was a competition-level shooter from Seattle, training for the Olympic biathlon. Her Olympic tryouts were a disaster, thanks to Titan cultists who, acting on an incomplete oracular reading, took the training center hostage in the belief that they would capture a band of Shen Scions. What they got instead was Houyi intervening to save his daughter, and in their ashes Rebecca received her Visitation and her competition rifle was divinely blessed. Traveling now with a multi-pantheon Band, her face may never be on cereal boxes, but she'll never be bored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-06-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T22:43:58-08:00","id":1006596,"title":"","content":"<b>Kasen Palmer, Scion of Sun Wukong:</b> hailing from the island paradise of Jamaica, Kasen has been described by friends as a lovable ape, even though his father is technically a monkey. But even a life in the tropics grew boring sometimes when you're exposed to it all year round, and Kasen would find himself looking for other ways to soothe his rowdy tendencies. This ultimately resulted in him taking up boxing as a hobby, once he was old enough to compete. His punches were less about finesse and more about raw power, often laying his opponent unconscious within the first couple rounds, only to visit them after the fight to see if they wanted to hang out together!<br /> <br /> The first and last time Kasen attempted to make a professional career out of punching people's lights out, he had to end up in a fixed match. It seemed that a Titanspawn had bet a lot of money against Kasen, and had no intentions of losing the match. Unfortunately for both of them, neither did Kasen, and he refused the not so subtle threats against his person and ended up winning the match anyways. Neither Kasen, nor the monster he offended were aware that Sun Wukong had been in the audience that day, and arrived on the scene just as Kasen was being accosted by a band of thugs. Together, they succeeded in laying them out, while the monkey king gave him a brief explanation about his origins just before their boss came storming up to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kasen no longer boxes for sport, it's kind of unfair at this point when he has the strength of a gorilla coursing through his arms. But that doesn't mean he's stopped fighting all together. There are many Titanspawn looking to ruin peoples' day and he's all too happy to knock some sense into them. He joins his respective band as their heavy hitter, delivering blows powerful enough to shake the ground. Yet unlike most brawlers, he retains a happy go-lucky attitude towards life, instead of being a raging brute!<br /> <br /> The relic boxing gloves that Sun Wukong gave to him adds +3B to the Brass Knuckle template and adds his Legend to Strength + Brawl rolls. Additionally, they enable him to channel the Animal (ape) purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:41:18-08:00","id":1013191,"title":"","content":"<b>Tiffany Sweet, Scion of Titania:</b> What little girl doesn't dream of being a fairy princess at some point in their life? Unfortunately for young Tiffany, the reality proved much less appealing than the fantasy after she discovered her mother was Titania. As the queen of fairies, that made Tiffany a literal fairy princess in the eyes of the law. But Tiffany was an illegitimate child, the result of Titania having an affair with a mortal, and so she was smuggled out of the kingdom to avoid king Oberon's wrath. For the next 12 years, Tiffany would be raised in the care of her human father, who tried to subtly educate her about her heritage with fairy tales. Disney and Mother Goose were prominent in her childhood, but so too were the Brothers Grim, for her father wondered if she might need to learn about the darker side of her heritage.<br /> <br /> It turns out, she did, because Oberon eventually found out about the unsanctioned heir to his kingdom and decided to rid himself of her before she became a serious threat! On her 13th birthday, Tiffany received her visitation in the form of an attack by pixies flying into her home with the intent of assassinating her. Fortunately, Titania had already sent an agent of her own, and young Tiffany's life was saved by a handsome elf who bore a striking resemblance to Legolas. Yet despite his timely intervention, Tiffany's father was fatally poisoned in the attack. She was no longer safe in the company of mortals, and so the elf whisked her away to a place where he felt she could be safely protected. That place being in the company of other Scions like herself, beings who had their own supernatural powers to defend them against Oberon's fury.<br /> <br /> Under the guidance of her Alfar rescuer, Tiffany has begun training in the ways of archery, swordsmanship, and even fae magics. There will come a time when she must face the fairy king in battle to decide her fate, and she must be prepared for when that day arrives. Fortunately for her, she doesn't seem to possess the same intolerance for iron as the fair folk do. One benefit to being half human, she guesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-06-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T23:35:30-08:00","id":1017515,"title":"","content":"I wanted to explore a retelling of the Ares/Aphrodite/Hephaestus \u201clove triangle\u201d with their Scions, with more nuance and less petty and deliberately-hurtful behavior. People who generally mean well are just as capable of hurting each other while pursuing their hearts' desires, after all.<br /> <br /> I've yet to attempt using them as PCs (playing out the love triangle might be best left to a writing project), although earlier, less formed versions of them were used as NPCs in a 1e campaign.<br /> <br /> Coop, Gerry, and Frankie are intended as 2e characters, and will be adjusted as the ruleset becomes available.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <i><b>Cooper Atley, Scion of Hephaestus</b></i><br /> Callings: Creator (primary), Sage, Trickster<br /> Paths:<ul><li>Origin: \u201c<i>I didn't want to be stuck in a dead-end city, in a dead-end life</i>.\u201d (Blue-collar car thief; asset skills: Pilot, Subterfuge)</li> <li>Role: \u201c<i>I'm here to help save you guys. Now pass me the socket wrench and the Greek fire.\u201d </i>(Repair guy, artificer, and tech support to the gods; asset skills: Occult, Technology)</li> <li>Pantheon: \u201c<i>This feels just like high school.</i>\u201d (Son of Hephaestus, Scion of the Theoi; asset skills: Empathy, Persuasion)</li> </ul>Bio: A college dropout from Detroit, Cooper was a car thief who got into an accident the night of his Visitation. His divine father, Hephaestus, saved him; he was left with a permanent limp in his left leg, but also with his Birthrights and a mission to save the world while demonstrating how smart he is. After working with a number of Theoi Bands (and being the underappreciated \u201ctech guy\u201d around socialites and badass fighters), he hooked up with a multi-pantheon Band of wiseass do-gooders and found a real home there.<br /> <br /> Personality: Cooper is known for his dry humor under fire, his growing proficiency with repairing and creating relics, and an exaggeratedly world-weary attitude that poorly masks his concern for his friends. Older and somewhat more mature (for liberal values of \u201cmature\u201d) than most of his his Band-mates, Cooper isn't exactly the charismatic-leader type, but he finds himself falling easily into the role of \u201cteam dad.\u201d Under the world-weary concern is some lingering bitterness over his lame leg and the disdain from his glitterati pantheon-mates, but the friendship of his Band-mates and the adrenaline rush from daredevil heroics keeps it at bay most of the time.<br /> <br /> Powers/Birthrights: Cooper uses the Forge purview without need for a relic. His relic for the Epic Strength purview, the Olympic Slugger, is a baseball bat that, when imbued with Legend, assumes the qualities of a great sword (motif: \u201c<i>Percussive maintenance doesn't just work on machinery</i>.\u201d). His other relic, Vulcan's Override, is functionally identical to the Brigid's Key from Rhiannon Jernigan's writeup in the Early Access PDF.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Gerald Rafferty, Scion of Mars</b></i><br /> Callings: Guardian, Leader (favored), Warrior<br /> Paths:<ul><li>Origin: \u201c<i>A soldier defends the people who can't defend themselves</i>.\u201d (Former British Army officer; asset skills: Athletics, Firearms)</li> <li>Path: \u201c<i>Someone's got to clean this place up, and take care of the people.\u201d </i>(Idealistic warrior-king in the making; asset skills: Close Combat, Leadership)</li> <li>Pantheon: \u201c<i>Clausewitz had no idea how right he was</i>.\u201d (Son of Mars, Scion of the Theoi; asset skills: Empathy, Persuasion)</li> </ul>Bio: Gerald was an instructor and platoon leader in the British Army, deployed to Afganistan as part of Operation Toral. While on patrol one day, his platoon encountered titanspawn and the survivors of a Scion Band they were pursuing. Gerald and his platoon helped defeat the monsters, but most of them died in the process. In the aftermath, Ares (wearing his mantle as Mars) Visited his son, bringing him a weapon and informing him of the greater war he was now part of. Now believed to be KIA, Gerald and his surviving troops travel with the Band they helped, fighting the real enemy.<br /> <br /> Personality: Before his Visitation, Gerald was optimistic and idealistic, and his affable leadership won him respect from his subordinates and peers. (This same natural talent for command has made him his new Band's war leader.) He also attracted derision from his superiors, many of whom let their prejudices take the wheel when dealing with their Afghani allies and the local civilian population. Since his Visitation, however, a ruthless streak has surfaced in his personality. He is still driven to take care of his people and defend civilians, but he has grown frustrated how both the local leaders and the ones from the major powers are handling things in the region. A thought keeps occurring to him: \u201cI could do better than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Powers: Gerald uses the War purview without need for a relic, and his relic for the Order purview is a Roman legate's baton (motif: \u201c<i>Leaders stand in the line of fire.</i>\u201d). His relic weapon, Fuliminis, can take the form of either a gladius or an assault rifle; the rifle form has unlimited ammunition, and the sword form has the Piercing quality (motif: \u201c<i>The right weapon for any battle</i>.\u201d). His followers are the survivors of his platoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Francesca \u201cFrankie\u201d Russo, Scion of Aphrodite</b></i><br /> Callings: Liminal, Lover, Sage (favored) (Francesca would also possess any edges related to prophecy)<br /> Paths:<ul><li>Origin: \u201c<i>It's not fair, being treated as a resource instead of a daughter.</i>\u201d (Raised by adoptive parents who exploited her oracular talents; asset skills: Leadership, Occult)</li> <li>Path: \u201c<i>Sometimes on stage, I lose myself in the role. Those are the moments I live for.</i>\u201d (Stage actress making a name for herself; asset skills: Culture, Subterfuge)</li> <li>Pantheon: \u201c<i>What I want is not what I'm drawn to. Story of my life.\u201d</i> (Daughter of Aphrodite, Scion of the Theoi; asset skills: Empathy, Persuasion)</li> </ul>Bio: The child of Aphrodite's affair with a mortal prophet, Francesca was adopted at a young age by an ambitious Miami couple. Hearing of her eerily accurate predictions, they saw her as a \u201cgood investment,\u201d and proceeded to exploit her for her entire childhood. While she was well cared for physically, she was treated as little better than an employee, and her adoptive parents made a point of trying to snuff out her dreams of acting on stage. During this time, she managed to not only hone her prophetic talents, but learn to read and manipulate people, and finally managed to blackmail her way out from under the Russos' thumb.<br /> <br /> She moved to New York, using her self-appropriated \u201cseverance package\u201d to fund her tuition in Columbia's theater program. Her mother \u2013 her <i>real </i>mother \u2013 found her quickly, though, and this was one person Francesca didn't know how to outmaneuver. Without quite understanding why, she agreed to be an agent for her mother's interests (and the world's, of course). These days, she gets in her acting fix wherever she can, even though supernatural demands \u2013 playing oracle and face for her Band \u2013 seem to push her further and further off Broadway. She hasn't quite cottoned to the fact of the larger stage she's performing on yet.<br /> <br /> Personality: Like many of Aphrodite's children, Francesca loves the spotlight and being showered with attention. This is tempered by a sober awareness of her prophetic abilities, and how little joy they actually bring to the world. She is a compassionate individual, albeit one who has a tendency to hide that side of herself (the toll of the emotional exploitation of her adoptive parents has left its mark); because of this, she is rapidly becoming the emotional bedrock of her Band. Never quite comfortable in her own skin, and not comfortable at all when prophesying, she is happiest when immersed in a role on the stage. Sadly, the demands of being a Scion mean that she enjoys this escape less and less.<br /> <br /> One more thing. Never, <i>ever</i> use the term \u201cgood investment\u201d in front of her.<br /> <br /> Birthrights/Powers: Francesca uses the Deception purview without need for a relic. She wears her relic for the Artistry and Passion purviews, a pendant in the form of a silver-limned dove's feather, on a chain around her neck; the pendant can also assume the form of a silver dagger, ensuring she is armed at all times (motif: \u201c<i>I speak my truth, and I make my own fate</i>.\u201d). Her guide is Ione, a nereid talented with hydromantic auguries; she can be contacted by suspending a ring on a thread in a bowl of water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-15-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:26:19-08:00","id":1017588,"title":"","content":"I've had the beginnings of a team floating around in my head for a while, though details tend to change from moment to moment. Here's what I've got so far:<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bSabrina Benoit, Daughter of Hephaestus</b><br /> <br /> Bio: \u200bThe only daughter of an unmarried, struggling Parisian mechanic, Sabrina would've likely looked forward to a lean life herself had she not mysteriously won a scholarship to MIT, citing her natural brilliance as an engineer. While this was entirely accurate, the mysterious thing is that she never applied for any scholarship. Several years later, after her graduation party (double major in mechanical and electrical engineering) she got a surprise late visit from one of her professors, who only revealed his identity - and her nature - after a long talk about her future in the field. That future, he revealed, would have to wait: She had a part to play as a member of a Band whose role might be bigger than either of them knew.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonality: Sabrina considers herself an engineer first and all else second, but she can't deny an instinctive drive to protect her friends and family. As formidable physically as intellectually, she's more than capable of shouldering both burdens; sometimes she outright welcomes the challenge. Headstrong, loyal and honest to a fault, her lack of guile can lead to putting her foot in her mouth but her heart is always in the right place.<br /> <br /> \u200bBirthrights/Powers: Sabrina channels the Forge purview without a relic. Her two relics are a shield that expands from a large, bronze bracer on her left forearm (Epic Stamina, Epic Strength; motif: <i>\u200b&quot;This is my shield, I'm theirs.&quot;</i>\u200b) and a complicated tool of her own design, employing divine magic as much as mechanical technology to form a wide variety of tools or a large, flaming battlehammer (Fire, Earth; motif: <i>\u200b&quot;To shape and to shatter.&quot;</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bAva Chance, Daughter of Bastet</b><br /> <br /> \u200bBio: Born of a random encounter in a bar between a drunken goddess and a master assassin on his time off, Ava has been brought up understanding three things: First, that she is her own woman, free to do as she pleases and to accept the consequences; second, that there is value in both honesty and deception, so long as you know where and how to apply them; and third, that the world can be a pants-destroyingly terrifying place and it is irresponsible not to learn how to fight, lie and sneak. She received her Visitation early in life as her mother appeared to help her cope with her 'inner warrior,' but didn't set out on her own adventures until some time later. When she was ready her father pointed her in the direction of a nascent Band of Scions who might appreciate her talents... or in his words &quot;I'd be surprised if they last a week without you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personality: Ava Chance is a trickster at heart, and loves little more than to watch other peoples' reactions, whether to pranks of hers or absurd happenings around them. Always equipped with a sly quip and a grin, she firmly believes in living for the moment, not for any plan or ideal. With that said, she does value her Band more with each passing day, though she shows her loyalty more as a cat would, smug yet charming. She's learned to strike where she's least expected and always have an escape plan, traits that have served her well as the Band's scout and sometimes their thief.<br /> <br /> \u200bBirthrights/Powers: Ava channels the Epic Dexterity purview without a relic. She wears the Shroud of Nyx (Deception, Darkness; motif: <i>\u200b&quot;Shadow on my back and sand in their eyes.&quot;</i>\u200b) a cloak her father came across long ago and passed down to her. It has the ability to change her clothing to any set she can picture, though it gains no special properties - it's just an illusion. Her mother gave her Sandstorm, a cat that can grow to the size of a tiger when needed.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Logan McAllister, Son of Mannanan mac Lir</b><br /> <br /> \u200bBio: Fostered by an incarnation of Lugh and a mortal innkeeper, Logan spent his childhood shuffling back and forth between Lugh's <i>sidhe</i>\u200b realm and a neighboring town in rural Ireland. Even from a young age he knew what he wanted. He had an insatiable wanderlust, a burning desire to see the world, and a deep-seated need to find out who his mother was, the one question about his heritage that nobody seemed to have the answer to. Eventually this overcame his sense of caution: At the age of fourteen he set out on his own, with only a staff and a backpack, in search of wonders, adventure and answers. He found no shortage of the first two, but it was discovering his Band that brought him closest to family, as Mannanan himself - in the guise of a passing traveler with a fondness for cryptic lessons - guided him there.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonality: A man who sets off at age fourteen to see the world doesn't seem like a calm and thoughtful sort, but Logan is just that. He's learned to be observant, using his wit and charm to get around rather than resorting to force if at all possible. While he dislikes spending too long in one place, he never seems in any great hurry. He has a friendly, optimistic demeanor that only ever fades in dire circumstances, and his talent for helping, guiding and inspiring people makes him well-liked.<br /> <br /> \u200bBirthrights/Powers: Logan channels the Journeys purview without a relic. He wields a crook-tipped staff that always seems to be <i>just</i>\u200b the right length and shape for whatever he needs it for (Sky; motif: <i>\u200b&quot;A good staff is always useful.&quot;</i>\u200b) and wears a vial of waters from the healing springs of Sirona strung around his neck (Health; motif: <i>&quot;To ease the body and soul.&quot;</i>\u200b) that grant a sense of peace to anyone who drinks them. He also has the favor of an <i>aes sidhe</i> stargazer (Moon, Stars) whom he can contact using any reflective surface exposed to moonlight. He carries a polished silver mirror for this purpose, but there's nothing especially magical about it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bOther ideas I haven't really developed as far as these include a therianthrope soldier with a rifle and a mystical wolfskin used to control the affliction, a samurai whose blade lashes out with razor-sharp water and a blind Taoist immortal sage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:23:00-08:00","id":1018250,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a Scion of Mannanan who is disturbingly similar to Logan up there, albiet with a more 'reckless, passionate idiot' theme to him.<br /> <br /> I also have an idea for a Scion of Mars/Ares. The idea is that he had been conceived by the Graceo-Roman God of War in his Ares mantle and had inherited his vicious berserker tendencies, but was Visited by the God of War in his Mars mantle and gained an inclination towards orderly, guardian-like tendencies. So he'd go through his adventures trying to decide which version of his father he wanted to style himself after and would maybe towards the end realize it doesn't matter and that he can be his own person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T19:08:09-08:00","id":1019556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=973479#post973479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second, a former undercover cop named Vera Wolff... doesn't actually know who her divine parent is. Oh, she knows she's of the Aesir, Odin told her that when he made her Visitation <i>personally</i>, but he specifically told her that he wasn't her sire, and refused to tell her who.<br /> <br /> It's Loki. She wasn't told because the Aesir look at his Scions with suspicion at best. Odin picked her because she has a lot of Loki's more <i>useful</i> traits, but unlike him, if Vera gives her loyalty, it's dammed near absolute. She'll go undercover, sure, and play the part well, but at the end of the day her convictions are firm.<br /> <br /> (The unaware bit isn't essential to the second, mind you)</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea's... been <i>expanded</i> on. And been given a character image.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Vera Wolff, Scion of Loki</b></i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/7WpoMgn.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Callings: Liminal (Favoured), Lover, Warrior<br /> Paths:<ul><li><i>&quot;A Child Of New Money&quot;</i> (Born to a newly rich mother- who was often snubbed by Old Money. Asset Skills: Persuasion, Liberal Arts)</li> <li><i>&quot;A License To Kill&quot; </i>(Literally has Bond as a co-worker- she's 009. Asset Skills: Larceny, Aim)</li> <li><i>&quot;Surprising White Sheep&quot;</i> (Vera's many things, but not a coward- and that's earned surprising respect from many of the Aesir despite her father's Fated role in Ragnarok and his often-antagonistic relationship to the rest of the family. Asset Skills: Brawl, Integrity)</li> </ul>Bio: Born to a wealthy businesswoman, Vera Wolff never knew her father growing up- but she does understand that she always had a surprising amount of skill in subterfuge, a skill that lead her to join the Secret Intelligence Service as an operative agent- and from there, she grew in skill until she was assigned the code number of 009, given the task of being one of Britain's 'troubleshooters' when problems needed to be handled at least relatively quietly- but with lethal force. Her Visitation happened in the aftermath of an early mission, when the unexpected presence of Titanspawn caused a mission to go badly south and her father rescued her. In the wake, Vera was seconded to the SIS' Paranormal Activities Division, and works as a representative of the UK as much as she does for the Aesir- fortunately, the Aesir can appreciate that sort of intense loyalty towards one's homeland.<br /> <br /> Personality: On the job, Vera Wolff is relatively cold- she isn't cruel by any means, but she's got a job to do, a job that often includes killing people from the shadows, and like certain coworkers, she deals with that by taking a somewhat cavalier attitude to death. She's efficient, and she gets the job done by any means necessary. In private and off the job, she's a lot warmer- she's even got a steady girlfriend (note: who, exactly, the girlfriend is might vary), and she likes to get to know her fellow Bandmates. Behind the somewhat cold demeanour on the job, essentially, Vera Wolff is brave and intensely loyal- and those two things have gained her the respect of the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Purviews/Birthrights: Vera uses the Deception Purview without the need for a Relic. Her gun, a Walter P99 which Loki did... <i>something</i> to during her Visitation, can now be used to channel the Fire and Chaos Purviews (motif: <i>&quot;The Subtle Knife&quot;</i>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","user":"horngeek","date":". 12-19-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T22:58:03-08:00","id":1023131,"title":"","content":"Some more characters, intended for 2e: <hr /> <b><i>Ryuuzaki Mari, Scion of Takemikazuchi*</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Capsule: A B-list actress, hired primarily for her looks and ability to handle a sword, finding herself turned into a live-action swordfighting heroine.</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Face credit: <a href=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SehLkOhiNIc/maxresdefault.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Mizuno Sonoya</a></i><br /> <br /> Callings: Guardian, Lover, Warrior (primary)<br /> <br /> Bio: Mari was always fidgety and excitable. But her mother Kyoko, a kenjutsu instructor in Yokohama, understood what she needed: a focus for that nervous energy. And kenjutsu fit Mari like a glove. It reminded Kyoko of her late husband Kenichi, whom she'd met in university, and who also took to kenjutsu like a fish to water. The art was one of the few things that could calm her down, and the same went for when she discovered acting in high school. Far from ruining her focus on either one, both interests together acted as a kind of stabilizing agent on her personality. Mari blossomed, and people noticed (not that she really noticed them noticing).<br /> <br /> Once in college, Mari took some acting courses, and drew the attention of a TV producer who was looking for someone to fill out a new series. It was light fare, little more than the sillier Shinto myths dressed up in quasi-sentai frippery, and Mari's looks and kenjutsu background counted for more than her acting ability. But it was definitely a foot in the door, and again, people noticed. Unfortunately, some of those people were cultists in service to one of the more malicious Titans. Trained to recognize even un-Visited Scions, they attacked Mari, intending to make a gift of her to their patron.<br /> <br /> Takemikazuchi intervened instead, rescuing Mari and introducing himself. According to him, Mari's family on both side had a strong divine and heroic lineage, with her late father actually being a Scion that he had been unable to Visit before his untimely death. Mari was skeptical of what she was hearing, but she'd seen Takemikazuchi take apart the cultists with the giant glowing tachi, and the thought of helping other heroes save the world <i>for real</i> appealed to her.<br /> <br /> As it stands, Mari is now trotting the globe with an inter-pantheon Band, fighting monsters and saving innocents. Her acting career is apparently shot... although, from the growing amount of YouTube footage starring her and her friends, she might have a future in pictures after all.<br /> <br /> Personality: As befits a child of a storm god, Mari can be a little tempestuous and capricious. Her heart is generally in the right place, though, and most of the time her attitude is easy-going and likable, giving her an artless kind of charisma. There are two things she's never had trouble concentrating on, her acting and her kenjutsu, and her focus where these are concerned is laser-like. While she is friendly enough to pinch-hit as a social operator, such is not her forte; in her Band, she is usually the close-range muscle.<br /> <br /> Birthrights/Powers: Mari uses the Epic Strength purview without need for a relic. Her relic for the Sky purview, Arashibana, is a tachi forged by Susano-O from one of her father's lightning bolts, with a blade that is permanently glowing blue-white and crackling with electricity; it has a +3 enhancement to Damage (motif: \u201c<i>I hold the storm in the palm of my hand.</i>\u201d) Her relic for the Artistry purview is a pair of storm-grey magatama earrings, and she goes to great lengths to have them included as part of her characters' \u201clook,\u201d regardless of what role she is playing (motif: \u201c<i>Keep your eyes on me</i>.\u201d).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Mari's inherited power set is based on Takemikazuchi's assocated powers from Watcher and Sacerdos' Kami revision for their Scion 2.0 project. Dependent on what official stats for Scions of Takemikazuchi may look like, they may be adjusted.<br /> <hr /> <i><b>Martin del Rio, Scion of Quetzalcoatl</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Capsule: Attorney and political activist, who finds his activism and idealistic crusading moved to a greater stage.</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>Face credit: <a href=\"http://monrowemagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/20160627_MONROWE_PG_766-768x1152.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Peter Gadiot</a></i><br /> <br /> Callings: Healer, Leader (primary), Sage<br /> <br /> Bio: Martin spent most of his youth bouncing around the Dallas-Fort Worth foster-care system. Even at a young age, the academic talents of his divine father shone through, and he committed to his studies, with a determination to control his own life as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> At first, this was mostly a metaphorical middle finger, aimed at the well-meaning-but-clueless or prejudiced and uncaring people he'd encountered in the system. His goal was, more or less, to get himself into a position to stick it to them the way he felt they'd be sticking it to him. Eventually, though, he developed empathy for others in similar straits. That drive to control his own life, which had largely been aimed at getting himself into a comfortable position, became one to reform the political system so others wouldn't suffer.<br /> <br /> Martin made his way through college and law school at the top of his class, with a combination of rock-solid will and earnest affability. As he began his law career, he quickly drew attention, both positive and negative. As is so often the case with Scions, it was the latter that brought about his awakening. His involvement in a local controversial trial had tempers on both sides of the issue fraying and flaring, and some local radicals decided the best way to deal with it was to take out the lawyer.<br /> <br /> The Feathered Serpent intervened, in a spectacular fashion that left those radicals gibbering in the local mental ward for months. In the aftermath, as the mortal authorities cleaned up and Martin celebrated the trial's verdict, Quetzalcoatl told him about his heritage and the threats facing the World. He went on to point out how great the need for people with his skills were among the forces facing those threats. \u201cWe have warriors aplenty,\u201d Quetzalcoatl said earnestly. \u201cBut natural leaders and speakers? Those are as rare as relics from past Ages. Your talents are needed on a greater stage than that of mere nations.\u201d<br /> <br /> Martin was still coming to grips with the fact that this was his father, not to mention that he'd never done much of a father's job. But his attorney's ear could hear the the honesty in Quetzalcoatl's voice. It was an uncomfortable truth, and with a sense of destiny (and resignation), he agreed to lend a hand.<br /> <br /> Personality: Martin is a natural leader, radiating honest devotion to his activism and a magnetic affability. He is also eloquent and well-read. However, he constantly struggles with stridency; when he loses, those who are indifferent or hostile to his aims often find him off-putting (or, worse, threatening). As a Scion, he tends to act as the face of his Band, though his command of the Sky purview gives him some potent combat ability.<br /> <br /> Powers/Birthrights: Martin can use the Sky purview without need for a relic. His relic for the Order and Passion purviews is a shirt woven from the discarded feathers of his divine father's feathered-serpent form, dyed with iridescent ichor-based hues from <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Xochiquetzal</span></span></span>; the shirt can take the form of any upper-body garment Martin desires, but will always retain that iridescent hue (motif: \u201c<i>One part of ruling is a commanding presence</i>.\u201d). His guide is Veronica Gomez, an older and more experienced Scion of Quetzalcoatl who has already achieved upper-tier demigod status.<br /> <br /> <hr /> <i><b>Lydia Choudhary, Scion of Hermes</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Capsule: Street racer turned professional wheelwoman, now playing courier and taxi for heroes and gods.</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>Face credit: <a href=\"http://st1.bollywoodlife.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/sonakshi-.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Sonakshi Sinha</a></i><br /> <br /> Callings: Liminal, Trickster (primary), Warrior<br /> <br /> Bio: Born and raised in Vancouver, BC, Lydia was always drawn to cars. (Much of this could be blamed on her stepfather Vikram, whom she is still close to. A mechanic and driver for the city's mass-transit system, he exposed her from a young age to motor vehicles as more than just simple transportation.) While not much of a mechanic, she had a natural flair for actually piloting vehicles. (This might have something to do with all the practice she got driving, ahem, <i>not</i> legally behind her parents' backs.)<br /> <br /> No great shakes at academics, Lydia got a job in an auto parts store after high school. From there, she found her way into the street racing scene, and quickly became prominent in it for her driving talents and risk-taker attitude. This latter tendency drew her towards riskier and less legal ventures, until one day she was approached indirectly by an anonymous employer to drive for a \u201csimple, easy job.\u201d Naturally, it was anything but, and completing it (to say nothing of getting away cleanly) took all of Lydia's driving genius and ability to run the edge.<br /> <br /> At the rendezvous waited that mysterious employer, a handsome man of Mediterranean ancestry with a beautifully-maintained muscle car. As the other thieves dispersed with their payouts, he asked Lydia to go for a ride, and tossed her the keys. They drove around for hours, as Hermes introduced himself, and told her a story about the true state of the World and how it needed heroes to save it from cosmic terrors. Lydia knew a line of bullshit when she heard it, but this story had an uncomfortable ring of truth.<br /> <br /> Hermes told her that it was time for her to join the fight, gave her a pair of Oakleys and her cut from the heist, and bade her drop him off at the nearest intersection. The next day, Lydia told her mom and stepdad goodbye, spinning a line about a \u201cbetter job in Ontario.\u201d Taking her Birthrights and a 9mm she'd... acquired somewhere, she hit the road, uneasily expecting adventure to find her. She wasn't wrong.<br /> <br /> Personality: Lydia is something of an adrenaline-junkie, and is happiest behind the wheel, breaking local speed ordinances and racing against time to save the world. This often conflicts with her protective feelings towards her mother and stepfather, who are not \u201cin the know\u201d about her divine heritage. She tries to keep them in the dark about it (both out of a sense of protecting them and so she can avoid awkward questions). Devotion to a greater good or abstract ideals is something she struggles with, and few of her pantheon's myths do much to inspire loyalty either (eye-rolling obedience, yes. Loyalty, not really). Her family, or friends who've proven themselves to her, though... that's a different story. And her Band-mates have proven themselves to her. While her main function in her Band is wheelwoman, she is also fairly talented at the \u201crogue\u201d skillset.<br /> <br /> Birthrights/Powers: Lydia uses the Journeys purview without need for a relic. Her relic for the Epic Dexterity purview is a souped-up muscle car that adds +1 to Maneuverability (or 2e's equivalent), never needs refueling, and, when imbued with Legend, can make cosmetic changes to its appearance (the fact that it's a two-door sports car can never be changed, but its make, model, and paint job can be) (motif: <i>\u201cShe'll get you there, one way or another.\u201d</i>)<i>. </i>Her relic for the Deception purview is a pair of Oakley sunglasses (motif: \u201c<i>You see what you want to see. I'll help with that</i>.\u201d).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>This is a close approximation of <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4e/1966_Shelby_GT350_%282%29.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">the car</a>: </i></b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 02-18-2017, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:12:35-08:00","id":1034894,"title":"","content":"Stacy Barnes, Scion of Poseidon, cowgirl rodeo champion, destined to become Anastasia, Goddess of Horses. (I candidly admit that she's essentially Applejack from My Little Pony made in to a Scion.)<br /> <br /> At some point I'd like to play a Scion of Hestia who is potentially the God of Butlers. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:24:07-08:00","id":1034899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1034894#post1034894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stacy Barnes, Scion of Poseidon, cowgirl rodeo champion, destined to become Anastasia, Goddess of Horses. (I candidly admit that she's essentially Applejack from My Little Pony made in to a Scion.)<br /> <br /> At some point I'd like to play a Scion of Hestia who is potentially the God of Butlers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, I made a similar character idea to that. Except she becomes the Goddess of Animal Husbandry. She spends her free time wrestling ornery beasts into submission. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:23:00-08:00","id":1034925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1034899#post1034899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey, I made a similar character idea to that. Except she becomes the Goddess of Animal Husbandry. She spends her free time wrestling ornery beasts into submission. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, earlier I mentioned that I have an expy of Applejack, a child of the Manitouk.<br /> <br /> There's only one way to settle this. THUNDER DOME!<br /> <br /> THREE EXPIES ENTER, ONE EXPY LEAVES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:42:53-08:00","id":1034938,"title":"","content":"Yes, but mine is backed up by the Goddesses of Fashion (Scion of Apollo), Parties (Dionysus), Libraries (Athena), Nurturing (Pan) and Awesomeness (Iris). Brony-Nerd Advantage: Me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:04:21-08:00","id":1051164,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Astrid Thurston, Scion of Thor</i></b><br /> Callings: Lover, Trickster, Warrior (primary)<br /> Paths:<ul><li>Origin: \u201c<i>Dad was never around and Mom was an overbearing hypocrite</i>. <i>So yeah, my childhood could have better. Just-a-wee-bit.</i>\u201d (Runaway; Asset skills: Subterfuge, Survival)</li> <li>Role: \u201c<i>I\u2019m a Social Justice Skald. If that\u2019s not a thing, then I\u2019m totally going to make it a thing.\u201d </i>(Modern day punk rocker, rebel without a cause, and black bloc anarchist; Asset skills: Empathy, Persuasion)</li> <li>Pantheon: \u201c<i>Not too keen on having a king to boss me around, but at least they know how to have fun.</i>\u201d (Daughter of Thor, Scion of the Aesir; Asset skills: Athletics, Close Combat)</li> </ul><br /> Bio: Astrid Thurston is a punk rock musician (she prefers to be called a skald) barely out of her teens from a small town in Denmark that most people have never heard of and she\u2019d like to forget about. When Astrid was younger she repeatedly ran away from home whenever things got heated with her mother who would berate her constantly for being too much like her absentee father. Consequently, her biggest role models growing up were her friends in similar domestic situations and the burned-out rockers that she would see performing in bars whenever she ran away. The cycle of running away and crashing with friends only to come back for one reason or another finally came to an end when her mother died in a car accident during a thunderstorm. Filled with guilt over not being able to resolve her differences with her mother Astrid purposely got into a tavern brawl that quickly went too far. Fortunately, she was saved by a valkyrie sent by her father Thor, God of Thunder. Getting her Visitation has given Astrid a new sense purpose and she has taken to the adventures that come with being a Scion with gusto, if only because it serves as a distraction from thinking about her past.<br /> <br /> Personality: Irresponsible, immature, compulsive, destructive, hedonistic, brash, crass, and far too willing to get into a screaming match (or an outright brawl) when she gets into an argument with someone who sets off one of her neuroses, Astrid is someone whose fun to be around for a while but can quickly become unbearable when set off by something. That said, she is loyal to the few friends she does have and is willing to make to a sincere apologetic overture (albeit usually a very weird one) when she knows she\u2019s in the wrong. Usually rebellious towards any authority she finds unworthy of respect and prone to throwing caution to the wind, Astrid has tried to mature now that she\u2019s a Scion and at times has successfully used her street-smart cunning to resolve touchy situations. It doesn\u2019t always work, but it is an improvement from her former mode of always shout or punch her away out of a problem.<br /> <br /> Interests: Astrid has a wide-eyed love of 80s culture, particularly the heavy metal music, cheap horror films, and fashion styles that came from that period. She can do without all the glamor rock makeup though. She also used to play baseball in her teens and has found having a good back-swing to be immensely useful when fighting trolls.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Before her Visitation Astrid was a somewhat lanky youth with bright red hair, freckles, and even brighter blue eyes. As she\u2019s grown as a Scion of the Aesir she\u2019s become more toned and even taller.<br /> <br /> Sexuality: \u201cI dunno, I just like people, alright. No need to get all categorical about it, or whatever.\u201d<br /> <br /> Associated Character Tropes: Tomboy, Action Girl, Plucky Girl, Byronic Hero, Guile Hero, The Ladette, Rebellious Spirit, The Gadfly, Jerk with a Heart of Gold, Metalhead, Youthful Freckles<br /> Inspirations/Characters I Ripped Off: Peppermint Patty (Peanuts), Sera (Dragon Age: Inquisition), Toph (Avatar the Last Airbender), Marceline (Adventure Time)<br /> <br /> Future Goddess of Rebellion, Audacity, Rage, Tempests, and Skalds<br /> <br /> Face: Paloma Kwiatkowski<br /> <br /> - Props to yukikaze for the layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 05-06-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","cust