el=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Trivia the Roman name for Hecate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could be, I only know about them because of the Disney Hercules show when he made an appearance. They were voiced by the Clear Eyes guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T10:37:46-07:00","id":1085496,"title":"","content":"<b>Twin daughters of Izanami;</b> the elder sister is bright, cheerful and uplifting, while the younger sister is dark, moody and depressing. Their Legend paints a contrasting image on the nature of life and death when the elder sister becomes a goddess of death and funerals, while the younger sister takes on the mantle of birth and life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A son of Izanagi</b> who frequently tries to convince his father to get back into the dating world. Eventually becoming a god of love and romance; he is seen as a divine matchmaker among the Amatsukami, although his efforts are not always appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Triplet daughters of Raiden</b> who imitate their father's habit of eating people when they're in a bad mood. Together, they go onto become joint weather goddesses who bring various levels of storms to the land. The youngest daughter brings light, gentle rainfall that rejuvenates the land, the middle daughter brings heavy storms that may cause minor flooding issues. The eldest sister is the most violent of them all, bringing forth devastating storms that force people to seek shelter, or risk their destruction at her hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:25:05-07:00","id":1085891,"title":"","content":"I keep trying to come up with an NPC band that's an all women soccer team. I just can't figure out who they should be Scions of. Maybe Apollo, Huitzilopochtli, Heimdall (the goalie), Parvadi, and Vahram.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:36:44-07:00","id":1085895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1085891#post1085891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep trying to come up with an NPC band that's an all women soccer team. I just can't figure out who they should be Scions of. Maybe Apollo, Huitzilopochtli, Heimdall (the goalie), Parvadi, and Vahram.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Considering the Aztecs practically invented the sport of kicking somebody's head across the field, I'd say their pantheon should be the most prominent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T15:54:57-07:00","id":1085923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1085895#post1085895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Considering the Aztecs practically invented the sport of kicking somebody's head across the field, I'd say their pantheon should be the most prominent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the ancient Celts used to get credit for that as well. I've no idea how true said stories are, though. But apparently soccer/football was being played in medieval Britain, Ireland and France, as well as in first millennium China and Japan, so I guess it's just one of those ideas that was inevitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:55:15-07:00","id":1086014,"title":"","content":"Had the idea of a gonzo journalist Scion of Dionysus. He'd be more focused on the out of towner coming in and revealing truths but still gets to play with the madness and chemically altered nature of Dionysus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:15:55-07:00","id":1086023,"title":"","content":"A scion of <b>THE EMPEROR</b>, who goes around <b>ANNIHILATING HERETICS</b> with their relic <b>CHAINSAW SWORD!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0