t1088485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a student of religions and runs an occult book shop, more of an academic than a believer. That's why she's as surprised as anyone when Baphomet appears and reveals her heritage... something she vehemently objects to.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're one of the least-real gods out there! You were made up!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If I ever need another person to fit into one of my Scion games I'll hit you up, because your concepts are killer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T21:07:57-07:00","id":1090105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1090085#post1090085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I ever need another person to fit into one of my Scion games I'll hit you up, because your concepts are killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty powerful compliment, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T12:20:51-07:00","id":1090817,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a defense attorney who is well on the way to becoming the god of reasonable doubt. I'm just not sure who he should be a scion of. Something like Horus, Tyr, or Mithra seems too obvious. Maybe Hermes, Vishnu or one of the Celestial Bureaucracy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T12:21:42-07:00","id":1090818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1089757#post1089757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Scion of Bastet who uploads magical cat videos onto the internet, allowing his mother to spy upon millions of people's internet history across the world!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just crazy enough to work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T11:34:22-07:00","id":1094238,"title":"","content":"<b>A Scion of Fuxi</b> who combines magic and medicine to expand the realm of genetic engineering. He hopes to change the human form, while keeping its spirit intact, thus bringing about the age of trans humanism and self controlled evolution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Damballa</b> who's serves as the sassy, gay friend of his respective band. He favors using his well toned, muscular body to charm the pants off his enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Yama</b> who's cynical world view inadvertently lead to a sarcastic sense of humor. Aside from giving dry quips to friend and foe alike, he casually strolls into battle against the forces of the Titans, once they start causing trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:16:35-07:00","id":1103191,"title":"","content":"All his life, <b>Alex &quot;Shortlegs&quot; Ostlund</b> has struggled with the physical limitations of dwarfism. Only to find out that he's an actual dwarf; well, half dwarf, actually. It's complicated, but at least he isn't turning to stone in the sun or some crazy stuff like that! On the eve of his 16th birthday, he received a visit from Tyr, claiming to be his grandfather. The visitation came with many nifty perks that enabled him to manage his condition more easily, which Alex is grateful for. Unfortunately, it did nothing to fix his size, leaving him the butt of several running jokes among the rest of the Norse pantheon. That's okay, though, because &quot;Shortlegs&quot; has found a source of inspiration in Tyr, who knows what it's like to live with physical impairments. And he's determined to show all the &quot;Longlegs&quot; what a divinely empowered little person is capable of!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-25-2017, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:17:56-07:00","id":1118535,"title":"","content":"The reincarnation of Mongan ap Fiachna, the son of Manannan mac Lir. Like his former incarnation he was conceived upon his mortal mother in exchange for saving the life of someone she held dear. However in a odd twist the one saved was the character himself who was born without the breath of life. Manannan thus breathed the soul of his most famous scion into the infant's body to keep the bargain. Like in his past life the new Mongan is a friend of the sidhe, was taught shape-shifting (through Illusion) and esoteric knowledge (through Mystery). He is looking to become the Tuatha deity of Secrets, Philosophy, and Mysticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:14:34-07:00","id":1125068,"title":"","content":"Okay, wow! It took me <b><i>way too god damn long</i></b> to get around to writing this up! I think it was put on the back burner for over a year?<br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>The Rising Stars:</b> Consisting entirely of Greek Scions, the band known as The Rising Stars are a young group of teenagers who still have room to grow not only as agents of divine will, but also people. Despite their youth, the band is constantly on the move and never remains in any one place for more than a couple months if they can help it. This is due in large part to one of their members acting as a bounty hunter who's prey is constantly trying to avoid detection. But sometimes other factors come into play that force them to make a sudden relocation before things get too dangerous.<br /> <br /> Over the course of their existence, the band has managed to make themselves the arch rivals of another bunch of Scions calling themselves The Golden Pyramid (who will be posted... eventually). Consisting entirely of Egyptian related Scions, the Pyramid have clashed with The Rising Stars on several occasions, and it seems Fate conspires to arrange many more encounters in the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cooper Cross, Scion of Hades:</b> Only 16 years of age and already has a steady means of income. Cooper was assigned the position of bounty hunter for the Underworld and much of his time as a Scion is spent tracking down the escapees from Tartarus and sending them back to prison. This duty often dictates where his band travels to next, but Cooper is not opposed to taking detours if his fellow Scions have personal business of their own to deal with. It's not as if Hades gave him a time limit for bringing down wanted criminals. Before his visitation, Cooper was a completely normal high school student and knew nothing of the existence of the supernatural. But when a cyclops killed his mortal parents while he was returning home from school, Hades decided to intervene.<br /> <br /> It was during this mission that he met Samantha and the two of them worked together to bring down the target. The cyclops had turned an entire youth center worth of boys into his thralls and it was now a bigger job than just facing one enemy. Afterwards, Samantha insisted on training him to be a more competent Scion. They've been having mandatory training sessions every week from then on.<br /> <br /> Cooper's relics include a yet unnamed kama who's handle is fashioned out of human bone and who's blade is composed of black iron. The kama allows him to channel the Death and Darkess purviews. He also carries a magically updating bounty list, which provides him with a rap sheet about his current targets.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Samantha Joves, Scion of Zeus: </b>The mirror opposite of Cooper in both gender and upbringing. Samantha's mother was a member of one of Zeus' cults, who raised her practically from birth in preparation for her life as a Scion. At 18 years of age, she is now a highly capable warrior who can trade blows with giants as long as its a fair fight. Unfortunately, her divine father has drawn the ire of Hera, who has gone out of her way to make Samantha's life a living hell. Through Hera's machinations, Samantha was subdued and captured by a brutish cyclops, who planned to keep her as a personal slave. He bound her in chains that were magically forged specifically for her, making it impossible for Samantha to break free on her own.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, this was the very same cyclops that Cooper had been hunting, and the brand new Scion used his kama to shatter her magically forged shackles. After a pitched battle, they managed to bring down the one eyed giant and his small army of thralls. With their work completed, Samantha became Cooper's mentor once she realized how fresh off the bus he was. Later, Samantha became the defacto leader of their growing band, as she is the most well trained in the ways of being a child of the Gods.<br /> <br /> Samantha carries a roman spatha, which enables her to channel the Justice purview. It also adds +1L, +1 Acc and +1 Def and -1 Speed to the Spatha template. She affectionately refers to this weapon by the name of 'Niki,' which roughly translates to 'victory' in Greek.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rocco Wooten, Scion of Apollo:</b> Serving as public relations manager wasn't the gig Rocco was expecting to find himself in when he discovered his Scion heritage. A 17 year old teen idol with an acting career, Rocco is accustomed to having other people clean up for his own mistakes, not the other way around. But as it stands, Rocco's the only member in the band (aside from Albert) who knows how to work the crowd. So when bashing your enemy over the head isn't a viable solution, Rocco uses his silver tongue and charming good looks to persuade, seduce or outright manipulate others into getting what they need.<br /> <br /> Rocco is the third member to join the band and was recruited during a trip to Hollywood. At the time, Cooper and Samantha were hunting a pair of bouda siblings who were marked for capture on Cooper's bounty list. Rocco proved instrumental in locating, baiting and eventually trapping the shapeshifting duo, for they had been planning to assassinate him. After sending them back to Tartarus where they belonged, Cooper suggested inviting Rocco to join them, which Samantha agreed to do.<br /> <br /> Apollo has granted Rocco with a pair of movie star glasses that allows him to channel the Sun Purview as long as he's wearing them. He also has access to an enchanted screen play which allows him to channel the Prophecy purview when reading through it.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Felicia Booth, Scion of Poseidon:</b> The raw powerhouse of the band, Felicia is the girl they turn to when they aren't concerned about the collateral damage left over from their battles. She is 19 years of age and grew up on a farm in the state of Georgia. Her hobbies include mud wrestling and bull riding, both of which have contributed to making her a tough as nails combatant.<br /> <br /> Felicia was the fourth member to join the band, only agreeing to do so if the others could match her in a competition of skill at her two favorite hobbies. Despite putting up an impressive effort, Samantha was not able to beat Felicia's record on bull riding and was tossed to the ground by the ornery beast. When it came time for the mud wrestle challenge, Samantha just barely managed to get the upper hand thanks to her superior combat experience. Despite one loss and a barely achieved win, Felicia decided their performance was satisfactory enough to earn her respect. She proceeded to join them with the offer of a mud encrusted handshake.<br /> <br /> Originally just a set of work clothes, Felicia's trademark denim overalls have been divinely empowered by Poseidon's blessings, granting her access to both the Earth and the Animal (Cow / Bull) purviews, while adding +2L / +1B to the leather armor's soak template. As the only member of the band with access to an elemental power, Felicia is able to manipulate the environment in ways the rest of her team can not.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Albert Stricker, Scion of Hermes:</b> The youngest member of the band in both age and chronological order. Having just recently turned 14 years old, Albert was living on the streets of Germany, where he taught himself slight of hand parlor tricks in order to con people out of their money. He received his visitation through second hand account, and thus doesn't have a very good relationship with his divine father, whom he feels didn't care enough about his well being to check in on him. It would be a stretch to say that he's an 'expert' on magic, but Albert is more qualified for the position than anybody else on the team.<br /> <br /> Since awakening as a Scion, Albert's street magic has been radically improved to the point where even an experienced mortal can't see through his trickery without supernatural awareness. The first time he met his current band, he managed to rob them blind, prompting a chase scene in which they just barely managed to corner him. After realizing what he was and discovering the fact he was living on the streets, Samantha invited him to join up with them, which Albert hesitantly agreed to.<br /> <br /> In true street magician fashion, Albert carries a pack of playing cards with him at all times. The cards allow him to channel the Magic purview. The cards also possess a unique power that allows Albert to instantly summon them to any location within his line of sight (or that he has a clear, mental image of), allowing him to perform tricks that are impossible for any mundane audiences to figure out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-04-2018, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:51:39-07:00","id":1125640,"title":"","content":"<b>This one didn't take nearly as long.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>The Golden Pyramid:</b> Arch rivals and primary antagonists to The Rising Stars, the band known as The Golden Pyramid mirrors their nemeses by being entirely composed of Scions from the Egyptian pantheon. In contrast to their rivals, most of the band's members have also reached adulthood (or close to it), as opposed to being a bunch of teenagers. While they are not strictly evil, their primary mission is to advance the power of their respective pantheon by any means necessary. They do not seem particularly concerned with who gets caught up in their machinations, believing that at the end of the day, their actions served the greater good.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is no surprise then that The Golden Pyramid maintains a large collection of followers and mentors to aid them in their operations. Indeed, the band appears to have an entire organization centered around helping them achieve their goals. It is for this reason that The Golden Pyramid has yet to be fully stamped out by the other pantheons who've become aggravated by their interference with their plans. In a fair fight, it's possible that other Scions might be able to take them down. But when you've got a bunch of Scions reinforced by a security detail of heavily armed guards with orders of 'shoot to kill', the scales begin to tip to one side over the other.<br /> <br /> Despite being classified as a band, most of their enemies will only encounter 2 or 3 members at a time. This is because at least two within The Golden Pyramid delegate themselves to a more hands off approach to achieving their goals. Kafele and Rosa enter the field only when they have little choice in the matter, and instead prefer to give advice / orders from a safely guarded location. This might change in the future as the band finds itself faced with more serious challenges that compel them to gather their forces together.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Kafele Moghadam, Scion of Osiris:</b> Founder of The Golden Pyramid and its physically oldest member, Kafele is a 46 year old pure blooded Egyptian who handles the band's secret financial expenses, such as the acquisition of soldiers and weapons, the disposing of evidence, and pretty much anything else that you wouldn't want showing up on a legitimate business record. Being an underworld broker has made him stupidly wealthy over the years, but not nearly as much as the investments he made following his visitation.<br /> <br /> Because Kafele rarely takes a hands on approach to battle, even the members of The Golden Pyramid do not know the full depths of Kafele's power. In truth, Kafele is on the verge of Demigod status, if he has not already obtained it. He considers engaging mortals to be little more than petty squabbling, and instead focuses his attentions on more otherwordly threats. In the eyes of the public, Kafele is an entrepreneur who owns a chain of manufactures, shipping companies, private universities and historical museums. The exhibits in said museums are all forged replicates of actual relics, however. The real things have been smuggled back to the Egyptian Overworld for safe keeping.<br /> <br /> Although he doesn't like fighting mortals, Kafele is not completely defenseless. Osiris has bestowed him with a golden ring embedded with a large, ebony stone which allows him to summon a replenishing pack of up to 20 Mummies at will. In addition, he is accompanied at all times by a team of 15 elite mercenaries who offer a more public means of security than reanimating the dead. Finally, when he absolutely has to throw down, he wields a khopesh (Gatekeeper) which allows him to channel the Death and Justice purviews and adds +3 Def to the khopesh template.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Jake Almasi, Scion of Set:</b> fearless archaeologist and head of The Golden Pyramid's acquisitions department. At 30 years old, this half Egyptian immigrant has reached an astonishing level of success in the short time he's been in business. The man is fluent in just about any dead language you can think of, and has traveled all over the world in search of lost or hidden treasures and uncharted landscapes. He is also a teacher at one of Kafele's private universities, which is where he met his partner, Caitlin who now assists him on his field research.<br /> <br /> As a Scion, Jake Almasi plays the role of a villain straight out of likes of Tomb Raider, or Uncharted. He is constantly traveling around the globe with enough guards to constitute a private militia as he explores dangerous ruins and lost civilizations. He is also quite willing to threaten and kill other archaeological teams in order to keep them from getting their hands on the treasure first. Of course, the fact that such crimes occur half way across the world and in the middle of nowhere means that there is little chance of Mr. Almasi being convicted of such allegations.<br /> <br /> With his visitation, Set granted Jake an enchanted machete (the Seeking Sword) which allows him to channel the Guardian purview. It also adds +2L and -2 Speed to the Machete template, which makes it invaluable when exploring dense vegetation. He also has access to 15 grunt level soldiers who personally accompany him during his archaeological travels.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Rosa Page , Scion of Thoth:</b> every band should have its own magician; it's a necessity when you're dealing with supernatural threats from the mythic age of human history. And at 31 years old, Rosa is one of the best in her field of expertise. Raised by one of her father's cults, Rosa is fluent in ancient Egyptian, and has been able to translate many of their spells into modern English. When she's not working for Kafele, Rosa can be found managing a hobby shop, which specifically deals with objects of the occult. The store is protected by special magics, ensuring that ordinary mortals completely ignore its existence, and thus reduces the chance of her merchandise falling into the wrong hands.<br /> <br /> As a member of The Golden Pyramid, Rosa is primarily tasked with addressing the magic related concerns that emerge from time to time. If they need to bypass a ward, subude a monster, decipher a ritual or appraise a relic, she's the one with the know how. Of course, being one of the most valuable members on the team means that Kefele is no more comfortable putting her life in danger than his own, so she is usually contacted via long distance communication unless there is an emergency which requires her to make a personal appearance.<br /> <br /> Since her visitation, Thoth has bestowed his magically inclined daughter with a number of powerful birthrights. The most prominent of which is her hardback copy of the Book of Thoth, which affords her access to the Animal, Earth, Magic and Sky purviews, as well as dissuades thieves by killing one of their loved ones every week until the book is returned to her. But her most favorite birthright is the Benu amulet, which she frequently uses for taking joy rides through the open skies.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Caitlin Stone, Scion of Geb:</b> personal assistant to Jake Almasi, and the fourth member to join The Golden Pyramid. Caitlin is a 21 year old explorer who first met Jake a few years ago before graduating from the university he was teaching at. Upon discovering they both shared a similar heritage to one another, he offered her the chance to work alongside him directly, to which she accepted the offer. Caitlin has been traveling all over the world with him ever since, and their involvement with one another has sparked more than a few rumors as to the status of their relationship.<br /> <br /> Don't let the assistant position fool you, Caitlyn is every bit as capable and determined as Jake is when it comes to upholding the band's ideals. When she's on the job, she's got a personality like granite, having no tolerance for either interference from her enemies, nor incompetence from her allies. It is said that even her own guards are nervous to be around her when she's in a bad mood, as she's been known to shoot people for their stupidity before!<br /> <br /> While working for The Golden Pyramid, Caitlin always carries two relics on her person. The first is a rock climber's pick called Excavator, which allows her to channel the Earth and Health purviews while using the Kama template in battle. The second is a custom made pistol which adds +2 Acc to the Desert Eagle template and never needs to reload. Finally, Caitlin is usually accompanied by a personal security team who are equivalent to 10 grunt soldiers whenever she goes exploring.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Isaac Mercer , Scion of Sobek:</b> a former member of the U.S army, Isaac now serves The Golden Pyramid as their chief of security. At 26 years old, he was recruited into the band shortly after his second tour of duty had ended. It is not known how Kafele discovered Isaac's heritage, much less his existence, but the most likely reason is the gods themselves told him to seek Isaac out. Isaac received his visitation while serving over seas in the middle east. It was during this experience that he decided not to enlist for a third tour so that he could reevaluate his life.<br /> <br /> Since joining The Golden Pyramid, Isaac has become their strongman. When they need muscle power to solve a problem, he's the guy they turn to. He's served in two tours on the army's front lines and has more direct combat training than anyone else in the group. Unfortunately, he's not much good at anything else, when you consider the rest of the band is composed of intellectuals and history buffs. Such an environment might frustrate a normal man, but Isaac is accustomed to following orders, so he sets his personal feelings aside for the sake of the mission.<br /> <br /> As a militant Scion, Isaac Mercer wields two prominent birthrights. The first is his beloved AK-47, which adds +2 Acc, -3 Speed to the standard template. The second is his Beretta sidearm, which allows him to channel the Animal (elephant) and Water purviews, as well as never runs out of ammo. Finally, Isaac leads a full regiment of 20 grunt soldiers that he can deploy in strategical operations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-16-2017, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T11:17:30-07:00","id":1147830,"title":"","content":"<b>A compassionate Scion of Tyr</b> who works as a physician for disabled veterans, helping them overcome their battlefield injuries.<br /> <br /> <b>A traitorous Scion</b> <b>of Hades</b> who works in the mining industry. The shafts they dig out serve as axis mundi, through which others may escape the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>An ambitious Scion of Sobek</b>, who's not content with serving as a background character in somebody else' Legend. They work extra hard to prove their own worthiness and earn the recognition of those around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-16-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T02:34:56-07:00","id":1154653,"title":"","content":"Still working out the details of this one:<br /> <br /> <b>Max Roman, Scion of Zeus/Jupiter</b>. Inspired by Marvel's Netflix television series and Jackie Estacado from The Darkness. He was the heir to a mafia empire, but turned from their wicked ways; now he fights a war against crime as a super-powered vigilante.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 11-01-2017, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:42:49-07:00","id":1154724,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea I've been toying with for a while. Who knows, it might actually be playable in 2E!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A selkie</b> who puts together a team of monsters under the patronage of the Titans, hoping that with the blessings of their masters, they stand a better chance against the children of the Gods.<br /> <br /> <b>A vampire</b> who is understandably angry with the Gods for waving her embrace off as an 'acceptable casualty' in order for their Scions to lure out and slay her powerful sire.<br /> <br /> <b>A cyclops </b>who voluntarily underwent the transformation process, hoping life as a mythical creature would allow them to act as a proper rival to the accomplishments of their Scion half-sibling.<br /> <br /> <b>A kitsune</b> who's trickery has been cultivated into an art form. They are especially passionate when it comes to deceiving the Gods and their children, viewing such manipulative works as part of their 'masterpiece' performance.<br /> <br /> <b>A satyr</b> who claims to be the charming face man that allows his band to operate in public. Honestly, though, he's just tagging along for the ride, and views the rest of his band's activities as a source of great amusement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:15:46-07:00","id":1155830,"title":"","content":"I've been pondering the idea of a Masked Mexican Luchador of Aztec decent who battles vampires, killer robots and Satan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:43:47-07:00","id":1155864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1155830#post1155830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been pondering the idea of a Masked Mexican Luchador of Aztec decent who battles vampires, killer robots and Satan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their mask is a relic that ensures any kind of divination that tries to reveal the character's name only comes back as their Luchador identity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who is La Monta\u00f1a?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;La Monta\u00f1a is La Monta\u00f1a.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Useless ass bones!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T15:18:37-07:00","id":1155873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1155864#post1155864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their mask is a relic that ensures any kind of divination that tries to reveal the character's name only comes back as their Luchador identity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who is La Monta\u00f1a?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;La Monta\u00f1a is La Monta\u00f1a.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Useless ass bones!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Luchador Rules:</b> You want to know who's under the mask? You gotta beat them in a match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T15:23:49-08:00","id":1156811,"title":"","content":"I admit I was always a little disappointed that first edition Scion didn't follow the same template as White Wolf's original WoD games, with each pantheon getting it's own big sourcebook covering anything and everything about them, such as Mexican wrestling for the Aztecs, blues folklore for the Loa, and so on. The Aztecs could get a lot of mileage out of luchador masks, Mexican style tattoo art, Catholic synchronism, telenovelas, and the like. <br /> <br /> Now I'm pondering an actress aspiring to be the goddess of telenovelas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That and some sort of Fast &amp; Furious style muscle car that runs off of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T16:10:05-08:00","id":1156827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1156811#post1156811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I was always a little disappointed that first edition Scion didn't follow the same template as White Wolf's original WoD games, with each pantheon getting it's own big sourcebook covering anything and everything about them, such as Mexican wrestling for the Aztecs, blues folklore for the Loa, and so on. The Aztecs could get a lot of mileage out of luchador masks, Mexican style tattoo art, Catholic synchronism, telenovelas, and the like.<br /> <br /> Now I'm pondering an actress aspiring to be the goddess of telenovelas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That and some sort of Fast &amp; Furious style muscle car that runs off of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was kind of relieved they went that route, actually. One reason I decided to buy V20 is so I don't have to buy like 50 other books just to play the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But it is true that I know very little about most of the playable pantheons, so I feel pressured into playing Greek Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:36:49-08:00","id":1177461,"title":"","content":"(Holy Thread Necro, Batman!)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i>People come to clubs to get away from the outside. From their lives, from their troubles.<br /> <br /> I work to help them with this. They call me DJ Ember, and not to toot my own horn, I'm pretty damn good. I keep the beats pumping, the dancers moving, make sure that there's enough water for those who need to take care of themselves... They're my crowd and fans. I need them, they need me.<br /> <br /> But SOME people don't play by the rules. People getting rowdy on the dance floor, people getting grabby, people starting fights... THAT isn't something that flies in my clubs. We have bouncers for that, thankfully.<br /> <br /> But sometimes, it gets even worse. Sometimes creatures that many people like to pretend don't exist slip in. If they come to dance, I leave them be. Music is for everyone, after all.<br /> <br /> But if any of them want to try and make victims out of the people here? That's when things get messy. And I'm not a girl who's afraid of getting her hands dirty.<br /> <br /> My name is Ash, Scion of Xiochipilli. The club is my sanctuary and my temple. And its patrons are under <b>my</b> protection.</i><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So yeah, Ash is a Scion of Xiochipilli... And a DJ. Obviously her Innate Purview is Artistry (Music), and I <i>believe</i> her Callings would be Guardian, Trickster, and Liminal. Though Trickster may be replaced with Lover, I'll have to see when the books come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T01:03:04-08:00","id":1178011,"title":"","content":"A genderfluid child of Loki aiming for more the god/dess of stories in current Marvel, hoping to go heavily into wyrd. Drawing on some of the old myths where if a woman left her husband and children it was assumed to be Loki in disguise, so my dad is basically Greg Universe. Aiming to be a god/dess of bards and witches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T09:30:21-08:00","id":1178090,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">a quiet and restless Sailor born and carved out from the SeaSalt (made by Njord probably). Looking out for &quot;THE ISLAND&quot; he heard from stories and legends</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I would love having a boat as birthright</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And an anchor.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T14:08:57-08:00","id":1178187,"title":"","content":"I'd like some help with my concept, actually! The loose idea is to create a son of Sekhmet who, very eventually, becomes the god Maahes. Maahes was a real god worshipped in Egypt, specifically in the cult center of Leontopolis. He was considered a son of Sekhmet, and considered the god of knives, Killers, deserts, and of the wind. Basically, purview wise, he's Sekhmet + Sky.<br /> <br /> The first thing I need to figure out is whether to make him an incarnation, or to do what Scion Ragnarok did and say that while Maahes exists conceptually in real history, he's new to the World as an actual God, and this is how his story starts (as Ragnarok did with Hermod and Vali).<br /> <br /> The other debate I'm having is that, while I really like the idea of his power set being Sekhmet but also with wind, I recently saw pictures of a rare melanistic, IE totally black lion, and now my brain is filled with an alternative power set more inspired by the likes of Amun such as Sky, Darkness, and Stars. I'm also imagining a bunch of really cool divine epithets such as The Lion of Night (thanks, GRRM), He Whose Mane is the Stars, and The Lord of Knives. That last one is historical to the real Maahes by the way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Son of Sekhmet, but I can't figure out what power set. Please help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","user":"Karasu-sama","date":".  Edit: spelling. 01-23-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:03:55-08:00","id":1178543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1156811#post1156811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I was always a little disappointed that first edition Scion didn't follow the same template as White Wolf's original WoD games, with each pantheon getting it's own big sourcebook covering anything and everything about them, such as Mexican wrestling for the Aztecs, blues folklore for the Loa, and so on. The Aztecs could get a lot of mileage out of luchador masks, Mexican style tattoo art, Catholic synchronism, telenovelas, and the like.<br /> <br /> Now I'm pondering an actress aspiring to be the goddess of telenovelas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That and some sort of Fast &amp; Furious style muscle car that runs off of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> You know I was kind of thinking the same thing myself. As there are plenty of other gods and goddesses in all the pantheons that were unused. It would have also allowed them the ability to correct many of the mistakes they made with the original Scion books. Though in a way they did kind of make individual books and such with the Yatzata and the Gaelic Pantheons and such but yeah a more complete full book detailing everything would have really fleshed them out more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T04:06:37-08:00","id":1178718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karasu-sama</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1178187#post1178187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some help with my concept, actually! The loose idea is to create a son of Sekhmet who, very eventually, becomes the god Maahes. Maahes was a real god worshipped in Egypt, specifically in the cult center of Leontopolis. He was considered a son of Sekhmet, and considered the god of knives, Killers, deserts, and of the wind. Basically, purview wise, he's Sekhmet + Sky.<br /> <br /> The first thing I need to figure out is whether to make him an incarnation, or to do what Scion Ragnarok did and say that while Maahes exists conceptually in real history, he's new to the World as an actual God, and this is how his story starts (as Ragnarok did with Hermod and Vali).<br /> <br /> The other debate I'm having is that, while I really like the idea of his power set being Sekhmet but also with wind, I recently saw pictures of a rare melanistic, IE totally black lion, and now my brain is filled with an alternative power set more inspired by the likes of Amun such as Sky, Darkness, and Stars. I'm also imagining a bunch of really cool divine epithets such as The Lion of Night (thanks, GRRM), He Whose Mane is the Stars, and The Lord of Knives. That last one is historical to the real Maahes by the way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Son of Sekhmet, but I can't figure out what power set. Please help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmmm...<br /> So, Sekhmet but inverted?<br /> She is the sun's scorching fire, he is the cool starry sky.<br /> She is straightforward and personal violence, he is the hidden blade in the dark?<br /> She is driven and full of purpose, he is mercurial and unpredictable?<br /> Would be an interesting approach.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:36:45-08:00","id":1179923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=998593#post998593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope they accurately capture the nuance of the different pantheons (that is to say, 'races' of god) within Norse Mythology, instead of just having everyone be on team Aesir.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a problem I had with 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, it's happened again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:07:33-08:00","id":1179931,"title":"","content":"My idea currently is to have Hades place the heart of one of Persephone's lost children in the corpse a dead man so that they both may have a &quot;son&quot; together. He would be a vagabond doctor who travels the world helping any who need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T18:46:24-08:00","id":1181884,"title":"","content":"I have a few ideas:<br /> <br /> A Theoi Scion who is fed up with the Theoi's fixation on the perfect body and wants some love paid to the perfect brain. After all, Greece and Rome birthed philosophy in the West, and &quot;psi&quot; is often used for the mind and it's &quot;hidden potential,&quot; so why not a patron of philosophers and thinkers? For his Callings, I'm thinking Sage, Creator, and Judge. Possibly some epic Dexterity, because there should be no mind/body seperation, but what other purviews? <br /> <br /> Or, instead of the Ideal Mind, we could have a deity representing the Real Mind. I;m thinking for him/her, we go with Trickster, Lover, and Creator. This is the mind as seen by ancient peoples: tricky, impulsive, and sometimes a source of wonder and horror. <br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, Purviews contain their opposites, right? so the Beauty Purview can also give up ugliness and frightening? Or Prosperity can take prosperity away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T07:11:29-08:00","id":1182253,"title":"","content":"This is kind of a question rather than an answer but it's related to this topic so I figured that folks looking here as well as the origonal poster might be able to answer this for me. This is under the assumption that any of you might be backers and have the print only version already. <br /> <br /> What is the difference between your Concept and your Role Path? They read as the same thing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T07:21:29-08:00","id":1182256,"title":"","content":"Weird, I posted but it didn't go through. I'll try this again. This isn't really a reply to the post but a question the Origonal Poster, someone reading, or even one of the Dev's can answer [I'm assuming that at least a few of you are 2.0 Backers and have read it]. <br /> <br /> What is the difference between your Concept, and your Role Path? I've read them and they both seem like they're the same thing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T07:48:43-08:00","id":1182262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1182256#post1182256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird, I posted but it didn't go through. I'll try this again. This isn't really a reply to the post but a question the Origonal Poster, someone reading, or even one of the Dev's can answer [I'm assuming that at least a few of you are 2.0 Backers and have read it].<br /> <br /> What is the difference between your Concept, and your Role Path? I've read them and they both seem like they're the same thing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Role / Path is what Concepts where originally supposed to be in 1st edition, but they didn't come off as fluidly. You ended up with characters who's concept was &quot;used car salesman,&quot; Which was good for telling about your character's past, but didn't really paint a picture of what kind of deity or legend that character would eventually grow up to become.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Fenris who struggles against his titan heritage, desperately chaining the beast within himself, just as the gods have chained his father.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Prometheus who was sculpted from molten bronze. His flawless, shiny body serves as an inspiration to those mortals who gaze upon him.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Gaia who was born during an earthquake that destroyed a sizable chunk of their home city. As they grow up, they become recognized as an omen (or perhaps a beacon) for natural disasters about to occur!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-04-2018, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T11:03:22-08:00","id":1182318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1182262#post1182262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Role / Path is what Concepts where originally supposed to be in 1st edition, but they didn't come off as fluidly. You ended up with characters who's concept was &quot;used car salesman,&quot; Which was good for telling about your character's past, but didn't really paint a picture of what kind of deity or legend that character would eventually grow up to become.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Fenris who struggles against his titan heritage, desperately chaining the beast within himself, just as the gods have chained his father.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Prometheus who was sculpted from molten bronze. His flawless, shiny body serves as an inspiration to those mortals who gaze upon him.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Gaia who was born during an earthquake that destroyed a sizable chunk of their home city. As they grow up, they become recognized as an omen (or perhaps a beacon) for natural disasters about to occur!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So than basically than that'd be a yes Paths and Concept are essentially the same thing, but with the perks of getting skills out of the Paths. I was curious about that since they start by asking you your concept, but than they go into paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T11:08:07-08:00","id":1182321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1182318#post1182318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So than basically than that'd be a yes Paths and Concept are essentially the same thing, but with the perks of getting skills out of the Paths. I was curious about that since they start by asking you your concept, but than they go into paths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kind of, I guess. Your concept is what kind of character you have in mind, while your role / path details how you go about fulfilling that concept. A squad leader can be played very differently, depending on if they follow the path of the Warrior, or the Trickster, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:27:23-08:00","id":1182389,"title":"","content":"Ah okay I got'cha. Concept is basically what it's always been. Path's are the how they got there and how they go about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T05:34:12-08:00","id":1182558,"title":"","content":"My concept is a woman who was carved from a protective boulder that had lined Wall Street in NYC. Workers there kept running into it and cursing it during Occupy Wall Street and it was eventually removed, and Sun Wukong carved her from said boulder. Now she's a leftist podcaster and Black Bloc member of Antifa. Her calling is Warrior and is tough like the rock she was carved from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T19:29:50-08:00","id":1188061,"title":"","content":"A scion of Huitzilopochtli that is wary of his own bloodthirsty nature and potential for violence. <br /> <br /> Pre-visitation: In order to curb his violent tendencies he paradoxically does boxing and focuses on the technical aspect of the sport. In game terms, while his favored approach is Power he will use Finesse as much as he can. On the professional ring he was given the nickname ''Hummingbird'' for his fancy footwork. But when he loses his composure or he is pushed against a wall, he reverts to his more naturally brutal approach. <br /> <br /> Unbeknownst to him, his father is manipulating things so that he faces ever more difficult fights that forces him to push beyond the techniques he strives to keep. His father will go as far as empowering (divinely) subtly his son's opponents. <br /> At some point, he will accidently kill an opponents and he will subsequently receive his visitation where his father tells him he is unsuited for the sports and should focus on being his warrior. <br /> <br /> My problem here is that i can't think of a name. It might be silly but i absolutely love the ... fateful? names given to character in scion. Like Horace scion of Horus or Eric Donner scion of Thor (also known as Donar i think). Sadly my knowledge of spanish, mexican culture or aztec mythology isn't good enough to think of an interesting name. <br /> The only idea i've had is the nickname Hummingbird (which is one of the purview of Huitzilopochtli)<br /> Anyway, any help will be appreciated. <br /> thx <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T12:58:14-08:00","id":1189985,"title":"","content":"To Maitrecorbo:<br /> You might like &quot;Jos\u00e9 Matadivine&quot; if you're looking for spanish<br /> &quot;Jos\u00e9&quot; Simply means &quot;God will give&quot;<br /> while &quot;Matadivine&quot; is a fictional surname in the family of Matajud\u00edos, \u2018Jew slayer\u2019, and Matamoros 'Moor-Slayer&quot;. In this case being &quot;Divine Slayer&quot;, though more realistically the whole name probably translates to &quot;God gives us a divine warrior&quot; or &quot;God will give us a titan slayer&quot;<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <b>Juliet Cabberin</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent:</b> Loki<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Perfectionist<br /> <b>Calling:</b> Cutthroat criminal prosecution lawyer<br /> Juliet doesn't care about the war between the titans and the gods. She doesn't care for her fathers plans. The only reason she does not renounce the pathetic excuse for a god? The power she can drain from him help her achieve her own goals.<br /> <br /> Juliet is the kind of lawyer that can argue circles around her opponent and the entire courtroom. Unravelling loopholes and revealing withheld information with the fastest and most intense line of questioning one is likely to see in their lifetimes.<br /> <br /> So dedicated is she to her work that even out of the courtroom, she continues to pour over legal texts and analyse cases past and present, looking for the slightest issue or concealment. The only person she ever found any human comfort in was a repeat expert witness she called on for many cases over the course of her career. He was a local computer engineer professor who was able to see through and explain any and every digital forgery or attempt at concealment of computer files she presented him with. Sadly however, he passed away in a car crash not long after their only night of actual intimacy, leaving her with the unluckiest and most unfortunate of outcomes; a child.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ryan Cabberin</b><br /> <b>Divine Parent:</b> Hephaestus<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Pedagogue<br /> <b>Calling</b>: Teacher<br /> Ryan's Father is Hephaestus, who intentionally orchestrated the situation leading to his birth, as an experiment in the mixing of two pantheon heritages.<br /> <br /> Imagine if the 6'7&quot; 310lb football coach had a masters degree in both Mechanical and Electrical engineering, and a Bachelors in Chemical Engineering.<br /> <br /> What Ryan loves most about teaching, is helping kids find a way to connect what they're learning, to what they love. He's become adept at reading students and helping them find something they're passionate about even if they didn't realise it themselves.<br /> <br /> Should he manage to ascend to godhood, Ryan is destined to become the god of Passion and Obsession. He could help you realise and enhance your dreams, or punish you by turning your passion into an all consuming, life destroying, obsession.<br /> <br /> Ryan has two Birthrights: Newtonemesis(A trenchcoat based on the bulletproof vest template with +2L/+2B and access to Fire and Earth Purviews) and The Font of Inspiration(A pen with access to the Arete purview and the first boon of the Health purview)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23957,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman","user":"AtlasSniperman","date":". 02-28-2018, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman","name":"AtlasSniperman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T21:38:00-08:00","id":1190561,"title":"","content":"<b>Astrid Thurston, Scion of Thor</b><br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Astrid Thurston is a travelling twenty-something punk rock musician (she prefers skald). Barely out of her teens, she comes from a small town in Norway that she\u2019d like to forget about. When she was younger, she repeatedly run away from said town whenever things got heated with her mother, who would constantly berate her for being too much like her absentee father. Consequently, her biggest role models growing up were her friends in similar domestic situations and the burned-out rockers that she would see performing in bars whenever she runaway. The cycle of running away and crashing with friends only to come back for one reason or another finally came to an end when her mother and her new husband died in a car accident during a thunderstorm. Filled with grief and guilt over not being able to resolve her differences with her mother, Astrid purposely got into a tavern brawl that quickly went too far. Actually surviving that encounter, and &quot;adopting&quot; her half-brother soon after, has given her new lease on life and a desire to finally find her long-lost father.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: A tall, fit twenty-something with bright red hair, freckles, and even brighter blue eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Divine Parent</b>: Thor (Aesir)<br /> <b>Concept</b>: Rebel Without a Cause<br /> <b>Calling</b>: Guardian or Warrior<br /> <br /> <b>Paths</b><br /> <b>Origin</b>: Angsty Runaway \u2013 Astrid ran away from home several times growing up and knows how to survive on the streets, and on the road, and keep her dignity intact. (Close Combat, Integrity, Subterfuge)<br /> <b>Role</b>: Wandering Punk Rock Skald \u2013 Astrid has always had a talent for playing the electric guitar and has used it to make ends meet on the road. (Culture, Persuasion, Pilot)<br /> <b>Pantheon</b>: Daughter of Thor (Supernatural) \u2013 Astrid knows her father was not like most people. That he was someone thing, like her. She knows it\u2019s her destiny to meet him one day. (Athletics, Close Combat, Occult)<br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Athletics 2, Culture 4 (Music), Close Combat 5 (Baseball Bats), Integrity 3 (Bucking Authority), Occult 2, Persuasion 4 (Making Friends), Pilot 4 (Driving), Subterfuge 3 (Streetwise)<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intellect 3, Might 4, Presence 5; Cunning 2, Dexterity 3, Manipulation 2; Resolve 2, Stamina 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Knacks</b>: The Biggest Target, Close the Gap, Death by Teacup<br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b>: Uses trusty aluminum baseball for when the barflies get to handsy and use a reliable motorcycle for the road. Has a six year old brother she\u2019s basically illegally adopted. Social Services isn\u2019t happy about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 06-05-2018, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:04:42-07:00","id":1198632,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alex Martin: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Male scion of Ullr. Emotionally cold and extremely blunt in conversation. Catholic, raised in St. Michael's Orphanage in Washington State, after being moved around in the system all his life, his mother being murdered during childbirth, and him being blinded, both by a mysterious, unknown entity. He was adopted by the nun there, and she is the closest person to a mother Alex has ever had. Likes to read (uses Epic Perception to read normal books like braille), and listens to classical music. Keeps to self mostly. Has Heart of Ymir (see Birthright Compendium) in chest, after Ullr put it in place of heart removed during Aztec sacrifice, leading Alex to thrive in the cold, both physical and emotional, often to the sadness of those around him. It would take quite the special woman to warm the chilled blood of the Guidless Orion. Has enhanced Perception knacks due to blindness, keeps full extent of abilities secret.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24027-r_pon217","name":"R_Pon217","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24027_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:00:28-07:00","id":1199074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1182262#post1182262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> A Scion of Fenris who struggles against his titan heritage, desperately chaining the beast within himself, just as the gods have chained his father.<br /> <br /> A Scion of Prometheus who was sculpted from molten bronze. His flawless, shiny body serves as an inspiration to those mortals who gaze upon him.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Gaia who was born during an earthquake that destroyed a sizable chunk of their home city. As they grow up, they become recognized as an omen (or perhaps a beacon) for natural disasters about to occur!</div> </div> </div> </div>Love it...I've always favored the &quot;Old Gods.&quot; Have a scion of Nyx I'm working on that's annoyed at how the idea of &quot;shadow&quot; is always seen as &quot;darkness.&quot; (<i>&quot;It can be full of stars.&quot;</i>) <br /> But then I prefer &quot;elements&quot; that make up a general symbol the character in a way. Like the above character representing &quot;Day and Night&quot; replacing Sun, Fire, Darkness, Stars, and Moon. He would also have liminal, journeys, epic dexterity, and chaos.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:41:22-07:00","id":1199090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1199074#post1199074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love it...I've always favored the &quot;Old Gods.&quot; Have a scion of Nyx I'm working on that's annoyed at how the idea of &quot;shadow&quot; is always seen as &quot;darkness.&quot; (<i>&quot;It can be full of stars.&quot;</i>)<br /> But then I prefer &quot;elements&quot; that make up a general symbol the character in a way. Like the above character representing &quot;Day and Night&quot; replacing Sun, Fire, Darkness, Stars, and Moon. He would also have liminal, journeys, epic dexterity, and chaos.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I too love the idea of playing as non human characters, which is something we'll actually be able to do in 2nd edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Everyone being supernaturally endowed humans in 1E was disappointing, given the game's setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:21:40-07:00","id":1199103,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a Scion of Hephaestus. General concept is to be a rebuilder, focusing on repairing things and improving them. <br /> He'll be a bit of a perfectionist and a bleeding heart but just wants to see how far we can go. Strong relies on use of reverse engineering to expand their understanding of things, hasn't had too much chance to dissect humans though so his medical knowledge is mostly theoretical from reading textbooks or hard to translate to people. <br /> <br /> Since he's from the greek pantheon for flavour I'm thinking of having Metamorphosis passively assist him when he uses knacks or boons.<br /> When he uses the Innate Toolkit ability that's because his body morphs to act as those tools, if he uses the Adamant body boon his body will literally look like it turned into adamant. It won't have gameplay effects but I'm basically thinking of my character basically being like a cross between Inspector Gadget and the T-1000 in how they shift their body to do all these things. I suppose that would be a good flavour for any greek cyborgs or automaton characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T08:11:40-07:00","id":1199378,"title":"","content":"I hope to God I got the Japanese translation right on this...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Iti-Man Suiden no Bushi</u></b><br /> <b>Background: </b>Iti-Man Suiden no Bushi (the \u201cWarrior of 10,000 Rice Paddies) was created for his purpose by Inari Okami themselves. They said that they came upon a golden stalk of rice and, finding it beautiful, decided to make a man from it. Because the stalk proved hard to cut, they decided the man\u2019s duty would be to defend the farmers and fields of Japan (and the World) from the monsters and Titanspawn that were appearing in greater numbers. With no other name than the title granted him, the magical farmer\u2019s hat that Inari granted him, Iti-Man set about his duty faithfully. Shortly thereafter, he was trained in combat by a Tengu warrior and gained the companionship of one of Inari\u2019s kitsune devotees.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Iti-Man appears as a tall, thin Japanese man who dresses in traditional traveler\u2019s clothing. His face seems generic and non-descript, like the flavor of a plain rice-cake. He has a dry sense of humor which appears often, but he occasionally finds mortal (and Scion) social interaction a little confusing, which makes him appreciative of Midori\u2019s (his kitsune follower) help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24048-inari_okami","name":"Inari_Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24048_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T10:10:13-07:00","id":1199406,"title":"","content":"Speaking of non-human characters, this idea was inspired by popular stories like Redwall, Secret of Nimh and other tales that involve sentient animals living in the wilds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Any Appropriate Nature Deity:</b> Feeling particularly whimsical one day, they decide to bestow their Scion potential upon a simple field mouse. With the might of heroes now coursing through them, the mouse embarks on an epic journey through the wilderness, eventually becoming a celebrated figure among the beasts of the forest. Their (mortal) journey eventually leads to them establishing a woodland kingdom rarely seen by human eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T10:53:50-07:00","id":1199420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1199406#post1199406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of non-human characters, this idea was inspired by popular stories like Redwall, Secret of Nimh and other tales that involve sentient animals living in the wilds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Any Appropriate Nature Deity:</b> Feeling particularly whimsical one day, they decide to bestow their Scion potential upon a simple field mouse. With the might of heroes now coursing through them, the mouse embarks on an epic journey through the wilderness, eventually becoming a celebrated figure among the beasts of the forest. Their (mortal) journey eventually leads to them establishing a woodland kingdom rarely seen by human eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice. two things i'm thinking<br /> 1) i dont think one should be limited to nature deity. You could have, for example, a white bunny chosen of Ares.<br /> and<br /> 2) i realized that with the concept of scales you dont even need to adjust the attribute of the mouse. I'm really liking the system more and more.<br /> <br /> But yeah, i really like that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T11:22:31-07:00","id":1199430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1199420#post1199420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) i dont think one should be limited to nature deity. You could have, for example, a white bunny chosen of Ares.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Zeus:</b> So... are you going through like... a phase or something?<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> It's not a phase, Dad!<br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> So you, the God of War, decided to bestow divine power upon a weak, cuddly bunny?<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> I have my reasons, okay?<br /> <br /> <b>Aphrodite:</b> When I asked you for a pet rabbit, this isn't what I had in mind...<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> Well it's done now, so take it or leave it!<br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> Oh no you don't. You created this Scion, so you take responsibility for it!<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> Oh that is rich, coming from you!<br /> <br /> *Ares is smacked off the peak of Mount Olympus...*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T11:49:45-07:00","id":1199435,"title":"","content":"Oh, I can see it\u2026<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/sluggy/images/0/0a/Bunbun.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T13:08:48-07:00","id":1199457,"title":"","content":"The aformentioned Bunny Scion of Ares eventually joined Arthurian Myth. He is an existence between Titan and God among their eyes. <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XcxKIJTb3Hg\" data-code=\"XcxKIJTb3Hg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XcxKIJTb3Hg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> After reading some parts on the souls I'm imagining playing a character on spiritual journey trying to expand his existence. Going to various temples of various faiths and trying to find the pieces of his soul that correspond to each faith. He'd find the 5 pieces as described by the Netjer, the 4 described by the Orisha, find his own personal Manitou spirit, find his own personal Kami, discover his Hun and Po and keep going from there. <br /> If it gave them access to power it would be minor but it's more for the experience of discovering various parts of themselves and understanding how different cultures treat souls on a person level. Trying to find their place in a world of so many myths blended together.<br /> <br /> Then again I'm a sucker for hybrids or mixing things, I'd probably try to make a character that was part everything if I could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T13:44:50-07:00","id":1199463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1199430#post1199430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> So... are you going through like... a phase or something?<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> It's not a phase, Dad!<br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> So you, the God of War, decided to bestow divine power upon a weak, cuddly bunny?<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> I have my reasons, okay!<br /> <br /> <b>Aphrodite:</b> When I asked you for a pet rabbit, this isn't what I had in mind...<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> Well it's done now, so take it or leave it!<br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> Oh no you don't. You created this Scion, so you take responsibility for it!<br /> <br /> <b>Ares:</b> Oh that is rich, coming from you!<br /> <br /> *Ares is smacked off the peak of Mount Olympus...*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the pet farm<br /> <br /> <b>Child : </b> Mommy, mommy look a fwuffy bunny!<br /> <br /> <b>Ares : </b> Fool, i am no such thing as 'fwuffy'. I am mighty Ares the god of War. I am the Bloody Sword, the Pillager and the Crusher of armies. I am unstoppable. I ...<br /> <br /> <b>Child : </b>He is so pretty and his fur is white so i'ma call him Snowy.<br /> <br /> <b>Ares :</b> Grrrrrrraaaaaahhhhhhh !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T18:55:49-07:00","id":1199562,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><i><b>Time for some Companions!</b></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mr. Buttons:</b> A living teddy bear with retractable claws and fangs. They were created to protect young Scions from monsters long enough for them to reach maturity. After which, they are normally handed off to a new ward in need of their protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beefcake:</b> An enslaved minotaur who was claimed on the battlefield after being defeated by their Scion master. As a constant reminder of their station, their master's personal insignia was burned into their flesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Deep Cut:</b> A sentient sword with the power of speech. When unsheathed in battle, it regales those within earshot by performing heavy metal ballads.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nova:</b> A forest nymph who disguises herself as the leader of a hippie commune. She may be convinced to lend her services as a mentor for Scions who possess a strong connection with the natural world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cory Wright:</b> A young vampire who struggles to keep their monstrous nature under control and retain some resemblance of a normal life. Scions connected to the Death or Darkness purviews may attract them enough to become a follower, as well as a potential love interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2018, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:48:04-07:00","id":1200216,"title":"","content":"<i><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Time For Some Antagonists!</span></span></b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A failed Scion who's patron withdrew their support after a humiliating defeat at the hands of their enemy. Since then, they've harbored a grudge against all other Scions who are sponsored by the same patron, and have made it their life's mission to stand in the way of their path to apotheosis.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Scion of a pantheon's chief deity who gradually becomes mad with power. Believing themselves to be of higher status than even their fellow Scions, they abuse their divine gifts to establish their own militant country, which seeks to conquer the rest of the mortal World.<br /> <br /> <br /> A former best friend who blames you for the death of their loved ones after your enemies attacked them in an effort to get to you. The fact you kept your true nature a secret from them probably didn't help alleviate the tension between the two of you. Now it seems that Fate has conspired to put the two of you on opposite sides of the war, as the once ordinary mortal starts amassing a Legend of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T10:57:26-07:00","id":1200487,"title":"","content":"Do we count monster concepts?<br /> <br /> Since any animal that is aggressive, territorial and dangerous can count as Nemean I'm thinking of stacking templates together.<br /> I'm imagining it as a Nemean Hydra. Sure they are vulnerable to fire but they'd have the Nemean durability on top of Hydra healing to help them.<br /> What makes this Hydra stand out upon first sight is the fact that it only possesses one head as their mother wasn't capable of biting fully through their Nemean skin when it was a child.<br /> <br /> Some may think of it as cheap but I'd think of it as a challenge to be able to hit a creature hard enough and fast enough to kill it before it gets better. It doesn't have as many heads and can't focus on too many adversaries at once but at that point one head is enough.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T11:51:49-07:00","id":1200506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1200487#post1200487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we count monster concepts?<br /> <br /> Since any animal that is aggressive, territorial and dangerous can count as Nemean I'm thinking of stacking templates together.<br /> I'm imagining it as a Nemean Hydra. Sure they are vulnerable to fire but they'd have the Nemean durability on top of Hydra healing to help them.<br /> What makes this Hydra stand out upon first sight is the fact that it only possesses one head as their mother wasn't capable of biting fully through their Nemean skin when it was a child.<br /> <br /> Some may think of it as cheap but I'd think of it as a challenge to be able to hit a creature hard enough and fast enough to kill it before it gets better. It doesn't have as many heads and can't focus on too many adversaries at once but at that point one head is enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the Story Hooks section, I thought up a Typhonic Megladon. So it was basically 100 times bigger than your normal version of <i>whale eating shark. </i>and had all the benefits of being a typhonic animal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2018, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T13:43:58-07:00","id":1200552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1200506#post1200506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> In the Story Hooks section, I thought up a Typhonic Megladon. So it was basically 100 times bigger than your normal version of <i>whale eating shark. </i>and had all the benefits of being a typhonic animal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now imagining some mad scientist Scion of Gaia just going crazy and stacking creature templates on a creature like a DnD min-maxer/munchkin.<br /> <br /> This also makes me want a God tier Metamorphisis purview Boon that allows one to transform into Kaijus to fight that Typhonic Megalodon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T13:52:44-07:00","id":1200556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1200552#post1200552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm now imagining some mad scientist Scion of Gaia just going crazy and stacking creature templates on a creature like a DnD min-maxer/munchkin.<br /> <br /> This also makes me want a God tier Metamorphisis purview Boon that allows one to transform into Kaijus to fight that Typhonic Megalodon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, 1st edition openly encouraged players to home brew their own Boons. Maybe 2E will do the same?<br /> <br /> But yeah, in a game who's setting is derived from real world mythology, I would be very disappointed if we don't have some means of including colossal fist fights in a crowded city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T23:53:19-07:00","id":1200725,"title":"","content":"That's what Marvels are for :P<br /> <br /> As for my concepts....<br /> <br /> Daughter of Loki, who's personal destiny/wyrd is.... to rule over a kingdom of ashes after Ragnarok has settled. She ain't too happy about that. The World is where all of her favorite things are!<br /> <br /> Most other gods just say to Loki &quot;Not another one...&quot;<br /> <br /> Child soldier from Central Africa, scion of Oduduwa. Brought up in War, the Scion grabbed their destiny when they got fed up by injustice and slew his own warlord. Oduduwa was very proud of his son. Sadly, the scion is trying to adjust to his new life, while trying to get away from war... which Oduduwa does not condone. He chose this Scion so there'll be someone on the Orisha side who can be the warrior when threats come. There's a chance of this guy becoming a War Titan if he doesn't manage to diversify though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:34:31-07:00","id":1200934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1200725#post1200725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Daughter of Loki, who's personal destiny/wyrd is.... to rule over a kingdom of ashes after Ragnarok has settled. She ain't too happy about that. The World is where all of her favorite things are!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mmmaybe the word 'ashes' refers to a forest of ash wood trees?<br /> <br /> In which case, she has her own forest kingdom.<br /> <br /> Oh destiny... always so prone to being misinterpreted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:32:31-07:00","id":1201024,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Greek Hero descended from Apollo who is the world's best looking fitness model, destined to be the God of Physical Perfection, constantly harassed by the fallen Narcissus who is insanely jealous of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T16:13:34-07:00","id":1201037,"title":"","content":"A wanted Scion of Miclntecuhtli, who establishes himself as the leader of a suicide cult, using the mass deaths as sacrifices to empower his father's pantheon. After the deed is done, he moves to a new area and begins rebuilding his followers under a new pseudonym. The government, of course, neither comprehends nor approves of his activities, which is why he is constantly being pursued by Interpol.<br /> <br /> <br /> A rowdy Scion of Odin, who believes that the best way to deal with a threat is to hit it as hard as you can. If that doesn't work, then just keep hitting it until it stops being threatening! Receiving combat training directly from the Valkyries, she has been told many times about the glory that awaits her in Valhalla. As a result, she strides fearlessly into battle, openly inviting her foes to try and kill her.<br /> <br /> <br /> A mischievous Scion of Hades, who revels in being a master thief. With part of his father's portfolio being the God of Wealth, his child believes that anybody who does not properly respect Hades is undeserving of the riches they adorn themselves with. As punishment for their vainglorious behavior, he robs them of their most valuable possessions, reminding them of just by who's grace they were allowed such opulence in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T18:20:15-07:00","id":1201102,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for an antagonist that I've kicked around for a while now. A Scion of Shiva who's kind of an angry extremist. It started with just the officially renounced but still often practiced caste system, which he was born on the low end of, and his method of resolving this issue by targeting people who he sees as enforcing it and executing them in some public way. After one too many such executions (and his habit of using an axe, like some barbarian, and hardly ever a ranged weapon) he got exiled from India, but he's broadened his scope to generally trying to tear down corrupt systems and kill tyrants in whatever form he sees them. He's grown more cunning and more adept at deception over the years, but his plans all end the same way: Lots of blood and fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T19:24:14-07:00","id":1201120,"title":"","content":"Intentionally left the gender unspecified for these character concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A brand new Kitsune, who's quest for godhood takes them across 8 Legendary adventures. At the end of each one, they finds themselves rewarded with an additional tail. Ultimately, their journey culminates in the Kitsune having a total of 9 tails, transcending into a Kyuubi and obtaining godly status.<br /> <br /> <br /> A sympathetic Giant (preferably of Norse mythology), who inherited a bit too much God blood from their ancestral lineage. Realizing that the end of the World threatens their own people as well as the Gods, they hope to bring a more peaceful resolution to the war, thus preventing the catastrophe from ever happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> A fallen Dragon who was bound to human form as punishment for aiding the Titans against their fellow Gods. Their Legend involves a journey of atonement, eventually leading to the restoration of their true form and being accepted back into the divine hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T23:25:21-07:00","id":1201155,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Created Scion of H</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">era designed to hunt down the bastard children of Zeus and terminate them lest one of them </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">fulfill</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> the prophecy and bring about the King of Olympus' demise. Slowly starts to resent its reason for being and attempts to find ways to escape its fate and &quot;soulless&quot; nature.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A shapeshifting Scion of Odin who takes on various identities and names as they go on their Hero's Journey; The reckless hero, the powerful jarl,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> the old mentor, but also the curious witch, caring mother and ancient seeress depending on the situation and who their talking too. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:24:35-07:00","id":1201413,"title":"","content":"I keep wanting to do a Scion of Hades who's a banker/financier, just because I don't think his role as god of wealth gets enough love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:55:25-07:00","id":1201602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1201413#post1201413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep wanting to do a Scion of Hades who's a banker/financier, just because I don't think his role as god of wealth gets enough love.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually had a character in 1st edition for the same thing. Obviously, I leaned heavily on the knacks rather than boons to get it done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24048-inari_okami","name":"Inari_Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24048_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T07:50:39-07:00","id":1201613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1201413#post1201413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep wanting to do a Scion of Hades who's a banker/financier, just because I don't think his role as god of wealth gets enough love.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Check back one page for my previous Hades, related Scion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> These characters were not naturally born Scions, but rather chosen for the role as a reward for meeting other criteria.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> A modern descendant of Chiron, who's chaste and pious life style is virtually unheard of among her fellow Centaurs. Having been pleased by her purity, Artemis chooses to bestow her favor upon her. Under her patron's continued guidance, the young Centaur goes on to become a virgin Goddess of Innocence. Her cultists prefer to live in secluded communities, where they can avoid the coruptive influences of the outside world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> An obsessive historian, who will brave any danger if it leads to uncovering the secrets of the past. Such dedication to studying ancient lore earns him the favor of Thoth, who leads him on the path to becoming a God of Lost Knowledge. If you're looking for some obscure artifact or historical document from a bygone era, then chances are he has the original copy stashed away on his barge somewhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A traveling martial artist, who's fighting style is adapted from techniques he learned while studying under monsters. Impressed by his fearless dedication to the art of combat, he earns the favor of Nezha, who points him in the direction of increasingly more difficult opponents. Ultimately, his training leads to him becoming a demonic God of Battle, who's followers include those who wish to learn more than just 'self defense' techniques.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T08:29:52-07:00","id":1201625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karasu-sama</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1178187#post1178187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some help with my concept, actually! The loose idea is to create a son of Sekhmet who, very eventually, becomes the god Maahes. Maahes was a real god worshipped in Egypt, specifically in the cult center of Leontopolis. He was considered a son of Sekhmet, and considered the god of knives, Killers, deserts, and of the wind. Basically, purview wise, he's Sekhmet + Sky.<br /> <br /> The first thing I need to figure out is whether to make him an incarnation, or to do what Scion Ragnarok did and say that while Maahes exists conceptually in real history, he's new to the World as an actual God, and this is how his story starts (as Ragnarok did with Hermod and Vali).<br /> <br /> The other debate I'm having is that, while I really like the idea of his power set being Sekhmet but also with wind, I recently saw pictures of a rare melanistic, IE totally black lion, and now my brain is filled with an alternative power set more inspired by the likes of Amun such as Sky, Darkness, and Stars. I'm also imagining a bunch of really cool divine epithets such as The Lion of Night (thanks, GRRM), He Whose Mane is the Stars, and The Lord of Knives. That last one is historical to the real Maahes by the way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Son of Sekhmet, but I can't figure out what power set. Please help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a (Divine?) epiphany about trying to build the &quot;dark&quot; version of Maahes blessed by Amun. It occurs to me... that's just Riddick, isn't it? Like, with the knives and the bestial nature and the affinity for the dark and all that? I guess I know where I'm going with the character now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T03:54:34-07:00","id":1201888,"title":"","content":"<b>Why aspire to godhood, when you can become one of their creators?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The loner survivor of a plane crash who was forced to survive in the wilds for three years before they found their way back to civilization. In truth, it was only due to the mercy of Gaia that he managed to survive for as long as he did. To show his appreciation for the merciful bounty she bestowed upon him, he seeks to become a Titan of Fertility, using his powers to reverse the devastation Gods and mortals have caused to the World.<br /> <br /> <br /> A pyromaniac who's condition lead to her accidentally destroying everything of value in her life, including her own family. She would later come to discover herself to be a chosen Scion of Surtur, who's appetite for destruction makes even her own look tame by comparison. With no more attachments to the mortal world holding her back, she begins the journey to becoming a Titan of Fire. Much like the flames she seeks to emulate, she is blessed with a captivating beauty, though often brings disaster to those who let their guard down around her.<br /> <br /> <br /> An an extremely lucky man who was successfully resuscitated after being clinically dead for five minutes. During their short time in the Underworld, they discovered they were actually a child of Hela, who felt this was the best way to have a face to face conversation with him. Although he sustained no physical injuries after his recovery, his mind has become unhinged by what he witnessed on the other side. Now, he's on the path to becoming a Titan of Death and hastening the lives of others towards their inevitable destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T08:09:15-07:00","id":1204185,"title":"","content":"IDK if something like this was mentioned before, but I had an idea to make a Kami Scion of Tsuki-yomi who was directed to become a chef and eventual god of food. T-y is using the scion as an attempt to reconciliate with Amatarasu after his previous dealing with Uke Mochi. I have not developed the idea enough to decide whether the Hero will embrace his purpose or oppose it. But he will make damn good Udon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24048-inari_okami","name":"Inari_Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24048_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:57:10-07:00","id":1204204,"title":"","content":"<b>Time for some 'pure bloods!'</b><br /> <br /> <br /> A bastard child of Aphrodite and Ares who struggles to reconcile their feelings of love and hatred burning within them. In time, their legend involves them becoming the God of Impassioned Violence, delivering swift retribution upon those who bring suffering towards others.<br /> <br /> <br /> A legitimate child of Hephaestus and Aphrodite who's inventions are described as a 'thing of beauty' by those lucky enough to see them. Taking great pride in their handiwork, their legend involves them becoming a God of Craftsmanship, creating works that are not only functional, but aesthetically pleasing as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> A child of Zeus and Hera who has lofty expectations placed upon them by their divine siblings on Mount Olympus. Having inherited a mean streak that would make both his parents give a concerned blink, their legend involves them going on to become the God of Grudges, punishing others in the name of those who feel they have been wronged in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:56:41-07:00","id":1204244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1204204#post1204204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bastard child of Aphrodite and Ares who struggles to reconcile their feelings of love and hatred burning within them. In time, their legend involves them becoming the God of Impassioned Violence, delivering swift retribution upon those who bring suffering towards others.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Maybe I can go ask Inanna/Ishtar/Astarte for pointers&quot; seems like a ready-made shenanigans-creating plot-hook.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Scion: &quot;All right, I have climbed the sacred peak, vanquished the titanspawn, answered the riddles and brought back the relic as you requested. Would you now tell me how one manages to contain both Love and War?&quot;<br /> <br /> Inanna: &quot;Well, for starters, have you tried lots of angry sex?&quot;<br /> <br /> Scion: \u0ca0\ufe4f\u0ca0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 04-07-2018, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T21:53:26-07:00","id":1204428,"title":"","content":"My idea is a Scion of Hephaestus who is the unmaker. Where his father builds anew, the son shatters and destroys. I've got him with Chaos, Death and Forge Purviews but am not sure if there is another he should have to make the character (thinking maybe Epic Strength, but am not sure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:25:01-07:00","id":1209421,"title":"","content":"<b>Possibly my favorite PC:</b><br /> <br /> I once played a scion of a death God that had a set of followers/creatures in the form of zombies tattooed into the skin of his back. He had the ability to summon the zombies at will, but they didn't follow more than the most basic of orders and couldn't distinguish between friend and foe, instead attacking anyone nearby without the Death purview.<br /> In his first quest he vowed to avenge the death of a small Mexican girl, whose ghost followed him throughout the quest. Hilariously, he spoke no Spanish and she didn't know English while she was alive, so all communication was through over-the-top pantomime. He actually did avenge her, destroying the Death cult on the Mexican coast that was brutally sacrificing innocent mortal children, and rather than move to her own Afterlife, she chose to stay at his side, becoming a faithful Fatebound companion.<br /> Most of his life was devoted to avenging the restless dead this way, putting to rest souls and ghosts the world over. He became particularly strong in the Justice and Guardian purviews, which supplemented his Death boons and his Epic Strength and Stamina surprisingly well. His companion, the ghost girl, grew in power along with him, gaining the ability to channel the effects of his Death boons for him, as well as the ability to restrain and even dominate weaker spirits.<br /> He and his band were the most successful my group ever played, and we actually got them to Apotheosis, but stopped there because the system was so broken at that level. My character actually ended up becoming the God of Avenging the Innocent, with maxed out Death, Justice, and Guardian purviews.<br /> <br /> I know this is a full character and not a concept, but I wanted to share, because of the different and unusual ideas and concepts that went into him. I helped my ST with the actual mechanics of most of his powers, so let me know if you're curious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T18:05:13-07:00","id":1209463,"title":"","content":"A common house cat who jumped on top of their owner right as they were about to have their divine potential unlocked. As a result, the power was accidentally transferred to the cat, turning them into an unintentionally chosen Scion. Their owner, of course, is absolutely not pleased at having their destiny stolen from them by a stupid animal, thus vowing to do everything in their power to claim what is rightfully theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T18:59:05-07:00","id":1213263,"title":"","content":"A child of Loki who possess the form of a mighty she-bear. Exhibiting the capacity for human speech, their presence has the Gods concerned as to their part in the time of Ragnarok, if they indeed have one. Unfortunately, Odin has decided that it's probably best to not take any chances, especially considering what her siblings Fenrir and Jormagandr are like. So the All Father decides to have her eliminated before she can grow into her full power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A child of Hercules, who seems to have inherited in stamina what their father possessed in strength. Displaying the toughness to survive even the most galling of challenges over the course of their life, their Legend revolves around becoming recognized as the God of Endurance. At which point, they hold weekly competitions with the residents of Olympus to see who can hold out the longest before exhaustion sets in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A child of Ogoun, who lead a successful revolt against his tribe's warlord, resulting in him being unanimously voted in as its new chief. After their coronation, they soon have their hands full defending their tribe's land from poachers, wild animal attacks, potential new warlords looking to muscle their way into power and the occasional monster who feels like moving into the area.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:55:41-07:00","id":1213287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1199420#post1199420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) i dont think one should be limited to nature deity. You could have, for example, a white bunny chosen of Ares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah so this explains the origins of the Vorpal Bunny. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though on a serious note for this thread. I had a character concept in mind for one for 1e. Yeah I know &quot;Boo! Get off the stage! 1e sucks!&quot; Yeah I don't care.<br /> <br /> My concept was for scion of Izanagi (yeah I know he's not a god anymore blah blah blah once more I don't care) who is meant to end up wandering the Earth as a guardian and warrior in the name of justice, protecting the innocent and writing wrongs done by others. Eventually leading him to becoming known among the Amatsukami as &quot;Wanding God of Justice. A god who wanders the world protecting innocents, punishing the guilty. The idea that when when his sword falls no innocent blood is shed. Yet none who watch the sword fall are ever the same again. They leave changed in one form or another. Either they passed the test and the sword itself passed through them, or they failed the test to one degree or another. For the truly heinous of crimes there is but one punishment, death. Others leave marks on the body. As a warning. A warning that though they escaped death once before on his blade. They had best be careful lest they face the blade a second time and fail. But yet with all this talk of death and blood letting in all honesty he would much rather not. He'd much rather sit, talk and enjoy a cup of tea. Laugh and smile. To play with children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-29-2018, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T04:22:46-07:00","id":1213373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1199406#post1199406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Any Appropriate Nature Deity:</b> Feeling particularly whimsical one day, they decide to bestow their Scion potential upon a simple field mouse. With the might of heroes now coursing through them, the mouse embarks on an epic journey through the wilderness, eventually becoming a celebrated figure among the beasts of the forest. Their (mortal) journey eventually leads to them establishing a woodland kingdom rarely seen by human eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dang it, now I really want to see an entire campaign revolving around Scion animals.<br /> <br /> Redwall is an awesome series!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NsxvQipMdL4\" data-code=\"NsxvQipMdL4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NsxvQipMdL4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T19:12:38-07:00","id":1222566,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here are three competing Gods of the Internet. Each one warring aganist the other to be the sole bearer of the Mantle. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Scion of Lakshmi who is the God of the Internet as a Commodity. The Internet is just another technology, and like all the technologies and innovations that have come before it exists to be a commodity, provided by ISP's and given to the consumers. At a price. Sure people may complain that the Internet, like information, should be free for all to use, but this God knows better. Nothing is free. Everything has a cost and to deny that reality is the height of childishness. Thus, this well-dressed and always professional God of the Internet does its best to provide the best Internet service possible for those willing to pay for it. It's only natural. You don't expect the same quality of food from a fast food place that you would expect from a five star </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">restaurant</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> do you? Of course not. Quality costs money, and in this God's case worship as well. This God is usually male, but is willing to be female if The Chart says people are more comfortable around a female figure. In the end, making people feel more comfortable is the end goal because when they feel like they can trust you than they're far more willing to buy your product and accept your services.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Portfolio: God of the Internet, E-Commerce, Profit, and ISP's.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Scion of Ares who is the God of the Internet as a Weapon. The Internet is a tool, and better yet it is a weapon. The ultimate weapon in the modern day. With it careers can be ruined, movements ignited, lies and truths spread globally and governments toppled. More importantly though, the Internet is a battleground for an endless war. Call it the Culture War if you want, call it trolling, call it flaming, call it whatever, to this God its just plain beautiful. Humans aren't meant to passively accept the Status Quo of the Present. A real human is meant to topple whatever structure they deem unacceptable. Doesn't matter if you replace that structure with something new or something old or something good or something bad. Social Justice, the Dark Enlightment, the Alt-Right, Black Lives Matter, this God doesn't care about the ideology, so as long as its dogmas are used to smash the other side. Punch up, punch down, but whatever you do always keep punching and fighting for what you believe in. Compromise is for the weak. Be pure and never given into the Enemy, to do so is worse than dying. This God demands that you expose the Truth. It doesn't actually matter if you're Truth is actually true, in fact, its better if isn't. People will come to debunk you or shallow your lies and when they meet each in the comments another glorious fight can break out. This God appears in whatever form will best piss off its opponents. Gender fluid or hypermasculine, young or old, black or white, it doesn't matter. So as long as it brings hate and fear into someone's eyes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Portfolio: God of the Internet, Trolling, Hacking, Conspiracies, Fake News and the Culture War.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Scion of Loki who is the God of the Internet as Transformation. The Internet is the liberator of the human spirit. With it there is a new possibility of transformation and enchantment. Virtual reality, argumented reality, cybernetics, AI. While many of these transformations and technologies are just the stuff of science fiction currently the possibility and idea is out there and this God strives for its followers to make them a reality. Any fears of conseqences be damned. Anything is better than being in meatspace and not being able to reshape reality with just your knowledge of coding. This God sees the Internet as the way to transform all of humanity and turn them into something kin to the Gods themselves. Perhaps even something greater. So, it demands that its followers go the extra mile and be the test cases for this upcoming Cyber Age. Resistance is futile. Progressive is coming. So create new VR technologies, support biorobotics research and never be at peace with what Mother Nature left you with. This God is always changing its form. Sometimes masculine, sometimes feminine but usually neither and something completely alien and off the map.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Portfolio: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">God of the Internet, Virtual Reality, Cybernetics, Robotics and the New Flesh. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T15:47:04-07:00","id":1224825,"title":"","content":"<b>A son of Loki and a</b> <b>daughter of Heimdall</b>; they don't like each other very much. Maybe it's because their parents are supposed to kill each other during Ragnarok? Maybe it's because they literally can't be in the same room for more than 5 minutes before one of them inadvertently does something to offend the other? Well, whatever the reason, the two of them have been mortal enemies for as long as they have known each other, and have clashed in battle on a frequent basis. That changed recently, however, when their last confrontation ended up with Heimdall's daughter being 'magically' impregnated, and the son of Loki is confirmed to be the father! Now, the two bitter rivals must work together to raise their child properly, or else the Norns predict it will grow into a powerful Jotun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T00:41:19-07:00","id":1226215,"title":"","content":"Back to the idea of animal themed Scions...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Anansi,</b> who is born with the form of a sentient tarantula. They communicate with humans by weaving messages out of spider silk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Coyote</b> who is born with the form of their father's namesake. Unlike the cunning trickster who spawned them, it seems that Fate has deigned to make this particular canine into the butt of nearly every practical joke that occurs around them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Zeus</b> who is born with the form of a sentient swan, to which even Hera is incapable of suppressing laughter at the situation. That changes, of course, once the swan demonstrates the power to summon lightning bolts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T05:31:23-07:00","id":1237100,"title":"","content":"<b>The Perfect Warrior:</b> in an effort to create what he perceives as his masterpiece, Ares has used his powers to remove his latest chosen's heart and replaced it with a stone made from the crystalization his own divine ichor. The result of this impromptu surgery is a War Scion who is unfettered by petty attachments like human empathy or even a basic moral compass. They are wholly dedicated to the ways of bloodshed and warfare, which pleases Ares greatly, but disturbs and terrifies everybody who gets mixed up with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T19:38:25-07:00","id":1237658,"title":"","content":"My blog currently hosts about 18 character concepts including two scions actively being played, a character made to analyze the creation and advancement in scion (and which I screwed up and need to redo), and 15 theoretical characters in Origin and Hero versions. As with my page of theoretical D&amp;D 5e builds most of the idea is to look into how to build certain character concepts. I should probably go in and add some reasoning and analysis for choices later before I get into high numbers. A lot of these are characters I'd like to build or based on past characters of mine, one character has two variations in her build based on different connected gods. So I suppose that's only 17 concepts in total then.<br /> <br /> A daughter of incarnations of Sif and Thor who is very eager to be a real scion. Daredevil media darling with her own YouTube channel.<br /> <br /> A 18 year old runaway turned tomb raider who has found herself bound to an incarnation of Inari. Said incarnation hasn't noted that they were intrigued by the character because they could tell she was the child of another of Inari's incarnations.<br /> <br /> A child of Benten who was a marine martial arts instructor who turned Japanese cinema stunt coordinator and then actress taken into service by Amaterasu as an agent.<br /> <br /> A Hollywood agent, voice actress, and sometimes actress who looks like a living corpse because the producer of a previous movie she was part of toyed with Netjer magics and got her cursed. Taken on as a scion of Wesir sort of to return balance and justice to her due to the misplaced curse.<br /> <br /> A girl who survived an attack by a demon that killed her grandmother and now can talk to and command animals as well as a purpose to protect humanity and nature from demonic mockeries of life.<br /> <br /> A harpy trying very hard to not be a harpy and get taken on by a kami because &quot;Tengu are cool ninja&quot; attracting the eye of Frigg due to the sheer audacity of trying to get a pantheon to take her up.<br /> <br /> A 19th century vampire dug up and set into the world as part of some sort of mysterious long play strategy by Kali. (mythology of this one is she became a vampire due to having been forgotten by everybody including herself and her killer. which I pulled from a webcomic admittedly, but unconsecrated murder victims I believe are a potential source of vampires)<br /> <br /> A woman from a cult who infiltrates businesses as secretaries and use a combination of espionage and seduction to secure control of the companies and use those resources to fund heroes. Some of the branches have....questionable recruitment practices.<br /> <br /> A Korean-Japanese woman working as a stage magician in Las Vegas who is a child of Susano'o and refers to herself as The Trickster Fox due to using animal-fables in her stage show along with four friends of hers who took on identities as Dog (a police officer), Tiger (a tough), Mouse (a flirt), and Rabbit (a housewife). Unbeknownst to them, the scion does have kitsune blood (though this is a 1e rebuild so that blood never manifested much) and the four friends were all denizens as well (including a fifth Raven girl who just did research and didn't perform).<br /> <br /> A homonculus who wasn't aware that she was one, created by a sorcerer in a fit of grief and guilt after the death of his wife and brought to life by the grace of a merciful god (Ganesha in his Kami guise).<br /> <br /> A gender fluid alligator farmer and scion of sobek who swings from romance to heroism on the drop of a dime.<br /> <br /> An unethical Canadian archeologist who was boasting about her methods of circumventing archeology regulations within earshot of a drunken Egyptian woman at the bar and now finds herself press-ganged into hunting monsters.<br /> <br /> A daughter of Yama who is a grief consular and occasional exorcist and is preparing herself for a job in her father's operation later. Fascinated with the idea of true beauty being judged based on how &quot;useful&quot; a person is to others and The World at large.<br /> <br /> A meteorologist post-grad who ended up changed into a satyr and a fling with Zeus after getting lost and stumbling into a Satyr kegger. Most of this is rebuild of a silly CoH character from back in the day. (also, yes, any theoretical I've made so far that is a denizen is also a scion). Now she has an academic advisor who is an incarnate of Hera that is definitely trying to kill her. They have a truce, the incarnate doesn't touch the woman's child or parents and the satyr keeps going on her suicide missions.<br /> <br /> A child of an incarnate of Ares whose father was killed and she took up his knives, a pair of cursed knives with violent personalities embedded from a very obsessively focused US Marshal from the old west and a bloodthirsty soldier from the WWI trenches. She has to manage the rage from the knives and her developing scion nature.<br /> <br /> A child from an Italian coven that has been using magic and incest to keep the presence of divine blood in their veins strong. She ran away as soon as she could and became first a circus performer and then a high-class thief. Has magic-eating squirrels. Rebuild of an NPC from a 1e campaign.<br /> <br /> Think that's all of them right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T06:02:05-07:00","id":1237740,"title":"","content":"Considering An adaptation of Shadow Moon.<br /> Other concepts I am still working out: Magician (as in, doing card and coin Tricks on the street or stage plays) with Tuatha heritage (Havent decided on a parent yet), an MMA Fighter (Son of Zeus), a mob-employed bookmaker and fence (Daughter of Hermes) and a hobo who is the Child of the MonkeyKing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T06:28:44-07:00","id":1237749,"title":"","content":"After reading the Percy Jackson series and starting the Heroes of Olympus one, it occurred to me that I would really enjoy playing a scion of Aphrodite who is a modern day chivalric paladin complete with plate armor and sword who strives to protect and defend all that is truly beautiful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T07:07:06-07:00","id":1237755,"title":"","content":"Political activist of Sami descent who is the daughter of Freya","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T14:58:03-07:00","id":1237816,"title":"","content":"A sickly child of Sun Wukong who has been diagnosed with the aids virus, and thus relies heavily upon their divine potential to survive the hurdles life places before them. Anybody who makes a joke about simian aids gets smacked in the jaw with their magical cane!<br /> <br /> <br /> A musically inclined Scion who's performances have a tendency to attract the presence of demons, which they are forced to battle to the death. Eventually, it becomes clear that Fate has placed them on the path to joining the pantheon of Heavy Metal!<br /> <br /> <br /> A chosen Scion of Izanami, who was resuscitated back to life in the middle of their soul leaving their body. Such a jarring experience has left them existing on the border between life and death, embodying in spirit what their patron embodies in form.<br /> <br /> <br /> A white minotaur who swears they are a direct descendant of Poseidon, himself. Such claims are thought to be nothing more than outlandish slander, until they demonstrate their heritage by conjuring a spring of water in the center of Crete. Oh, yeah, he's also claiming to have some blood ties to King Minos, which makes him the rightful king of Crete!<br /> <br /> <br /> A chosen of Hephaestus who served as a military engineer until losing the use of their left leg to a land mine. Despite being declared no longer fit for active service, they continue to work on projects designed to improve and expand the Theoi's military capabilities in the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2018, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:07:37-07:00","id":1239550,"title":"","content":"A Scion of Tsuki-Yomi who's constantly neglectful father drives them further away from the path of the Kami. In a half hearted attempt to make amends between them, they have been presented with a magical mirror, said to contain the power of the Moon within its reflective surface.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Hades who's deep rooted depression has stripped them of any ability to find joy in life. Hoping to cheer them up, the Lord of the Dead has presented them with the Harp of Orpheus, which grants them power over Death itself!<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Apollo, who's archery skills are so impressive that the god presented them with a quiver of arrows made from the feathers of Icarus. The arrows are said to possess the might of the Sun itself, having absorbed a portion of its essence from when their previous owner flew too closely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-28-2018, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:13:45-07:00","id":1239570,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about a therapist to the gods.... definitely a Chosen, but I'm not sure of which god. Hestia or Geezhigo-Quae seem good options if they are recruited by a stable pillar who wants them to help their family - BUT, it occurred to me I should look to gods with the Passion Purview so the character can take that as their innate purview - so maybe a more fucked up god &quot;Choses&quot; them by coming to them for therapy in the first place...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T18:08:34-07:00","id":1240268,"title":"","content":"Thus far I've made a therianthrope boxer who spends his nights hunting down gangsters and beating them to a bloody pulp with his bare hands as a positive way to channel the beast within. Haven't figured out pantheon or beast that he turns into, latter depends in part on the former.<br /> <br /> Had 2 more based on the Sabaton song Resist and Bite: a Bulgarian wereboar who is rivals with a neo-nazi who makes a living training various raptors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T23:56:48-07:00","id":1240741,"title":"","content":"A Pre-Visitation Scion of Surya, who works for a corporation known as Titan Industries. He's a mercenary but also a real family man. Has a wife and a daughter who he is very devoted to. He works with the company to bring down mortal level threats. Like cults that threaten honest every day civilians. Eventually I am thinking he'll have access to Fire through a Cub of Dawon a Mythical Tiger Belonging to Durga who's name will be Yava Khan. His pre-vis cycle will be about him tracking this &quot;Threat&quot; down.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T15:48:40-07:00","id":1242518,"title":"","content":"A <b>Chosen of Thanos</b> (no, not that Thanos) who is savagely turned into a Vrykolakas prior to her visitation. Enraged by her new condition, she devotes her existence to hunting down and destroying the undead, punishing those who think they can cheat her master. Assuming she survives her adventures, she gradually becomes recognized as a Goddess of Fate, turning her wrath upon those who would seek to defy the natural order.<br /> <br /> <br /> A <b>Created of Hephaestus</b> who is just obsessed with the idea of animated colossi, and how to manufacture them. Probably because they happen to be one, themselves! Over the course of their adventures, they gradually ascend to divinity and become a God of Robotics. They leave behind a cult of self aware automotons who revere him as their divine creator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A naturally born <b>Scion of Hermes</b> who became the star athlete on the school's track team with a perfect win record. Impressed by their fitness level, the messenger of Olympus offers to provide them with a real challenge 'for once.' Over the course of their adventures, they continue to improve upon their inherent agility, eventually becoming renowned as the God of Speed and leaving all challengers in the dust.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T20:04:52-07:00","id":1256865,"title":"","content":"<b>A Scion of Artemis.</b> Who, in an effort to keep him focused on the more important tasks at hand, decided to curse her new representative with impotence. Until such a time as she deems him worthy enough to remove the affliction, or he becomes powerful enough to remove it, himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Scion of Geb</b>, who has become a multi-time champion in the art of sand sculptures. This artistic talent increases by nearly a hundred fold once their divine connection with the Earth is fully awakened. Shortly after discovering this, they head off towards the deserts of Egypt, to hone their abilities further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T18:16:59-07:00","id":1257060,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong of me to want to do a riff on Magnum PI as a scion of one of the Hawaiian deities (maybe Kaulu)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T09:19:40-07:00","id":1257787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1257060#post1257060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong of me to want to do a riff on Magnum PI as a scion of one of the Hawaiian deities (maybe Kaulu)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not! My wife has a Scion of Juno based on Sharon Stone's character (and the much sweeter real woman who that character was based on) in Casino.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T17:18:02-07:00","id":1258444,"title":"","content":"<b>Reincarnated Scion of Ravana.</b> Wielding the shastra blade Chandrahas, he's going to take back the throne of Lanka and lead the rakshasas to glory once more! If he can avoid kidnapping princesses this time. He's got a bit of a Ganondorf thing going...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T20:45:34-07:00","id":1258665,"title":"","content":"So this one's been building for a few days now. It's going to require a lot of explaining, though, since it involves something that hasn't been released and that I don't know anything about, so I'm largely making stuff up. It begins with the lost gods of Atlantis - specifically one god of my own invention: Karnon. <br /> <br /> Every Atlantean god is a god of intellect, just as every Teotl is a god of sacrifice. But many different Atlanteans had different kinds of intellect in which they excelled, and only together were they the highest form of the immortal mind. Karnon was a god of belief and metacognition; irrespective of objective reality, he saw true and false beliefs equally, information and logic without regard for fact. The flow of information was all that concerned him, and how it could be swayed and controlled so as to make anyone believe anything. He was known for both wisdom and trickery, cursed as a thief and deceiver (and not without reason) yet praised for his insight in the same breath. He held the Mastery of Darkness, dominion over secrets and the unknown, of rats and of ravens, and was apt to bargain with knowledge that was <i>usually</i> reliable. Finally, he was patron saint of the spurned. He would offer outcasts succor and balm within the shadows, safe from the harsh and unforgiving light, to use his own words. Whether victimized beggar or ostracized extremist, those on the outskirts of society often found a place under his wing. <br /> <br /> When the fall of Atlantis came, it was only Karnon who realized his own panic would hinder more than help. Seeing the chaos, fear, bravado and confusion of his kinsmen, he surrendered to the inevitability that Atlantis would fall... and began to plan beyond it. Though he suffered greatly to do so, he first peeled away his own Mantle and split it into four parts - Emeron, who Thinks of Thinking; Mell-Uras Ver, King of Rats and Ravens; Black Soril, the deceptive Master of Darkness; and the Lord In Rags, friend to the outcast - and disguised them as nuts, which he gave to passing birds. The birds flew far from Atlantean shores, but were struck down, for no creature could live that had seen Atlantis with its own eyes. The nuts survived, though, and circulated throughout the world, carried by bird and beast until they fell in the darkest places. <br /> <br /> Stripped of his very identity, there was but one thing left for the empty god to do: He tore out his own heart and cast it into the ocean. There it was eaten by a fish, which lived for a time on its bounty before being eaten by another, larger fish. That fish was then caught off the coast of West Africa, brought to mortals who'd never heard the name of Atlantis, and eaten by a happy village. In that village, one woman became pregnant, though she'd been thought barren. It was seen as a miracle, and indeed it was, for the daughter she bore was the first of a line of reincarnations that would continue on to the modern day, men and women across the world, throughout many cultures and eras. Wise and clever in equal measure, each would go on to have great adventures, but be plagued by strange dreams and a sense that there was something they weren't doing. Only a few would discover their purpose: To reassemble their divine identity, learn the fate of lost Atlantis, and return it to the World once again. <br /> <br /> None have succeeded in finding more than a single part of the Mantle, but as a new day dawns in the twenty-first century, the current bearer of the Atlantean Soul rises to meet it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T14:35:12-07:00","id":1258773,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m working on the signature characters for my Mal\u2019akhim project. Right now I\u2019m leaning toward a Jewish pantheist (in the tradition of Sagan, Einstein, and Spinoza) physicist Chosen of Raziel, trying to know G-d by unraveling the mysteries of the universe (much to the frustration of those Gods and Angels who don\u2019t want miracles scrutinized by science because of Fatebinding); a Johnny Cash based Christian Chosen of Gabriel who is a righteous prophet of justice for those who would exploit their fellow man; and a Sufi Muslim Chosen of Azrael who is an end of life councilor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:07:40-08:00","id":1269046,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theevilblackbunny.tumblr.com/post/180293573206/new-goddess-idea-shes-an-earth-goddess-of-the\" target=\"_blank\">O'sha, Earth Goddess of Steel Structures</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T19:16:40-08:00","id":1269416,"title":"","content":"A Scion of Baron Samedi who has taken it upon themselves to protect and revitalize the various endangered species of the world. Unfortunately, they seem to share their father's sense of humor, or perhaps they simply have a few screws loose. With their affinity for the Death purview, they've started to revive animals that have long since been extinct. Maybe that explains why he's banned from entering natural history museums throughout the country?<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------<br /> <br /> A Scion of Amaterasu who apparently really enjoyed her video game. In fact, they enjoyed it so much, that the sun goddess bestowed them with a magic calligraphy brush, who's power is more than a match for any mortal blade. Now they're painting the town black, on a divine mission to rid Japan of the corrupting evil that threatens its good people!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T21:16:37-08:00","id":1270269,"title":"","content":"A Born Scion of Loki.<br /> <br /> Their father is Loki.<br /> <br /> Their mother is ALSO Loki.<br /> <br /> Two Incarnations met in a bar, didn't realize who the other was, and thus Loki pranked themselves.<br /> <br /> Loki would probably be angrier, but they have to admit that from the outside it IS really funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-24-2018, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T21:49:49-08:00","id":1270277,"title":"","content":"The only one who doesn\u2019t think it\u2019s funny is the kid!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T17:13:53-08:00","id":1270459,"title":"","content":"A scion with an affinity for the Chaos purview, who becomes perversely fascinated with exploring the intricate mysteries of Chaos Theory.<br /> <br /> Over time, they begin to drift away from the role of a divine trickster and become more like a force of nature, having found the Titans to be much more appreciative of their work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T04:23:53-08:00","id":1270798,"title":"","content":"About to start 3 Scion games as my group loved the backer PDF's so much.<br /> <br /> My characters are:<br /> <b>Man of the Nile</b> A Scion of Sobek, born to a nile crocodile who's natural state is a crocodile (Sobek got a little funky).<br /> Unable to speak any human but has a gut feeling to protect the Scion of Horus for obvious lore reasons, so spends most of his time eating, sleeping, fighting and learning random words (So far he can say &quot;Clothes&quot; in Arabic after an unfortunate instance of him walking around a cruise ship nude)<br /> Oh and he is a Were-crocodile who can swap between human and croc at Origin level, but as soon as he gets his Legend full Hybrid crocodile monster time!<br /> <br /> <b>Renton Paris </b>A Greek Scion in 1864 Nevada in an old west scion game. He is the eldest in a family of 4 Siblings, one of whom is married into a family of 3 siblings all scions of the Irish pantheon. The combined family run a cattle ranch outside Virginia City, while secretly being outlaws. The game is very much in the GM's hands as to our parentage but the plan is everyone in this extended family will be chosen by a god of their respective pantheons and have to work together against a larger threat in the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampiric Scion </b>Our third game is more experimental as we plan to port a more juiced up version of VTM/ VTR using scions rules. The GM and I are both big story path fans and big into both Homebrewing games and Vampire so decided to smash the 2 together (He has written over 800 pages of VTR homebrew adding dozens of clans, covenants and powers to the game). Mostly we are replacing Disciplines with Purviews with more specific focuses via Motifs and specialties, while making new Purviews to cover areas that where harder to sort. I am looking to test a new Purview of Flesh as effectively a Tzimice Cult Leader.<br /> We have lots of little edited subsystems like a tweak of Virtues that throw you into frenzy if you max out, a hunger health tracker where as you use abilities you get &quot;Hunger Conditions&quot; that make it harder to avoid feeding and push you closer to Hunger frenzy, and only by feeding can you remove the conditions. Vampiric Banes are conditions that pile up, rewarding players with Momentum for succumbing to their Banes. etc etc. Big playtesting game initially going to be set in New Orleans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:10:01-08:00","id":1271625,"title":"","content":"How long until we have a Tuatha rapper that diss his/her enemies with Tongue of the Bard? (Not exactly a genious concept but...)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:17:34-08:00","id":1271628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/921296-what-are-your-character-concepts?p=1270798#post1270798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vampiric Scion </b>Our third game is more experimental as we plan to port a more juiced up version of VTM/ VTR using scions rules. The GM and I are both big story path fans and big into both Homebrewing games and Vampire so decided to smash the 2 together (He has written over 800 pages of VTR homebrew adding dozens of clans, covenants and powers to the game). Mostly we are replacing Disciplines with Purviews with more specific focuses via Motifs and specialties, while making new Purviews to cover areas that where harder to sort. I am looking to test a new Purview of Flesh as effectively a Tzimice Cult Leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I wonder how many gods would work as potential parents for one or more Scions who aspire to becoming the god of vampires. Hecate, perhaps. Maybe Hel. I wish some of the Slavic pantheons were available already. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T07:28:20-08:00","id":1271767,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to do a historical game where I play Alexander Hamilton as a Scion of the Orisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T22:07:53-08:00","id":1287428,"title":"","content":"These are all 1e, but I think I'd enjoy playing them again adjusted as 2e...<br /> <br /> Daughter of Hel - Amelia (Emma) Fauntane - Tall, blonde, drop-dead gorgeous, and the lead singer in a local rock-band...She had it all until someone, actually a couple of someones, slipped something into her drinks at her high-school graduation after-party. She would have died if not for her Visitation; the records say she did.... Her Appearance, mundane and Epic (positive), is always maxed-out. Her Epic Dex rises at a 2-to-1 ratio (2 of 4) with her Epic Strength (1 of 4) and Epic Stamina (1 of 4). Her relic items are a pair of hand-axes that always return when called, a cell-phone-of-the-gods, and a set of (attached) functional wings fashioned of Stygian feathers that can be &quot;thrown&quot; like knives when fed Legend. Her Previews are Death, Darkness, and Frost, accessed through relic tattoos, Animal (Corvids) (accessed with the wings) and Psychopomp (accessed with the cell-phone). She sees herself as a defender of those unable to defend themselves (a guardian angel) and a guide who ensures the departed souls reach the proper afterlife. Just don't call her Hel's Angel...<br /> <br /> Daughter of Coyote - Moonglow Fox - With a mother who was a (politely phrased) &quot;Woodstock devotee&quot; (and all the negatives that go with that), she grew up on the reservation. Returning one day after getting her mother out of jail, again, she discovered the foster grand-mother who raised her, the only person in the world that treated her as if she were worth something, murdered... While tracking the killers, she received her Visitation. Upon finding out he knew about the attack but did nothing, out of grief she tried to kill her divine father... Still, he left her some relics - A silver tipped spear that changes size with legend usage (up to X- or 1/X-times size per dot of Legend), a Spirit Horse for transportation that can be summon for a scene(s) up to a day with legend, a &quot;Coyote Ugly&quot; tee-shirt that functions as a bullet-proof vest, and relic tattoos that allow her to access her Previews of Illusion, Animal (Canines), War, and Prophecy. [Later, she will receive a bow and arrows - unlimited ammo, range is line-of-sight, including epic perceptions - and a cell-phone-of-the-gods (Preview: Psychopomp)]. She focuses on Epic Perception and Epic Dex. When she's not temping at bars for cash, she's an agent-of-vengeance and hunter-of-titanspawn.<br /> <br /> Son of Hephaestus - Mac Sheen - &quot;I'm Iron-Man... sort-of...&quot; 'Nuff said....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25054-seekingone","name":"SeekingOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T20:11:51-08:00","id":1293642,"title":"","content":"<b>The idea I have for this character's future would really be more appropriate for the Theoi (due to their PSP), but his origin story fits better with the Aesir</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Oliver Prestegard:</b> The allegiances of many of Loki's children have been called into suspect over the ages, but in the case of Oliver, it seems all but certain that he will stand on the opposite side of the pantheon when the time of Ragnarok begins. Oliver hails from a different realm than our own, one in which fantastical creatures and wondrous magic not only survive, but also flourish as openly as humanity does within the World we call home. There, mortals live side by side with creatures who one might describe as <i>'monsters'</i> seemingly without much incident. But all of this changed when Loki introduced the young Scion to the real World.<br /> <br /> The sudden onslaught on mundanity, along with prejudice towards mythical creatures resulted in Oliver Prestegard experiencing several weeks worth of culture shock as he tried to adjust to the new situation. For reasons unknown to him (though probably Loki's doing), he was unable to return home to the world he grew up in, leaving him stranded in this one. After finally managing to regain his composure, he realized what must have been Loki's reason for doing what he did. Merely talking to the other members of the pantheon would never convince them that monsters were anything other than a threat to be eradicated. The only way to get through to them would be to pry their eyes open and show them a better path forward!<br /> <br /> Since then, Oliver has taken it upon himself to travel the World, strengthening the mythical population in whatever manner he can. He lobbies for equal rights and freedom of expression, hoping to convince society that a frost giant isn't going to bite their heads off as soon as it crosses the city limits. But mortals are timid creatures, and there will always be paranoid bigots who fear losing their station as the apex members of society. That is when Oliver has to channel his inner Trickster, and forcefully remove them from power!<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Origin Path:</b> Terra Incognita<br /> <br /> <b>Callings:</b> Liminal, Creator, Trickster<br /> <br /> <b>Titles:</b> Driver of Change<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>In The Beginning:</b> Oliver is a 21 year old man of Norwegian descent with short, brown hair and dark green eyes. He stands 6'2 in height, and weighs 156 lbs. He is athletically built, but not to the point of being a muscle bound jock. His features and body language are also unusually calm and collected. You probably wouldn't believe him if he told you he belonged to a pantheon who believes death on the battlefield is among the greatest achievements one can attain!<br /> <br /> Oliver's connection to mortals are tenuous at best. He adamantly rejects the idea that humans deserve to be the dominant life form of the planet, and strives to bring about a world in which all creatures may flourish. While he does not go around slaughtering mortals for the fun of it, he also does not shed any tears for mortals who are injured or killed by the actions of monsters. He recognizes that some creatures in this world must prey on humans to survive, and so long as they exercise self control and don't take more than what they need, he has no problem with allowing them to do so!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, most people (i.e humans) have extreme difficulty seeing the world from his perspective, leading to him being vilified by those who are aware of his more questionable morality. It also means he has great difficulty finding reliable allies who are simultaneously loyal to the Gods. So, as much as it disappoints him to do so, he has few options but to turn to the aid of those who have thrown their hat in with the Titans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-03-2019, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:38:03-08:00","id":1293771,"title":"","content":"Well, having a first look at some of the rules, I thinking of a Scion of Hermes. He was a writer focused on the occult and liminal subjects. Non-fiction for Fortean Times type mags and his fiction was Space Opera with occult/spiritual themes. Early skills Academics, Art(Prose writer), Occult. His paths, if I'm using the right term, would be <b>GUIDE</b>, <b>LIMINAL</b>, and <b>SAGE</b>.<br /> More later as he is worked out. Don't know the first name, but his family name is Mercer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:35:40-08:00","id":1294279,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering the idea of a Scion of Ares (or possibly some other war god) who aspires to be/is destined to be the God of Armorers/Arms Dealers, with an iron clad devotion to the &quot;armourer's faith&quot; from Shaw's play Major Barbara: &quot;To give arms to all men who offer an honest price for them, without respect to persons or principles, to ... all nationalities, all faiths, all follies, and all crimes.&quot; I'm not sure what paths would suit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T13:07:48-07:00","id":1313728,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the books being out, i decided to post a list of characters i made. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When making multiple characters i like giving myself guidelines to follow. In this case i have decided that I make one scion per featured pantheon before making more characters. Furthermore, each scion must inherit a different Calling and Purview. In order not to overburden the thread i\u2019m limiting the character presentation. Just things like name, title, inherited calling and purview and the most relevant (or interesting) birthright.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hope you enjoy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aesir:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aidan Leborgne, The Omen Seeker</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen Scion of Odin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Sage</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Fortune and Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthrights: Pair of Drones called Huginn and Muninn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: Meteorologist with a paranoid bend. He uses his incredible pattern analysis capabilities (especially on the subject of weather phenomenon) to help Odin in finding out the early signs of prophecies. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deva:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Akshay, Councillor to the recently departed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen (or Created) Scion of Yamaraja</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Liminal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Death and Yoga</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Chakrams that can be controlled at distance. Also give access to moon purview. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: A kind person whose purpose is helping the newly dead acclimate to their state before being sent to Yamaraja. In life was a social worker that died of work exhaustion, which Yamaraja can certainly relate with. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kami:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yoshirou, Rich Heir of a demon hunting legacy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen, Scion of Okuninushi</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Leader</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Prosperity and Yaoyorozu-no-kami</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Social follower that is a cool Yuki-Onna lawyer.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: The heir to a rich company. Studying diligently for the day he would take over, he was unprepared when his parents died in a fire and he learned that, for generations his family were merchants in service to Okuninushi as demon hunters. He now balances catching up on demon hunting while taking over the family business and keeping the company aloft.</span></span><br /> <br /> (continued in part 2)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 05-22-2019, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T13:09:34-07:00","id":1313729,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Part 2)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manitou:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Joseph Flint, Author of Nightmares</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Born, Scion of Tawiscara</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Creator</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Passion (fear), Dodaem</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Writing pen that can be used to summon a spawn of Djieien (a giant spider that hid its heart elsewhere so it could not be destroyed). Gives access to the purview Artistry (Horror)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: Ever since his birth, Joseph has been plagued with dark thought and terrible nightmares. Spending a lot of time in therapy even his parents feared for his future in society. But channeling these thoughts creatively made him an incredibly successful horror writer. While he has the reputation of a creepy and gloomy person, in truth he has a genuinely kind and compassionate heart. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Netjer:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sabra (?), Silver Tongued Snake</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen Scion of Aset</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Trickster</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Deception, Heku</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Snake </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(or one of its offspring)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> that Aset used to get the name of Ra . A creature that can detect when someone has a dark secret.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: A criminal that worked by learning the dark secret of rich people and then blackmailing them with it. Culminated with him trying that on an Incarnation of Aset and when he was caught tried to talk and charm his way out. Surprisingly (or maybe not) Aset found it quite amusing. So now he works for her in finding out other people's \u201ctrue name\u201d i.e. their secrets and exposing them to truth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Orisha:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jean-Christophe Dieudonn\u00e9, The Surviving Sacrifice</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen (maybe born) Scion of Sonponna</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Healer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Wild and Cheval</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Sacred broom of Babalu Aye. Gives acces to the Health purview and enhancement on action of purifications. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: Abandoned in the wilds by his father as sacrifice to gain great powers. Then found and taken care of by Sonponna. Saw some doctors without borders in action and was impressed. Decided to learn modern medicine to add to his traditional knowledge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> (continued in part 3)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 05-22-2019, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T13:10:29-07:00","id":1313730,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(part 3)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shen:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dai Lung (name to be changed), Most Dutiful Son of Ao Kuang</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen Scion of Confucius</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Judge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Order and Tianming</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: The spirit of Di Renjie (Judge Di). Guide stunts that give more stunts to do with clues. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: Youngest son of Ao Kuang, he has been tasked with finding back a bunch of relic that were stolen. To do so he sought the help of his old mentor Confucius. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Teotl:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hector Aguillera, Thousand winged warrior</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen (could be born) Scion of Huitzilopochtli</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Warrior</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: War and Nextlanahualli</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Charm of Hummingbird. Followers with the Mob tag and the They\u2019re Everywhere warrior knack. (picture more than 50 war hummingbirds)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: A kind ornithologist turned Eco-warrior when he witnessed a bird sanctuary cruelly despoiled. Now leads a host of fallen warriors (in the form of hummingbirds) in terrifying revenge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theoi:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anthony Powell, The Breaker of Bonds</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Born Scion of Ares</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Lover</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Chaos and Metamorphosis</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Bullet ant gun. A gun that shoots bullet \u2026 ants that form temporary Myrmidon soldiers as followers. Number of followers is dependant on wound given by the gun. Made by Myrmidon Manufacturing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: Born in a heavy military family but never fitting in the rigid mold of the military. He instead joined an intelligence agency and use his abilities to foment discord and betrayal around the world. (think Sterling Archer essentially) </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Edward \u201cEddy\u201d Manx, The Perfect (or Kindly) Host</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Born Scion of Aengus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calling: Guardian</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Beauty and Geas</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birthright: Son of the king of Cats (Cat prince). A guide that gives complication on targets who transgress laws of hospitality. Gives access to purview Beasts (Cats)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description: Son of Aengus and Caer Ibormeith he became tired of living with the Sidhe and asked of his father to give him a place to rule. He is now the manager of a new Youth Hostel called BnB (for Bru na Boinne). </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 05-22-2019, 04:13 PM"},"att